00:11:05.131 --> 00:11:07.767
and it is very popular souvenir of Tokyo.

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:11.070
And they turn into Kit Kats.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:13.305
Ta-da! Ooh!

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:16.676
It's gross.

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:19.311
When you come to Tokyo, you
should try Tokyo bananas,

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:22.415
but you should not try
Tokyo banana Kit Kats.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:24.350
Rum raisin.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.118
It's from Tokyo.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:28.421
Tokyo is not famous for rum raisin.

00:11:28.421 --> 00:11:31.057
But it says, "Rum raisin's gorgeousness

00:11:31.057 --> 00:11:34.060
and fanciness matches the image of Tokyo."

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:42.101
There is a shot of rum.

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:42.935
I don't like it!

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:44.804
It contains a lot of alcohol.

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:46.138
Ooh.

00:11:46.138 --> 00:11:47.406
Nande?

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:48.240
Last one!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.642
Sake flavor,

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:53.112
which is a Japanese traditional
alcohol made from rice.

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:54.747
This is a really interesting one.

00:11:56.315 --> 00:11:57.583
Oh.

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:58.818
Personally, I like it.

00:11:58.818 --> 00:12:01.320
And this is an acquired taste.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.355
So, when it comes to sake flavor,

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:07.293
we were supposed to have
yogurt sake, yuzu sake,

00:12:07.293 --> 00:12:10.196
limited-edition Japan sake umeshu,

00:12:10.196 --> 00:12:13.132
but these were not available
at the time of filming this.

00:12:13.132 --> 00:12:16.402
And we have Kit Kat desserts.

00:12:16.402 --> 00:12:18.137
We have Kit Kat Colliders,

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.572
which I could not find
at the filming of this,

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:22.174
but it looks to be almost
like vanilla-flavored cups

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:25.111
with Kit Kat chunks broken up in it.

00:12:25.111 --> 00:12:27.646
Oh, man, I ate too many Kit Kats.

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:29.348
And then we have these.

00:12:29.348 --> 00:12:31.884
These Kit Kat ice cream cones.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:33.819
Eh.

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:36.222
I hit a wall real hard.

00:12:36.222 --> 00:12:39.925
I hit a giant Kit Kat XL wall,

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:42.328
and I officially do not
want to do this anymore.

00:12:43.395 --> 00:12:45.197
Better, but not by much more.

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:47.299
Yeah, so that's it for the US.

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:49.135
Sorry we have so few flavors.

00:12:49.135 --> 00:12:51.971
Japan has a Kit Kat called Otona no Amasa,

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:55.875
which translates to
"sweetness for adults."

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.978
Ow! R-rated!

00:12:58.978 --> 00:13:01.413
Don't let your kids watch this part!

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:03.716
All right, so it's a
line of Kit Kat flavors

00:13:03.716 --> 00:13:04.984
that are a little more bitter

00:13:04.984 --> 00:13:07.086
and less sweet than regular Kit Kats.

00:13:07.086 --> 00:13:10.523
So, here we have Otona
no Amasa strawberry,

00:13:10.523 --> 00:13:11.957
white,

00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:14.026
and dark matcha

00:13:14.026 --> 00:13:15.561
and dark chocolate.

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:16.662
All right, so let's give it a try.

00:13:16.662 --> 00:13:17.496
First.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:19.431
This is just straight-up dark chocolate,

00:13:19.431 --> 00:13:20.266
as you can imagine.

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:21.667
Strawberry.

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:24.970
Ooh, it's actually tart.

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:25.805
This is good.

00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:27.439
All right, so let's
move on to the next one.

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:29.275
We've got dark matcha.

00:13:29.275 --> 00:13:30.776
Mm.

00:13:30.776 --> 00:13:32.478
This is so deep.

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:35.414
Much deeper than the other matcha flavors.

00:13:35.414 --> 00:13:39.685
So, last one, we've got Otona
no Amasa white chocolate.

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:42.755
This is the best one

00:13:42.755 --> 00:13:45.324
among these Otona no Amasa chocolates.

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:47.726
Just right sweetness.

00:13:47.726 --> 00:13:51.831
All right, so let's do matcha taste test.

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:55.601
In Japan, matcha-flavored
Kit Kats are so popular.

00:13:55.601 --> 00:13:58.871
Over the years, we've
introduced 13 different,

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:01.207
different, different,
different matcha flavors.

00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:04.443
But currently, we were only
able to get these three.

00:14:04.443 --> 00:14:06.946
So let's see how different they are.

00:14:06.946 --> 00:14:08.447
First, dark matcha.

00:14:09.281 --> 00:14:10.850
Deep matcha.

00:14:11.884 --> 00:14:12.852
But it's also deep.

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:15.020
Ito Kyuemon Uji matcha.

00:14:15.888 --> 00:14:18.691
So freaking hard to tell the difference.

00:14:18.691 --> 00:14:22.194
But I'd say this one is
the most delicious one.

00:14:22.194 --> 00:14:23.662
Kyoto.

00:14:23.662 --> 00:14:26.866
You can get it in Kyoto or order online.

00:14:26.866 --> 00:14:30.603
So, here we have classy
chocolates called Sublime.

00:14:30.603 --> 00:14:33.072
So we have white Sublime

00:14:33.072 --> 00:14:35.107
and raw milk Sublime

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:37.543
and a volcanic green Sublime

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:40.212
and orange volcanic Sublime,

00:14:40.212 --> 00:14:41.113
yellow,

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:42.414
ruby Sublime.

00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:44.183
All right, so let's try some out.

00:14:44.183 --> 00:14:46.685
I'm getting sick of the sweetness.

00:14:46.685 --> 00:14:47.753
Itadakimasu.

00:14:51.624 --> 00:14:53.125
It doesn't taste anything!

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:55.594
I was thinking that it'd
taste like strawberry

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:57.396
or raspberry or something, but.

00:14:58.931 --> 00:15:00.132
Did I get COVID?

00:15:00.132 --> 00:15:01.433
COVID-19?

00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:03.002
OK, let's keep going.

00:15:03.002 --> 00:15:05.504
All right, so I'm going
to go yellow volcanic.

00:15:05.504 --> 00:15:07.740
Volcano! Pew!

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:10.276
Ooh!

00:15:10.276 --> 00:15:12.344
This is the bitterest.

00:15:12.344 --> 00:15:14.079
I've got orange.

00:15:17.516 --> 00:15:18.817
Bitter.

00:15:18.817 --> 00:15:19.985
Now I'm so scared.

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:21.720
Green Sublime.

00:15:23.422 --> 00:15:27.192
It tastes exactly same
as these two. So bitter.

00:15:27.192 --> 00:15:29.762
Next we have milk Sublime.

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:34.333
It tastes exactly the
same as regular flavor.

00:15:34.333 --> 00:15:35.567
I prefer this one.

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:37.870
Last one, I've got white Sublime.

00:15:40.572 --> 00:15:44.176
Compared to the Otona no
Amasa white chocolate,

00:15:44.176 --> 00:15:45.311
it's much better.

00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:46.145
I'm done.

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:48.280
Hey, guys, it's Harry.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.882
I can't let you do a Kit
Kat episode without me,

00:15:49.882 --> 00:15:52.952
because Kit Kats were actually
invented in the UK in 1935.

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:54.687
They would eventually
be distributed by Nestlé

00:15:54.687 --> 00:15:56.855
across the UK, the EU, and Japan.

00:15:56.855 --> 00:15:58.190
But in the US, Kit Kats are made

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.725
and distributed by Hershey's.

00:15:59.725 --> 00:16:01.193
If you watched our Snickers episode,

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:02.962
you'll know that there are
some major taste differences

00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:05.030
between the chocolate
in the UK and the US.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.932
Mostly that the UK's is way better.

00:16:06.932 --> 00:16:08.100
I'm going to do a three-way taste test

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.836
between UK, US, and
also a Japanese Kit Kat

00:16:10.836 --> 00:16:12.871
to see if there's any major
differences between the three.

00:16:12.871 --> 00:16:15.774
And, Harry, thank you for sending me this

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:17.409
with your cute handwriting.

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:19.545
Thank you, Harry! Arigato.

00:16:19.545 --> 00:16:21.680
Let's try UK Kit Kat first.

00:16:24.016 --> 00:16:25.751
The UK one is obviously
the one I'm used to.

00:16:25.751 --> 00:16:27.119
The chocolate is very smooth,

00:16:27.119 --> 00:16:29.621
not overwhelmingly sweet,
and just very tasty.

00:16:29.621 --> 00:16:31.590
The UK is already a lot richer.

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:35.094
OK, OK.

00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:36.695
Can I try US Kit Kat?

00:16:36.695 --> 00:16:37.563
I also couldn't find

00:16:37.563 --> 00:16:39.231
just a standard American Kit Kat anywhere.

00:16:39.231 --> 00:16:41.500
I guess we didn't bother
importing the regular one.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.568
The closest thing I could find

00:16:42.568 --> 00:16:44.870
was this Kit Kat Duos
mocha and chocolate one.

00:16:47.206 --> 00:16:49.408
Something doesn't taste
quite right about that.

00:16:49.408 --> 00:16:50.242
Yep.

00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:52.111
UK, US,

00:16:52.111 --> 00:16:53.445
they suck.

00:16:53.445 --> 00:16:55.948
They both have too much sugar.

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:58.784
Joe, Harry, try Japan's Kit Kat.

00:16:59.918 --> 00:17:00.753
Mm.

00:17:00.753 --> 00:17:02.354
Much smoother. Creamier.

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:03.355
In terms of picking a favorite,

00:17:03.355 --> 00:17:05.557
I think the US one gets
discounted immediately.

00:17:05.557 --> 00:17:07.126
Then, between the UK and the Japan one,

00:17:07.126 --> 00:17:09.428
it's kind of a different
style of Kit Kat, I guess.

00:17:09.428 --> 00:17:11.430
I would say Japan and UK
are pretty neck and neck.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.431
They seem very similar.

00:17:12.431 --> 00:17:15.534
Japan's Kit Kat is the best in the world.

00:17:15.534 --> 00:17:17.436
Ugh, I've eaten too much candy.

00:17:17.436 --> 00:17:18.537
Ugh!

00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:20.272
Perhaps we can pinpoint
the taste difference

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:21.106
to the ingredients.

00:17:21.106 --> 00:17:22.775
In the US, a Kit Kat is made up of

00:17:22.775 --> 00:17:24.309
sugar, wheat flour --

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:25.144
[beep]

00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:27.880
[beep]

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.748
Our Kit Kats have the following.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:32.851
Looking over the ingredients,

00:17:32.851 --> 00:17:35.320
I noticed our Kit Kats have
cocoa butter and chocolate,

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.655
although it does not specify

00:17:36.655 --> 00:17:38.190
what that chocolate is made up of.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:39.358
Do we assume it is the same

00:17:39.358 --> 00:17:40.592
as the Hershey's chocolate bar?

00:17:40.592 --> 00:17:41.427
I don't know.

00:17:41.427 --> 00:17:43.662
Whereas the Japan Kit Kat has cocoa mass,

00:17:43.662 --> 00:17:46.465
cocoa butter, and cocoa powder.

00:17:46.465 --> 00:17:48.867
Now, if we're to believe
that Nestlé in Japan

00:17:48.867 --> 00:17:50.369
holds their chocolate
to the same standards

00:17:50.369 --> 00:17:51.737
they do in the UK, it would mean

00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:54.173
that it would have a higher
fat and cocoa content.

00:17:54.173 --> 00:17:56.041
According to the UK rules,

00:17:56.041 --> 00:17:59.111
"a product must contain no
less than 25% cocoa solids

00:17:59.111 --> 00:18:01.213
to be considered 'milk chocolate.'"

00:18:01.213 --> 00:18:03.615
The US definitely does
not go by this rule.

00:18:03.615 --> 00:18:05.684
Our Kit Kat is made up of palm oil,

00:18:05.684 --> 00:18:08.020
where theirs is vegetable
oil. Same in the UK.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.389
It is cheaper, but it's also
worse on the environment,

00:18:10.389 --> 00:18:11.723
adding to deforestation,

00:18:11.723 --> 00:18:13.192
increasing greenhouse [gas] emissions,

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:14.660
and water pollution.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.496
So it is bad on the
environment and tastes worse.

00:18:17.496 --> 00:18:18.630
Fantastic.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.066
But good news for all you vegans,

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:23.535
Nestlé has created a vegan Kit Kat,

00:18:23.535 --> 00:18:27.272
with substituted milk with
a rice-based alternative,

00:18:27.272 --> 00:18:29.608
but availability is currently limited,

00:18:29.608 --> 00:18:32.544
so they are not available
in the US or Japan.

00:18:34.546 --> 00:18:36.615
This is a US Kit Kat miniature,

00:18:36.615 --> 00:18:38.517
and it is 8.5 grams.

00:18:38.517 --> 00:18:40.652
It's the closest size
we had to Japan's mini.

00:18:40.652 --> 00:18:42.287
This is 42 calories,

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:43.956
2.2 grams of fat,

00:18:43.956 --> 00:18:45.557
6 milligrams of sodium,

00:18:45.557 --> 00:18:47.126
5.8 grams of carbs,

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:48.627
4 of those are sugar,

00:18:48.627 --> 00:18:50.629
and 1 gram of protein.

00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:53.532
In Japan, the mini is
the most popular size.

00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:55.367
It's 62 calories

00:18:55.367 --> 00:18:57.469
and 3.5 grams of fat,

00:18:57.469 --> 00:19:01.039
3.5 to 11.4 milligrams of sodium,

00:19:01.039 --> 00:19:04.977
8.99 to 19.4 grams of total carbs,

00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:07.713
and 0.9 grams of protein.

00:19:07.713 --> 00:19:09.982
The most common Kit Kat size in the US

00:19:09.982 --> 00:19:11.650
is the four-finger bar.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.252
210 calories,

00:19:13.252 --> 00:19:14.286
11 grams of fat,

00:19:14.286 --> 00:19:15.587
7 of those are saturated,

00:19:15.587 --> 00:19:17.389
20 milligrams of sodium,

00:19:17.389 --> 00:19:18.690
28 grams of carbs,

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:20.359
23 of those are sugar,

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:21.793
and 2 grams of protein.

00:19:21.793 --> 00:19:24.096
The closest size we have to that in Japan

00:19:24.096 --> 00:19:25.531
is the Kit Kat bar.

00:19:25.531 --> 00:19:28.233
It contains 224 calories.

00:19:28.233 --> 00:19:30.135
The most caloried Kit Kat in the US we got

00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:31.703
is the Kit Kat XL.

00:19:31.703 --> 00:19:33.272
Now, I unwrapped it here so you could see

00:19:33.272 --> 00:19:34.473
just how big it is.

00:19:34.473 --> 00:19:36.742
It contains 640 calories.

00:19:36.742 --> 00:19:39.945
The most calories you will
get in a Kit Kat in Japan

00:19:39.945 --> 00:19:41.680
is the big little pouch bite.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.583
This bag is 275 calories.

00:19:44.983 --> 00:19:47.119
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:19:47.119 --> 00:19:48.921
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:51.657
between Burger King in Japan and the US.

00:19:51.657 --> 00:19:53.592
This is "Food Wars."

00:19:58.597 --> 00:20:00.799
Here's everything you can find on the menu

00:20:00.799 --> 00:20:04.069
at the Burger King in
Japan but not in the US.

00:20:04.069 --> 00:20:07.105
Here's everything you can
find at a US Burger King

00:20:07.105 --> 00:20:08.974
you cannot get in Japan.

00:20:08.974 --> 00:20:12.678
All right, so let's start
with exclusive burgers.

00:20:12.678 --> 00:20:16.148
So, here we have teriyaki lettuce burger

00:20:16.148 --> 00:20:18.250
and teriyaki Whopper.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.319
Ooh!

00:20:20.319 --> 00:20:21.920
Huge.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:25.824
Next we have avocado salad burger

00:20:25.824 --> 00:20:27.526
and avocado Whopper.

00:20:27.526 --> 00:20:31.430
Aah, a little cute baby.

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.764
Look at this.

00:20:32.764 --> 00:20:36.001
And Whopper.

00:20:38.003 --> 00:20:40.339
It's totally different.

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:42.374
This one is so huge.

00:20:42.374 --> 00:20:44.543
And avocados, tomato,

00:20:44.543 --> 00:20:46.078
no tomatoes.

00:20:46.078 --> 00:20:47.279
I don't know why.

00:20:47.279 --> 00:20:50.983
Next we have quattro cheese Whopper.

00:20:50.983 --> 00:20:54.353
Oh, big boy.

00:20:55.487 --> 00:20:58.323
We've got smoky barbecue Whopper

00:20:58.323 --> 00:21:01.326
and smoky barbecue Whopper junior.

00:21:01.326 --> 00:21:04.630
And here is spicy Whopper.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.468
Ooh!

00:21:09.468 --> 00:21:10.502
It's hot sauce.

00:21:11.837 --> 00:21:15.274
Next, we have tartar chicken burger.

00:21:15.274 --> 00:21:18.110
Ooh, it's got

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.479
a lot of tartar sauce,

00:21:20.479 --> 00:21:22.814
chicken, crispy.

00:21:22.814 --> 00:21:25.484
Burger King in Japan just
released a brand-new burger

00:21:25.484 --> 00:21:27.819
called Guilty Burger.

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:30.455
It's basically butter burger.

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:31.356
Why?

00:21:31.356 --> 00:21:33.058
What have you done?

00:21:33.058 --> 00:21:37.329
Let's check out this Guilty
butter beef burger first.

00:21:37.329 --> 00:21:38.764
The bun is different.

00:21:38.764 --> 00:21:40.832
Itadakimasu!

00:21:43.302 --> 00:21:45.671
Just a little bit of butter flavor,

00:21:45.671 --> 00:21:48.907
but I don't feel as guilty as it claims.

00:21:48.907 --> 00:21:52.044
This one is Guilty butter
croquette sandwich.

00:21:52.044 --> 00:21:54.046
Ooh.

00:21:55.047 --> 00:21:56.548
Guilty!

00:21:58.583 --> 00:22:02.954
And here is Guilty butter chicken burger.

00:22:04.022 --> 00:22:06.525
First one is something
that BK has exclu --

00:22:06.525 --> 00:22:08.427
oh, my God.

00:22:08.427 --> 00:22:10.462
This is called the Texas Whopper.

00:22:12.364 --> 00:22:14.866
Look at the size of this f---ing thing.

00:22:16.601 --> 00:22:19.738
Two patties, cheese,
bacon, bunch of veggies.

00:22:19.738 --> 00:22:20.939
Wait for it!

00:22:24.509 --> 00:22:26.144
The triple Whopper.

00:22:26.144 --> 00:22:28.880
Look at the size of this thing.

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:32.584
The weight of it has completely
flattened the bottom bun.

00:22:32.584 --> 00:22:35.987
And there's nothing between
the patties of meat!

00:22:37.089 --> 00:22:39.524
What the hell are you
guys doing over there?

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:40.859
Next.

00:22:40.859 --> 00:22:42.160
Oh, the Bacon King.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.462
Oh, my God.

00:22:43.462 --> 00:22:46.798
Looks to be pretty bacon centric.

00:22:46.798 --> 00:22:48.100
Looks like a double Whopper with cheese,

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:50.369
bacon, mayo, ketchup, mustard.

00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:52.504
They didn't mess with
the veggies. Thank you.

00:22:52.504 --> 00:22:53.538
You're not fooling anyone

00:22:53.538 --> 00:22:55.273
getting lettuce and onion on that one.

00:22:55.273 --> 00:22:58.643
The rodeo burger is a
little guy with onion rings.

00:22:58.643 --> 00:23:00.979
The rodeo burger. Yeehaw.

00:23:00.979 --> 00:23:02.514
On to the chicken.

00:23:02.514 --> 00:23:03.548
I'll just put this over here.

00:23:03.548 --> 00:23:04.983
Japan does not have

00:23:04.983 --> 00:23:07.552
what we call the original
chicken sandwich.

00:23:07.552 --> 00:23:09.221
And I don't know why Burger King,

00:23:09.221 --> 00:23:10.756
maybe just to set itself apart,

00:23:10.756 --> 00:23:13.024
the chicken sandwich is
this, like, sub shape.

00:23:13.024 --> 00:23:14.559
It's like I'm holding the phone.

00:23:14.559 --> 00:23:15.427
This is great.

00:23:15.427 --> 00:23:17.429
Chicken junior, spicy chicken junior.

00:23:17.429 --> 00:23:18.263
Let's go spicy.

00:23:21.967 --> 00:23:23.335
Barely registers in the spice meter.

00:23:23.335 --> 00:23:24.369
Wait!

00:23:24.369 --> 00:23:25.203
Yeah.

00:23:25.203 --> 00:23:28.273
BKs in the US have something
called the Ch'King sandwich.

00:23:28.273 --> 00:23:30.108
You can get the sandwich
regular or deluxe.

00:23:30.108 --> 00:23:33.245
You can also get the sandwich
flavor regular or spicy.

00:23:33.245 --> 00:23:37.182
So here is the regular regular.

00:23:37.182 --> 00:23:38.216
And as you can see,

00:23:38.216 --> 00:23:40.752
just comes with sauce and
pickles and the chicken.

00:23:40.752 --> 00:23:42.921
You can get it deluxe and spicy,

00:23:42.921 --> 00:23:44.990
so we went with deluxe,
comes with all these veggies

00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:47.959
that you brush off right
when you start eating it,

00:23:47.959 --> 00:23:52.297
and it has got a spicy kind
of hue to the chicken there.

00:23:52.297 --> 00:23:54.566
Here's our side menu.

00:23:54.566 --> 00:23:56.368
Let's start with this one.

00:23:56.368 --> 00:23:58.437
We've got hot dog.

00:23:58.437 --> 00:24:01.006
It's got such a big sausage.

00:24:03.975 --> 00:24:06.378
This one is chili beans hot dog.

00:24:07.879 --> 00:24:11.249
And next we have this little guy,

00:24:11.249 --> 00:24:13.218
snack chicken.

00:24:13.218 --> 00:24:16.555
And last we have this one,

00:24:16.555 --> 00:24:19.124
chili cheese fries.

00:24:19.124 --> 00:24:23.061
And if you want some veggies,
you can order Caesar salad.

00:24:23.061 --> 00:24:26.231
But my bad, I forgot to order.

00:24:26.231 --> 00:24:29.267
Also exclusives to the US
are these, chicken fries.

00:24:29.267 --> 00:24:30.669
As you can tell, they look like fries,

00:24:30.669 --> 00:24:32.437
but they're pieces of chicken.

00:24:32.437 --> 00:24:33.772
Not bad.

00:24:33.772 --> 00:24:36.174
You can get Mott's applesauce.

00:24:36.174 --> 00:24:37.976
Jalapeño cheddar bites.

00:24:37.976 --> 00:24:39.244
I've never heard of these.

00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:43.448
And now I know why.

00:24:43.448 --> 00:24:47.152
Burger King in the US has
two iced-coffee flavors,

00:24:47.152 --> 00:24:48.487
mocha and vanilla.

00:24:48.487 --> 00:24:49.988
Assuming that's the mocha.

00:24:53.458 --> 00:24:55.026
Tastes exactly like chocolate milk.

00:24:55.026 --> 00:24:55.861
Blech! No.

00:24:55.861 --> 00:24:57.329
Oh, the aftertaste is horrible.

00:24:57.329 --> 00:24:58.363
What the hell?

00:24:58.363 --> 00:24:59.898
That's ridiculous how bad that is.

00:24:59.898 --> 00:25:01.900
And the vanilla.

00:25:04.135 --> 00:25:06.271
That is so sweet.

00:25:06.271 --> 00:25:07.472
I'm gonna keep this one.

00:25:08.373 --> 00:25:10.609
So, here is our dessert menus.

00:25:10.609 --> 00:25:13.078
Here we have coffee float.

00:25:13.078 --> 00:25:14.846
A little bit melting, sorry.

00:25:14.846 --> 00:25:17.849
And we have melon soda float.

00:25:17.849 --> 00:25:21.152
Coke float and Coke Zero float.

00:25:21.152 --> 00:25:26.024
And here we've got premium
sundae chocolate and coffee.

00:25:26.024 --> 00:25:28.894
And here is our chocolate sundae

00:25:28.894 --> 00:25:30.695
and strawberry sundae.

00:25:30.695 --> 00:25:34.199
And my favorite is this apple pie.

00:25:38.370 --> 00:25:39.571
Desserts.

00:25:39.571 --> 00:25:42.207
Here in the US you can get
yourself a Hershey's sundae pie.

00:25:43.708 --> 00:25:45.544
Ugh.

00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:48.947
This one might have got a
little roughed up in transit.

00:25:48.947 --> 00:25:52.951
And in the US Burger King, you
can also get various shakes.

00:25:52.951 --> 00:25:55.954
Here we have Oreo shake,
a chocolate Oreo shake,

00:25:55.954 --> 00:25:57.956
a chocolate shake, and a vanilla shake.

00:25:57.956 --> 00:25:58.790
All right.

00:25:59.658 --> 00:26:00.825
God, that's so good.

00:26:00.825 --> 00:26:02.060
The straight-up chocolate.

00:26:03.495 --> 00:26:04.896
Oh, man, this is trouble.

00:26:04.896 --> 00:26:06.798
Mm!

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:08.800
Wow, Burger King's shakes are really good.

00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:11.202
I'm assuming this is just
the straight Oreo one.

00:26:13.505 --> 00:26:17.042
Oh, my God, this is fantastic.

00:26:17.042 --> 00:26:20.178
Are we all curious what a
chocolate Oreo shake tastes like?

00:26:20.178 --> 00:26:21.513
Wonder no more.

00:26:23.448 --> 00:26:25.417
Good. This one's the best.

00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:28.019
Also at a US Burger King, you
can get a soft-serve cone.

00:26:28.019 --> 00:26:28.954
I didn't get it,

00:26:28.954 --> 00:26:31.856
only because we have no
refrigeration unit here

00:26:31.856 --> 00:26:34.859
and it would just be a cone
with a puddle of ice cream. So.

00:26:34.859 --> 00:26:38.196
Victoria, please turn me
into a giant soft-serve cone.

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:42.133
So, here are our drinks.

00:26:42.133 --> 00:26:43.768
Let's start with this one.

00:26:43.768 --> 00:26:45.203
This one is ginger ale;

00:26:45.203 --> 00:26:47.005
and Fanta melon;

00:26:47.005 --> 00:26:48.740
oolong tea,

00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:50.709
which is Chinese tea;

00:26:50.709 --> 00:26:52.510
and orange juice.

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:56.214
And this one is Earl Grey iced tea.

00:26:56.214 --> 00:26:58.817
Next we have Darjeeling tea.

00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:02.220
And here is Calpis,

00:27:02.220 --> 00:27:06.124
which, you guys call it
Calpico in your country.

00:27:06.124 --> 00:27:09.294
But in Japan we say "ka-ru pi-su."

00:27:09.294 --> 00:27:12.597
I know it sounds like
"cow piss" in English,

00:27:12.597 --> 00:27:15.000
but if you say Calpico to Japanese people,

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.569
they will never understand
what you're talking about.

00:27:17.569 --> 00:27:21.606
So in Japan, once again,
we say "ka-ru pi-su."

00:27:21.606 --> 00:27:24.309
Repeat after me. "Ka-ru pi-su."

00:27:24.309 --> 00:27:26.311
Very good!

00:27:26.311 --> 00:27:27.312
First things you can get,

00:27:27.312 --> 00:27:29.447
you can get a little orange juice guy,

00:27:29.447 --> 00:27:33.284
and you can also get
Capri Sun apple juice.

00:27:33.284 --> 00:27:35.387
Shout-out to the pouch.

00:27:35.387 --> 00:27:37.822
Burger King in the US has
Coke products as well,

00:27:37.822 --> 00:27:40.358
but we have something called
a Coke Freestyle machine.

00:27:40.358 --> 00:27:41.660
If you haven't seen it,
it's this big machine

00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:44.195
that has a bunch of
Coca-Cola-related beverages.

00:27:44.195 --> 00:27:45.230
You can mix and match them.

00:27:45.230 --> 00:27:47.766
Anyway, we can get Hi-C fruit punch,

00:27:47.766 --> 00:27:50.969
Hi-C pink lemonade, Fanta
orange, Mello Yello,

00:27:50.969 --> 00:27:55.173
Powerade Zero, Dr Pepper,
Barq's, diet Barq's.

00:27:55.173 --> 00:27:57.942
You can also get yourself a fat-free milk.

00:27:57.942 --> 00:27:58.777
There it is.

00:27:58.777 --> 00:28:00.378
Sweetened or unsweetened tea.

00:28:00.378 --> 00:28:01.746
I think I got the sweetened.

00:28:01.746 --> 00:28:04.783
I don't want any tea. Tea sucks.

00:28:04.783 --> 00:28:07.385
We also have something
called frozen Cokes.

00:28:07.385 --> 00:28:08.853
That is this right here.

00:28:08.853 --> 00:28:10.121
As you can see, it's
been sitting for a while,

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:10.989
it's starting to separate.

00:28:10.989 --> 00:28:12.157
But we have frozen Coke,

00:28:12.157 --> 00:28:14.359
we also have a frozen Fanta wild cherry,

00:28:14.359 --> 00:28:16.227
a frozen Fanta blue raspberry,

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:18.396
and a frozen strawberry lemonade.

00:28:18.396 --> 00:28:19.230
Mm.

00:28:20.432 --> 00:28:21.332
Oh, yeah.

00:28:21.332 --> 00:28:24.235
Japan has a few exclusives
that are similar

00:28:24.235 --> 00:28:26.237
but different to that in the US.

00:28:26.237 --> 00:28:31.109
So, for example, this is
our plant-based Whopper.

00:28:31.109 --> 00:28:35.380
This burger is made from 100% soybeans.

00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:36.815
Itadakimasu!

00:28:39.384 --> 00:28:40.952
It's actually delicious.

00:28:40.952 --> 00:28:42.387
I like it.

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:43.221
Mm.

00:28:43.221 --> 00:28:46.324
When it comes to
vegetarianism and veganism,

00:28:46.324 --> 00:28:48.259
they are not that popular in Japan.

00:28:48.259 --> 00:28:51.329
But gradually, especially
the restaurants in Tokyo

00:28:51.329 --> 00:28:54.466
are offering more vegan
or vegetarian meals

00:28:54.466 --> 00:28:56.634
because there is more Japanese people

00:28:56.634 --> 00:28:59.738
and non-Japanese people
who are vegan or vegetarian

00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:01.773
compared to other places in Japan.

00:29:01.773 --> 00:29:04.442
But overall, the vegan
or vegetarian option

00:29:04.442 --> 00:29:06.211
is still limited in Japan.

00:29:06.211 --> 00:29:08.847
And in the US, we have
the Impossible Whopper.

00:29:08.847 --> 00:29:09.714
What's the difference?

00:29:09.714 --> 00:29:12.884
Well, the Impossible burger
has all these ingredients.

00:29:12.884 --> 00:29:15.286
So as you can see, a lot more.

00:29:15.286 --> 00:29:17.489
I am curious.

00:29:17.489 --> 00:29:19.023
That looks like meat, right?

00:29:22.060 --> 00:29:22.961
Tastes exactly like a Whopper.

00:29:22.961 --> 00:29:24.462
I don't think I would
notice the difference.

00:29:24.462 --> 00:29:26.364
They're covering the
lack of meat with, like,

00:29:26.364 --> 00:29:29.033
with that char flavor
that they have on there.

00:29:29.033 --> 00:29:31.102
Oh, it's good.

00:29:31.102 --> 00:29:33.505
In Japan, we call this burger

00:29:33.505 --> 00:29:35.406
crispy chicken burger.

00:29:35.406 --> 00:29:37.075
And in the US, we have
the before-mentioned

00:29:37.075 --> 00:29:38.243
Ch'King sandwich,

00:29:38.243 --> 00:29:41.513
which comes in varieties
of spicy and/or deluxe.

00:29:41.513 --> 00:29:45.316
For breakfast, our hash
brown comes in one big piece.

00:29:46.351 --> 00:29:47.919
Whereas in the US,

00:29:47.919 --> 00:29:50.221
our hash browns come in little bites.

00:29:50.221 --> 00:29:54.993
And in Japan, we have this cheese bites.

00:29:54.993 --> 00:29:56.427
Look at this.

00:29:56.427 --> 00:29:59.097
And in the US, we have
eight-piece cheesy tots.

00:30:00.832 --> 00:30:03.001
And on to the US breakfast exclusives.

00:30:03.001 --> 00:30:04.769
As you can see, we have
a lot more going on

00:30:04.769 --> 00:30:08.106
in our breakfast menu here
in the US than Japan has.

00:30:08.106 --> 00:30:10.041
Here in the US, you can
get your breakfast sandwich

00:30:10.041 --> 00:30:13.378
in biscuit or Croissan'wich options.

00:30:13.378 --> 00:30:16.080
Croissan'wich is, of course,
a croissant sandwich.

00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:18.449
Took those two words, put
them together. Croissan'wich.

00:30:18.449 --> 00:30:20.985
So we have bacon, egg, and cheese;

00:30:20.985 --> 00:30:23.488
ham, egg, and cheese;

00:30:23.488 --> 00:30:26.791
and sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:30:26.791 --> 00:30:29.894
We have two breakfast burritos.

00:30:29.894 --> 00:30:32.096
The Egg-Normous breakfast burrito,

00:30:32.096 --> 00:30:33.598
which I'm assuming is this one,

00:30:33.598 --> 00:30:36.434
'cause it is enormous.

00:30:36.434 --> 00:30:38.403
The breakfast burrito junior.

00:30:38.403 --> 00:30:39.904
Look at this little guy!

00:30:39.904 --> 00:30:41.339
French toast sticks.

00:30:41.339 --> 00:30:43.775
Who doesn't like French toast?

00:30:43.775 --> 00:30:46.578
Finally, pancake platter
with just three pancakes

00:30:46.578 --> 00:30:49.180
or a pancake platter with three pancakes

00:30:49.180 --> 00:30:51.015
and a side of sausage.

00:30:53.318 --> 00:30:56.454
The fries at Burger King in
Japan come in three sizes,

00:30:56.454 --> 00:30:57.288
small,

00:30:59.290 --> 00:31:00.124
medium,

00:31:01.726 --> 00:31:02.660
and large.

00:31:04.696 --> 00:31:07.265
Fries in the US at Burger
King come in four sizes,

00:31:07.265 --> 00:31:09.834
value, small, medium, or large.

00:31:09.834 --> 00:31:13.171
Or maybe it's value, small, medium, large.

00:31:14.372 --> 00:31:15.673
Does this look right?

00:31:15.673 --> 00:31:17.075
Any of you "Food Wars" heads

00:31:17.075 --> 00:31:19.978
would've seen the Burger
King US vs UK episode

00:31:19.978 --> 00:31:22.113
where we uncovered Frygate.

00:31:22.113 --> 00:31:26.284
Two sizes had pretty much
the exact same unit of fries.

00:31:26.284 --> 00:31:27.919
Now, as you can see from these,

00:31:27.919 --> 00:31:31.222
I can't tell which is
the value and the small.

00:31:31.222 --> 00:31:32.824
I'm assuming this is the medium.

00:31:32.824 --> 00:31:37.695
Well, unfortunately, we cannot
do that amazingly accurate

00:31:37.695 --> 00:31:40.365
scientific test that we
did in the last episode

00:31:40.365 --> 00:31:42.800
because the fries have been compromised.

00:31:42.800 --> 00:31:44.869
They all came in the same bag, and ...

00:31:46.004 --> 00:31:48.072
I think they knew what we were up to

00:31:48.072 --> 00:31:51.042
and they purposely dumped
all the fries in the same bag

00:31:51.042 --> 00:31:54.312
to contaminate the experiment.

00:31:54.312 --> 00:31:56.080
You've outsmarted us this time.

00:31:56.080 --> 00:31:57.282
George: Let's weigh the large fries

00:31:57.282 --> 00:31:59.017
to see how much you actually get.

00:31:59.951 --> 00:32:02.287
151 grams.

00:32:02.287 --> 00:32:03.521
What if we did a thing where, like,

00:32:03.521 --> 00:32:06.524
whatever lands and stays on counts as it?

00:32:06.524 --> 00:32:08.927
Does that seem like a fair thing to say?

00:32:08.927 --> 00:32:11.529
That's really smart, what
I just did there, I think.

00:32:14.399 --> 00:32:16.067
It's 195 grams.

00:32:17.302 --> 00:32:18.970
Let's weigh Japan's Whopper.

00:32:20.571 --> 00:32:22.140
250 grams.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:26.010
Joe: And let us weigh
our Whopper in the US.

00:32:26.010 --> 00:32:28.079
Yo!

00:32:28.079 --> 00:32:29.347
270?

00:32:29.347 --> 00:32:30.815
Yeah, 270 grams.

00:32:30.815 --> 00:32:32.750
So pretty close. Surprisingly close.

00:32:32.750 --> 00:32:35.019
If you're not feeling like having beef,

00:32:35.019 --> 00:32:37.288
Burger King also has some chicken options.

00:32:37.288 --> 00:32:38.656
You can order your chicken nuggets

00:32:38.656 --> 00:32:41.459
in five pieces and eight pieces.

00:32:41.459 --> 00:32:43.594
Here in the US, you can
get your nuggets in sizes

00:32:43.594 --> 00:32:46.631
of four pieces, eight
pieces, or 16 pieces.

00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:49.634
And it's worth noting that
you can only get the 16-piece

00:32:49.634 --> 00:32:52.303
online or through their
app, and even if you do,

00:32:52.303 --> 00:32:54.872
they still just give you two eight-pieces.

00:32:54.872 --> 00:32:56.507
I don't know why either.

00:32:56.507 --> 00:32:58.676
So, let's weigh eight-piece nuggets.

00:32:59.777 --> 00:33:02.647
130 grams.

00:33:02.647 --> 00:33:05.717
Divide by eight equals

00:33:05.717 --> 00:33:09.687
16.25 grams per nugget.

00:33:09.687 --> 00:33:11.622
I don't know if we can get
as accurate of a measurement

00:33:11.622 --> 00:33:12.523
for something so small.

00:33:12.523 --> 00:33:16.427
So we will use this guy instead.

00:33:16.427 --> 00:33:20.064
So I'll just do this
and put this scale here.

00:33:22.233 --> 00:33:23.468
Ah!

00:33:23.468 --> 00:33:24.502
This is a bad idea.

00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:28.973
Eight pieces is 104 grams,

00:33:28.973 --> 00:33:33.544
divided by eight is 13 grams.

00:33:35.013 --> 00:33:37.181
In Japan, we have three drink sizes,

00:33:38.249 --> 00:33:39.083
small

00:33:40.551 --> 00:33:41.819
and medium

00:33:43.321 --> 00:33:44.922
and large.

00:33:46.057 --> 00:33:48.159
In the US, we have four drink sizes.

00:33:48.159 --> 00:33:50.294
Value, which only comes with a value meal;

00:33:50.294 --> 00:33:52.597
small; medium; and large.

00:33:52.597 --> 00:33:55.500
Now, I want to note that
the US's largest drink size

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:59.237
is 112% larger than Japan's largest drink.

00:34:02.373 --> 00:34:03.875
Now, what's the biggest meal

00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:06.144
you can get in Japan's Burger King?

00:34:06.144 --> 00:34:09.747
Over here, it's the King Meal.

00:34:09.747 --> 00:34:14.285
[singing "Circle of Life"]

00:34:14.285 --> 00:34:16.454
The King Meal ranges anywhere

00:34:16.454 --> 00:34:19.791
from 790 to 990 yen

00:34:19.791 --> 00:34:21.659
depending on the burger you choose.

00:34:21.659 --> 00:34:24.162
It has your choice of an avocado Whopper,

00:34:24.162 --> 00:34:26.631
double cheeseburger, or Whopper.

00:34:26.631 --> 00:34:28.900
We chose the double cheeseburger,

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:31.636
which comes with small fries,

00:34:31.636 --> 00:34:33.171
five-piece nuggets,

00:34:33.171 --> 00:34:36.007
medium Coke, and apple pie.

00:34:36.007 --> 00:34:39.644
And in the US, currently
our single biggest menu item

00:34:39.644 --> 00:34:43.014
at a Burger King is the
$30 Ultimate Party Bundle.

00:34:43.014 --> 00:34:45.216
Now, you could only
order this party bundle

00:34:45.216 --> 00:34:48.920
through the BK app, and
it includes two Whoppers,

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:50.254
two double cheeseburgers,

00:34:50.254 --> 00:34:51.789
two original chicken sandwiches,

00:34:51.789 --> 00:34:53.558
two eight-piece chicken nuggets,

00:34:53.558 --> 00:34:56.494
four small fries, and four small drinks.

00:34:56.494 --> 00:34:58.396
And it costs:

00:34:58.396 --> 00:35:00.131
$30.

00:35:00.131 --> 00:35:02.533
In Japan, a Whopper cheese set,

00:35:02.533 --> 00:35:07.305
it costs around 890 yen, or $7.80 US.

00:35:07.305 --> 00:35:08.739
Whereas in the US, the same meal

00:35:08.739 --> 00:35:11.943
with a small fry and drink is $9.29,

00:35:11.943 --> 00:35:15.980
or 1,059.65 Japanese yen.

00:35:15.980 --> 00:35:16.848
What about the medium?

00:35:16.848 --> 00:35:18.316
You get that with the
medium fry and medium drink,

00:35:18.316 --> 00:35:19.917
it's $10.29,

00:35:19.917 --> 00:35:24.889
or 1,173.71 Japanese yen.

00:35:25.089 --> 00:35:26.591
What about the large?

00:35:28.326 --> 00:35:30.461
Poof! Hey, there it is,
right in front of me.

00:35:30.461 --> 00:35:34.132
Large fries and drink, $11.29,

00:35:34.132 --> 00:35:39.003
or 1,287.78 Japanese yen.

00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.508
Let's look at calories.

00:35:43.508 --> 00:35:47.512
In Japan, a Whopper is 676 calories.

00:35:47.512 --> 00:35:49.413
The calories aren't too bad,

00:35:49.413 --> 00:35:52.150
but watch out for the sodium levels.

00:35:52.150 --> 00:35:55.286
One Japan Whopper is 113%

00:35:55.286 --> 00:35:58.022
of your daily recommended
amount of sodium.

00:35:58.022 --> 00:35:59.690
Too much!

00:35:59.690 --> 00:36:02.927
In the US, our Whopper is 667 calories.

00:36:02.927 --> 00:36:04.896
Both Whoppers are pretty comparable

00:36:04.896 --> 00:36:06.130
in most of the categories,

00:36:06.130 --> 00:36:08.633
but there's one statistic
that really stands out,

00:36:08.633 --> 00:36:09.867
the salt content.

00:36:09.867 --> 00:36:14.605
The sodium level in Japan's
Whopper is 122% higher

00:36:14.605 --> 00:36:16.240
than that in the US.

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:18.009
Let's make that a meal.

00:36:18.009 --> 00:36:20.611
A Whopper with large
fries and a large Coke

00:36:20.611 --> 00:36:24.015
is 1,323 calories.

00:36:24.015 --> 00:36:28.619
And the same meal in the
US is 1,680 calories,

00:36:28.619 --> 00:36:29.620
so a lot more.

00:36:29.620 --> 00:36:31.789
Now, a big portion of the calories

00:36:31.789 --> 00:36:34.025
actually come from the large Coke.

00:36:34.025 --> 00:36:37.929
The US's is roughly 182% more calories

00:36:37.929 --> 00:36:39.096
than that of Japan's.

00:36:39.096 --> 00:36:41.832
Let's look at the highest-calorie sandwich

00:36:41.832 --> 00:36:43.134
at Japan's Burger King.

00:36:43.134 --> 00:36:45.870
The double Whopper cheese is here.

00:36:45.870 --> 00:36:49.473
Eating one of these is already
half of your daily calories

00:36:49.473 --> 00:36:52.410
and a little over your
daily recommended protein.

00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:55.947
The main thing to watch
out for here is the sodium,

00:36:55.947 --> 00:37:00.518
which is 152% of your
daily recommended value.

00:37:00.518 --> 00:37:02.453
Whereas in the US, our
highest-calorie sandwich

00:37:02.453 --> 00:37:06.457
is the spicy chicken
deluxe sandwich, seen here.

00:37:06.457 --> 00:37:07.692
If you're worried about your health,

00:37:07.692 --> 00:37:08.960
steer clear of this one.

00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:13.698
The fat content is 190%
your daily allowance,

00:37:13.698 --> 00:37:18.669
and the sodium is over 200%
of your daily allowance.

00:37:18.669 --> 00:37:20.104
Yikes.

00:37:20.104 --> 00:37:21.539
As I mentioned earlier,

00:37:21.539 --> 00:37:24.542
the biggest menu item is the King Meal.

00:37:24.542 --> 00:37:27.411
If you get it with a
double bacon cheeseburger,

00:37:27.411 --> 00:37:31.449
the total calories are 1,329.

00:37:31.449 --> 00:37:34.885
That's 66% of your daily calories.

00:37:34.885 --> 00:37:38.189
And, of course, the $30
Ultimate Party Bundle,

00:37:38.189 --> 00:37:41.425
which is 8,903 calories,

00:37:41.425 --> 00:37:45.162
or 445% your daily

00:37:45.162 --> 00:37:47.064
caloric allowance.

00:37:50.701 --> 00:37:52.703
Burger King in Japan doesn't disclose

00:37:52.703 --> 00:37:54.405
the exact ingredients,

00:37:54.405 --> 00:37:57.708
but it does disclose where
the ingredients come from

00:37:57.708 --> 00:38:00.144
and where they're finished processing.

00:38:00.144 --> 00:38:02.079
For example, the Whopper beef patties

00:38:02.079 --> 00:38:05.983
are sourced from Australia,
New Zealand, and Europe,

00:38:05.983 --> 00:38:08.219
but they are processed in Australia,

00:38:08.219 --> 00:38:10.788
Japan, and Austria.

00:38:10.788 --> 00:38:12.189
Burger King in the US is pretty vague

00:38:12.189 --> 00:38:13.424
when it comes to its ingredients.

00:38:13.424 --> 00:38:16.494
They don't disclose a
comprehensive list anywhere.

00:38:16.494 --> 00:38:17.561
At the end of 2020,

00:38:17.561 --> 00:38:21.299
Burger King permanently
banned 120 artificial flavors

00:38:21.299 --> 00:38:24.135
from their menu, including aluminum,

00:38:24.135 --> 00:38:27.638
yellows 1 through 5, BHA, and BHT.

00:38:27.638 --> 00:38:29.674
Here's the complete list.

00:38:29.674 --> 00:38:31.776
It was actually a lot of stuff.

00:38:31.776 --> 00:38:32.810
Good for you guys.

00:38:33.311 --> 00:38:35.346
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:38:35.346 --> 00:38:37.148
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:38:37.148 --> 00:38:39.884
between Wendy's in Japan and the US.

00:38:39.884 --> 00:38:41.786
This is "Food Wars."

00:38:44.255 --> 00:38:46.090
In Japan, our Wendy's hamburgers

00:38:46.090 --> 00:38:47.625
come in four sizes:

00:38:47.625 --> 00:38:51.462
junior, single, double, and triple.

00:38:51.462 --> 00:38:54.298
In the US, our burgers come in four sizes:

00:38:54.298 --> 00:38:56.467
junior, Dave's single,

00:38:56.467 --> 00:38:59.770
Dave's double, and the Dave's triple.

00:38:59.770 --> 00:39:02.206
Look at the size of this thing.

00:39:05.076 --> 00:39:09.714
In Japan, our nuggets come
in orders of five and 10.

00:39:09.714 --> 00:39:12.550
Our US nuggets come in four, six,

00:39:12.550 --> 00:39:14.218
and 10-piece.

00:39:14.218 --> 00:39:16.487
Our Wendy's drinks come in three sizes:

00:39:16.487 --> 00:39:18.989
small, medium, and large.

00:39:18.989 --> 00:39:21.225
And in the US we also
have three drink sizes,

00:39:21.225 --> 00:39:22.860
small, medium,

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.161
you've gotta be kidding me.

00:39:24.161 --> 00:39:25.529
Look at the size of this thing.

00:39:25.529 --> 00:39:27.264
This might be 40 ounces, Yuelei.

00:39:27.264 --> 00:39:29.233
Only one way to find out.

00:39:29.233 --> 00:39:30.067
Ho!

00:39:31.402 --> 00:39:33.471
Oh, not quite 40.

00:39:33.471 --> 00:39:38.242
About 36 or 37 fluid ounces of Coca-Cola.

00:39:38.242 --> 00:39:39.710
And how big's a bladder?

00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:41.779
This looks like more
than I would normally pee

00:39:41.779 --> 00:39:42.646
in the morning.

00:39:42.646 --> 00:39:46.283
OK, let's measure our large drink.

00:39:47.318 --> 00:39:50.788
It measures exactly 500 milliliters.

00:39:51.655 --> 00:39:54.091
Our Wendy's fries come in two sizes.

00:39:54.091 --> 00:39:56.527
Small and medium.

00:39:56.527 --> 00:39:58.362
Our fries come in four sizes,

00:39:58.362 --> 00:40:02.032
junior, small, medium,

00:40:02.032 --> 00:40:03.701
pew, large.

00:40:03.701 --> 00:40:05.603
Let's weigh our largest.

00:40:05.603 --> 00:40:07.138
[laughs]

00:40:07.138 --> 00:40:10.908
Roughly 180 grams.

00:40:10.908 --> 00:40:14.078
It weighs 135 grams.

00:40:14.078 --> 00:40:16.280
Japan's chili comes in two sizes,

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:18.649
medium and large.

00:40:18.649 --> 00:40:21.252
And the US, our chili comes in two sizes,

00:40:21.252 --> 00:40:23.020
small and large.

00:40:23.020 --> 00:40:25.389
Let us weigh the largest now.

00:40:25.389 --> 00:40:29.126
Including the paper cup, 430 grams.

00:40:29.126 --> 00:40:31.929
George: Let's weigh our large chili.

00:40:31.929 --> 00:40:34.632
265 grams.

00:40:37.168 --> 00:40:39.537
In Japan, a Wendy's burger USA double

00:40:39.537 --> 00:40:44.442
is 730 yen, or $6.38.

00:40:44.442 --> 00:40:47.778
Our US Dave's double goes for $5.99,

00:40:47.778 --> 00:40:50.548
or around 685 Japanese yen.

00:40:50.548 --> 00:40:55.119
That's a 6.16% decrease
in price in the US.

00:40:55.119 --> 00:40:56.120
Let's make it a meal.

00:40:56.120 --> 00:40:58.789
In Japan, if you're getting
your burger as a set,

00:40:58.789 --> 00:41:00.391
it includes a small fries

00:41:00.391 --> 00:41:02.860
and a three-piece nuggets and a drink.

00:41:02.860 --> 00:41:05.396
It costs around 440 yen more.

00:41:05.396 --> 00:41:07.698
Our meals only include fries and drink.

00:41:07.698 --> 00:41:09.800
So a small Dave's double meal,

00:41:09.800 --> 00:41:10.868
and I threw in a four-piece

00:41:10.868 --> 00:41:12.203
because we don't have a three-piece,

00:41:12.203 --> 00:41:15.840
works out to $10.98.

00:41:15.840 --> 00:41:19.276
That's an 8.12% increased cost in the US.

00:41:19.276 --> 00:41:21.278
Mind you, we did get an extra nugget.

00:41:21.278 --> 00:41:22.913
Speaking of nuggets, in Japan,

00:41:22.913 --> 00:41:25.316
10-piece nugget is 510 yen,

00:41:25.316 --> 00:41:28.319
which breaks down to 51 yen per nugget.

00:41:28.319 --> 00:41:30.921
In the US, a 10-piece nugget is $4.29,

00:41:30.921 --> 00:41:34.692
which makes it per nugget around 43 cents.

00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:35.893
So per nugget average,

00:41:35.893 --> 00:41:38.929
the US is paying 8.11% less.

00:41:38.929 --> 00:41:40.498
A Baconator double in Japan

00:41:40.498 --> 00:41:45.169
is 850 yen, or $7.43.

00:41:45.169 --> 00:41:49.773
In the US, you get that
same Baconator for $7.49,

00:41:49.773 --> 00:41:52.810
or 857 Japanese yen.

00:41:52.810 --> 00:41:56.347
So close. Only a 0.82% increase.

00:41:58.749 --> 00:42:01.552
Here is everything you can
get at the Wendy's in Japan

00:42:01.552 --> 00:42:03.754
you cannot get in the US.

00:42:03.754 --> 00:42:05.422
And here's everything at a US Wendy's

00:42:05.422 --> 00:42:07.024
you can't get in Japan.

00:42:07.024 --> 00:42:09.727
One thing I want to point
out is that in Japan,

00:42:09.727 --> 00:42:13.130
Wendy's is known as Wendy's First Kitchen.

00:42:13.130 --> 00:42:15.599
First Kitchen is a
Japanese fast-food chain,

00:42:15.599 --> 00:42:18.736
and it was acquired by Wendy's in 2016

00:42:18.736 --> 00:42:22.039
and became a hybrid of Wendy's
and First Kitchen's menus.

00:42:22.039 --> 00:42:24.942
And we call them Fakkin,

00:42:24.942 --> 00:42:27.478
which is the abbreviation of First Kitchen

00:42:27.478 --> 00:42:28.712
in a Japanese way.

00:42:28.712 --> 00:42:30.881
It's like First Kitchen's "Fa"

00:42:30.881 --> 00:42:33.384
and kitchen's "ki" and "n."

00:42:33.384 --> 00:42:35.286
And say: Fakkin.

00:42:35.286 --> 00:42:38.322
Repeat after me: Fakkin.

00:42:38.322 --> 00:42:40.090
[beep]

00:42:40.090 --> 00:42:41.425
Got it, buddy.

00:42:41.425 --> 00:42:42.760
Very good!

00:42:42.760 --> 00:42:46.130
So, here are our Japan's
exclusive burgers.

00:42:46.130 --> 00:42:49.500
So, this one is bacon mushroom melt,

00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:52.002
and this one is just mushroom melt.

00:42:52.002 --> 00:42:55.606
We have Wendy's bacon egg burger.

00:42:55.606 --> 00:42:59.777
We also have Wendy's
cheese bacon egg burger,

00:42:59.777 --> 00:43:00.978
and this sauce,

00:43:02.279 --> 00:43:04.381
tartar sauce. Umai.

00:43:04.381 --> 00:43:06.817
Everybody's curious what this is.

00:43:06.817 --> 00:43:09.887
This one is Wild Rock.

00:43:09.887 --> 00:43:11.288
It's got no buns.

00:43:11.288 --> 00:43:13.290
It's got two beef patties.

00:43:13.290 --> 00:43:14.925
I think I should try this one.

00:43:14.925 --> 00:43:15.926
Itadakimasu.

00:43:17.428 --> 00:43:20.164
This meat itself has a good taste

00:43:20.164 --> 00:43:23.033
and some kind of, like, peppery flavor,

00:43:23.033 --> 00:43:25.235
but it's a little bit dry.

00:43:25.235 --> 00:43:26.670
I wouldn't get this again.

00:43:26.670 --> 00:43:28.005
And last things,

00:43:28.005 --> 00:43:30.975
we have junior teriyaki burger,

00:43:30.975 --> 00:43:34.545
and we have junior teriyaki cheeseburger.

00:43:35.779 --> 00:43:37.481
The big bacon cheeseburger.

00:43:37.481 --> 00:43:39.183
The big bacon double.

00:43:39.183 --> 00:43:42.486
Look at this! Yep, one, two,
three, the big bacon triple.

00:43:42.486 --> 00:43:47.124
I mean, I don't know what angle
is best to look at this at.

00:43:47.124 --> 00:43:49.660
And then we got big
bacons on the fancy bread.

00:43:49.660 --> 00:43:52.529
This must be the big bacons classicses.

00:43:52.529 --> 00:43:54.498
This looks like a big bacon --

00:43:54.498 --> 00:43:56.400
look, it's got shredded
cheese and stuff on this.

00:43:56.400 --> 00:43:59.370
Everything's bacon
something with these guys.

00:43:59.370 --> 00:44:01.538
At this point, it's just
like, how many slabs of meat

00:44:01.538 --> 00:44:03.407
do you want on your bacon sandwich?

00:44:03.407 --> 00:44:06.143
Two things you can get at a Wendy's

00:44:06.143 --> 00:44:08.545
in the US you cannot get in Japan

00:44:08.545 --> 00:44:11.849
or just the junior burger
and the junior cheeseburger.

00:44:11.849 --> 00:44:13.917
Look at this little guy. Look at this.

00:44:13.917 --> 00:44:15.919
Literally every fast-food burger place

00:44:15.919 --> 00:44:17.354
has a version of this.

00:44:17.354 --> 00:44:18.789
Chicken!

00:44:18.789 --> 00:44:20.224
[grunts]

00:44:20.224 --> 00:44:22.393
The Asiago chicken sandwiches.

00:44:22.393 --> 00:44:27.398
We got the Asiago chicken
ranch classic club.

00:44:27.398 --> 00:44:30.300
I said that in the wrong
order, but you get what I mean.

00:44:30.300 --> 00:44:31.568
Probably this one.

00:44:31.568 --> 00:44:35.606
This is the fried Asiago club with bacon.

00:44:35.606 --> 00:44:38.075
And then there is the spicy,

00:44:38.075 --> 00:44:40.444
which I'm assuming is this one.

00:44:40.444 --> 00:44:42.513
And then they got the grilled.

00:44:45.549 --> 00:44:46.884
That's pretty good.

00:44:46.884 --> 00:44:48.519
Don't like Asiago?

00:44:48.519 --> 00:44:49.887
Wendy's got you covered.

00:44:49.887 --> 00:44:52.122
So many chicken sandwiches at Wendy's

00:44:52.122 --> 00:44:54.591
that of course are not Asiago'd.

00:44:54.591 --> 00:44:56.493
This is the grilled chicken sandwich.

00:44:56.493 --> 00:44:59.296
As you can see, it is grilled.

00:44:59.296 --> 00:45:02.166
And then we have the
grilled chicken big bacon.

00:45:02.166 --> 00:45:05.736
Man, they must've gotten some
deal on bacon for Wendy's.

00:45:05.736 --> 00:45:07.037
Everything's got bacon on it!

00:45:07.037 --> 00:45:08.505
I'm going to go ahead
and assume this is the

00:45:08.505 --> 00:45:10.874
big bacon fried chicken sandwich,

00:45:10.874 --> 00:45:12.576
'cause it has bacon on it.

00:45:12.576 --> 00:45:15.412
So you have the spicy big
bacon cheddar chicken.

00:45:15.412 --> 00:45:18.282
In Japan, our Wendy's have pasta,

00:45:18.282 --> 00:45:20.651
which were originally on
the First Kitchen menu.

00:45:20.651 --> 00:45:24.021
So here we have
ramen-style soy cream pasta

00:45:24.021 --> 00:45:25.923
with spinach and ham.

00:45:25.923 --> 00:45:29.326
Expires 2023,

00:45:29.326 --> 00:45:31.161
January 20.

00:45:31.161 --> 00:45:33.597
Joe, I'll keep this for you.

00:45:33.597 --> 00:45:36.133
Nah, my guy, you can go
ahead and throw that out.

00:45:36.133 --> 00:45:40.304
And next we have ramen-style
dandan soup pasta

00:45:40.304 --> 00:45:42.673
with spinach and ham.

00:45:42.673 --> 00:45:46.810
So, dandan soup is kind of like
a spicy chili-flavored soup

00:45:46.810 --> 00:45:49.213
with miso and pork mince.

00:45:49.213 --> 00:45:53.684
Dandan soup and dandan ramen
are very popular in Japan.

00:45:53.684 --> 00:45:55.953
Tomato sauce pasta

00:45:55.953 --> 00:45:59.757
with mozzarella and bacon.

00:45:59.757 --> 00:46:04.027
All right, next we have beef
cheek meat cream spaghetti.

00:46:05.195 --> 00:46:06.296
Plastic.

00:46:06.296 --> 00:46:07.131
Mm.

00:46:08.332 --> 00:46:11.769
Next we have carbonara spaghetti.

00:46:11.769 --> 00:46:12.703
Naotomo: Carbon-AR-a.

00:46:12.703 --> 00:46:14.204
Carbon-AAH-ra.

00:46:14.204 --> 00:46:15.739
Carbona-rrra.

00:46:15.739 --> 00:46:16.840
A-rrra? OK.

00:46:16.840 --> 00:46:18.208
Carbra-rrra.

00:46:18.208 --> 00:46:19.176
[crew laughing]

00:46:19.176 --> 00:46:20.611
It's got bacon

00:46:20.611 --> 00:46:24.748
and this creamy carbona-rrra sauce.

00:46:24.748 --> 00:46:26.316
Molto bene!

00:46:26.316 --> 00:46:31.288
Last thing I have is
spicy cod roe spaghetti.

00:46:31.288 --> 00:46:35.392
So, spicy cod roe in Japanese is mentaiko,

00:46:35.392 --> 00:46:39.696
and mentaiko spaghetti is
also very popular in Japan.

00:46:39.696 --> 00:46:41.598
Unfortunately, some Americans I know

00:46:41.598 --> 00:46:43.700
don't like mentaiko so much

00:46:43.700 --> 00:46:45.869
because of the texture and smell.

00:46:45.869 --> 00:46:47.471
But for me, mentaiko,

00:46:47.471 --> 00:46:51.008
it's super Fakkin delicious.

00:46:51.008 --> 00:46:54.278
Uh, it's been a while
since I got this one.

00:46:54.278 --> 00:46:56.313
It's been, like, three hours.

00:46:56.313 --> 00:46:57.481
Itadakimasu.

00:47:00.350 --> 00:47:01.285
Mm.

00:47:01.285 --> 00:47:03.520
Joe, try it out.

00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:04.822
I appreciate the offer, George,

00:47:04.822 --> 00:47:06.657
but you can go ahead and finish that,

00:47:06.657 --> 00:47:09.560
'cause it looks Fakkin disgusting.

00:47:09.560 --> 00:47:10.894
We got salads.

00:47:10.894 --> 00:47:12.262
Over here on this end, the first one

00:47:12.262 --> 00:47:15.199
looks like we got the
Parmesan Caesar salad.

00:47:15.199 --> 00:47:17.568
Comes with, of course, Caesar dressing

00:47:17.568 --> 00:47:20.404
and what looks to be Parmesan crisps.

00:47:20.404 --> 00:47:22.706
This next salad is ridiculous.

00:47:22.706 --> 00:47:24.608
We're going to go ahead and
put quotes around salad.

00:47:24.608 --> 00:47:28.545
Wendy's has a taco "salad" that comes

00:47:28.545 --> 00:47:33.517
with tortilla chips, sour
cream, signature salsa,

00:47:33.517 --> 00:47:36.620
and, if that wasn't enough, chili.

00:47:36.620 --> 00:47:37.988
And before we continue,

00:47:37.988 --> 00:47:39.790
you confirmed that the taco salad

00:47:39.790 --> 00:47:41.391
is supposed to have chili on it?

00:47:41.391 --> 00:47:42.392
They told you that.

00:47:42.392 --> 00:47:44.761
Just gotta get the chips all around here.

00:47:44.761 --> 00:47:45.696
I can't believe this.

00:47:45.696 --> 00:47:47.364
This is so gross.

00:47:47.364 --> 00:47:50.934
Signature salsa, then chili.

00:47:50.934 --> 00:47:53.337
Oh, it smells so bad.

00:47:53.337 --> 00:47:55.239
Oh, God.

00:47:55.239 --> 00:47:56.073
Eh.

00:47:57.241 --> 00:47:58.575
I'm just -- this is just like eating chili

00:47:58.575 --> 00:48:00.110
with tortilla chips.

00:48:00.110 --> 00:48:00.911
They said there was some salt --

00:48:00.911 --> 00:48:02.613
I'm just pushing this s--- around.

00:48:04.448 --> 00:48:05.682
On to the next salad,

00:48:05.682 --> 00:48:08.385
the Southwest avocado salad.

00:48:08.385 --> 00:48:09.853
Oh, my God, there's bacon on it!

00:48:09.853 --> 00:48:10.821
That's weird.

00:48:10.821 --> 00:48:12.422
That was in Dave Thomas' obituary.

00:48:12.422 --> 00:48:14.057
"I want everything to
be covered in bacon."

00:48:14.057 --> 00:48:18.161
But yeah. Chicken, avocado,
bacon, cheese, and some sauce.

00:48:18.161 --> 00:48:18.996
This makes sense.

00:48:18.996 --> 00:48:21.265
And the last salad,

00:48:21.265 --> 00:48:22.499
apple pecan salad.

00:48:22.499 --> 00:48:23.400
That smells.

00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:25.535
Oh, 'cause it's got blue cheese on it.

00:48:25.535 --> 00:48:27.070
Roasted pecan bits.

00:48:27.070 --> 00:48:28.605
Pomegranate vinaigrette!

00:48:30.741 --> 00:48:32.109
Mm. Apples are nice.

00:48:32.109 --> 00:48:34.878
It's kind of nice to get a
little bit of actual fruit,

00:48:34.878 --> 00:48:36.413
something nutritious while doing this.

00:48:36.413 --> 00:48:38.582
It's like my body's like, "What is this?!"

00:48:38.582 --> 00:48:40.450
So, here are Japan's side menu.

00:48:40.450 --> 00:48:42.886
We have a few flavor options for fries.

00:48:42.886 --> 00:48:46.623
So we have happy butter flavor fries.

00:48:47.491 --> 00:48:49.493
Happy butter flavor.

00:48:49.493 --> 00:48:52.763
It has just subtle buttery flavor. Mm.

00:48:52.763 --> 00:48:56.066
Burnt butter soy sauce flavor.

00:48:56.066 --> 00:48:57.567
Rip it off. Bwah!

00:48:57.567 --> 00:49:00.570
I don't know what's going on
here, but it's pretty good.

00:49:00.570 --> 00:49:02.506
Much better than this.

00:49:02.506 --> 00:49:05.309
Savory steamed potato butter.

00:49:05.309 --> 00:49:08.045
It gets quite strong buttery flavor.

00:49:08.045 --> 00:49:09.913
Definitely I prefer this one

00:49:09.913 --> 00:49:12.082
than the happy butter flavor.

00:49:12.082 --> 00:49:13.550
This is not happy.

00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:17.187
This one is chicken consommé flavor.

00:49:17.187 --> 00:49:18.355
Mm.

00:49:18.355 --> 00:49:21.491
This is the best fries
I've ever had in my life.

00:49:21.491 --> 00:49:23.894
Now I'm going to introduce you

00:49:23.894 --> 00:49:28.498
this spicy chicken breast.

00:49:28.498 --> 00:49:30.934
Wendy's in the US also has baked potatoes.

00:49:30.934 --> 00:49:31.902
See what we got.

00:49:31.902 --> 00:49:34.838
Of course, there's your regular.

00:49:34.838 --> 00:49:36.173
And this one, oh, yeah.

00:49:36.173 --> 00:49:38.275
This one's got, like,
chives and stuff in it.

00:49:38.275 --> 00:49:40.444
If I was to stop here, you would go,

00:49:40.444 --> 00:49:44.481
"Wow, what a tasteful
selection of healthy potatoes."

00:49:44.481 --> 00:49:46.616
But of course we don't stop here.

00:49:46.616 --> 00:49:51.321
We move on to absolute
baked-potato madness.

00:49:51.321 --> 00:49:53.924
Ah, No. 1, oof.

00:49:53.924 --> 00:49:55.392
Cheese baked potato.

00:49:55.392 --> 00:49:57.160
Drowned this thing in cheese.

00:49:57.160 --> 00:49:58.628
It's like -- ooh!

00:49:58.628 --> 00:50:00.697
It's, like, caked to the side. Blech.

00:50:00.697 --> 00:50:02.199
Ugh. Ugh.

00:50:02.199 --> 00:50:05.502
Oh, God! [laughs]

00:50:05.502 --> 00:50:08.138
The chili and cheese baked potato.

00:50:08.138 --> 00:50:09.306
Blech.

00:50:09.306 --> 00:50:12.109
If you are like me, you're
wondering to yourself,

00:50:12.109 --> 00:50:13.577
something's missing.

00:50:13.577 --> 00:50:18.048
Something is missing from
this potato menu, Yuelei!

00:50:18.048 --> 00:50:19.449
Can you guess what that is?

00:50:19.449 --> 00:50:22.953
The bacon cheese baked potato!

00:50:22.953 --> 00:50:25.489
Oh, they got big pieces
of bacon on this one too.

00:50:25.489 --> 00:50:26.523
Oof!

00:50:26.523 --> 00:50:28.392
You can get spicy chicken nuggets.

00:50:28.392 --> 00:50:29.693
Yessiree Bob.

00:50:30.627 --> 00:50:32.496
Seasoned potatoes.

00:50:32.496 --> 00:50:34.498
All right, so fruit finally made the menu.

00:50:34.498 --> 00:50:35.332
Apple slices.

00:50:35.332 --> 00:50:37.367
It wouldn't be a Wendy's category

00:50:37.367 --> 00:50:39.870
without the Baconator fries.

00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:42.105
We need the bacon meter in this episode.

00:50:42.105 --> 00:50:43.673
Last of the sides.

00:50:43.673 --> 00:50:44.875
Oh, yeah.

00:50:44.875 --> 00:50:45.876
Oatmeal bar.

00:50:45.876 --> 00:50:47.010
Looks like a Clif bar.

00:50:48.745 --> 00:50:50.414
Whoa, that's actually pretty good.

00:50:50.414 --> 00:50:53.617
So, here are our Japan's exclusive drinks.

00:50:53.617 --> 00:50:56.787
We have tapioca royal
milk tea with brown sugar

00:50:56.787 --> 00:50:59.890
and tapioca milk with brown sugar.

00:50:59.890 --> 00:51:00.991
Tornado.

00:51:02.459 --> 00:51:03.527
Mm!

00:51:04.761 --> 00:51:06.430
This is amazing.

00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:07.697
Simply amazing.

00:51:07.697 --> 00:51:08.598
I love this.

00:51:08.598 --> 00:51:10.400
So, here are our other drinks.

00:51:10.400 --> 00:51:14.004
We have Pepsi, orange juice,

00:51:14.004 --> 00:51:15.672
and ginger ale,

00:51:15.672 --> 00:51:18.508
lemonade and melon soda,

00:51:18.508 --> 00:51:21.144
peach tea and iced tea,

00:51:21.144 --> 00:51:24.781
iced matcha, and this one is iced cocoa.

00:51:24.781 --> 00:51:27.684
So, here we have our hot drinks.

00:51:27.684 --> 00:51:30.787
We have Darjeeling tea,

00:51:30.787 --> 00:51:33.290
and we have café mocha,

00:51:33.290 --> 00:51:35.625
and we have peach tea.

00:51:35.625 --> 00:51:36.927
Mm.

00:51:36.927 --> 00:51:38.095
I like this.

00:51:38.095 --> 00:51:40.130
And we have café latte

00:51:40.130 --> 00:51:41.631
and cocoa

00:51:41.631 --> 00:51:43.834
and matcha.

00:51:43.834 --> 00:51:45.936
This is matcha, but it looks like

00:51:45.936 --> 00:51:49.072
water from 100 years ago.

00:51:49.072 --> 00:51:51.241
Our Wendy's has Frosty-ccinos,

00:51:51.241 --> 00:51:54.578
which I'm assuming are
Frostys meet Frappuccinos?

00:51:54.578 --> 00:51:55.779
Frosty-ccinos?

00:51:55.779 --> 00:51:59.015
But it does not appear that
there's Frostys in this.

00:51:59.015 --> 00:52:02.018
They have two flavors,
vanilla and chocolate.

00:52:02.018 --> 00:52:04.454
I'm assuming this is the vanilla.

00:52:04.454 --> 00:52:06.656
Wendy's did smart on this
one. It isn't that sweet.

00:52:06.656 --> 00:52:09.860
I was expecting it to
be, like, undrinkable,

00:52:09.860 --> 00:52:10.927
but it's actually kind of nice.

00:52:10.927 --> 00:52:13.363
All right, this one is the chocolate.

00:52:13.363 --> 00:52:14.197
Yeah.

00:52:14.197 --> 00:52:16.366
Also, it's a nice flavor.

00:52:16.366 --> 00:52:17.701
'Cause of the Frosty-ccinos,

00:52:17.701 --> 00:52:19.069
you know what that means.

00:52:19.069 --> 00:52:20.437
At Wendy's you can also get:

00:52:20.437 --> 00:52:22.105
booyah, Frostys.

00:52:22.105 --> 00:52:23.740
They don't have these in Japan?

00:52:23.740 --> 00:52:26.176
I feel like this is the staple menu item.

00:52:27.444 --> 00:52:32.382
[laughs]

00:52:33.583 --> 00:52:34.951
I love these so much.

00:52:38.221 --> 00:52:41.124
Fantastic. That's fantastic.

00:52:41.124 --> 00:52:42.159
Gotta go for the chocolate.

00:52:42.159 --> 00:52:43.160
Don't bother finding me a spoon.

00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:44.494
I'm just gonna do a little taste here.

00:52:44.494 --> 00:52:45.629
That's great.

00:52:45.629 --> 00:52:47.063
The Frostys are great.

00:52:47.063 --> 00:52:50.300
It's like a milkshake, but
it's super thick and delicious.

00:52:50.300 --> 00:52:52.602
Japan, you want this.

00:52:52.602 --> 00:52:53.503
Thick.

00:52:53.503 --> 00:52:54.871
It is thick!

00:52:54.871 --> 00:52:58.441
In Japan, we have floats
instead of Frostys.

00:52:58.441 --> 00:53:00.310
We have Coke float

00:53:00.310 --> 00:53:02.712
and melon soda float.

00:53:02.712 --> 00:53:06.149
Japan has an exclusive breakfast sandwich.

00:53:06.149 --> 00:53:09.386
It's called the breakfast sandwich.

00:53:09.386 --> 00:53:11.755
It's got tomato, lettuce,

00:53:11.755 --> 00:53:16.193
and I believe this is
beef or pork patties.

00:53:17.661 --> 00:53:20.230
OK, whereas Japan has one
exclusive breakfast sandwich,

00:53:20.230 --> 00:53:21.698
we have way more.

00:53:21.698 --> 00:53:23.166
Like all the fast food here in America,

00:53:23.166 --> 00:53:25.402
we take our breakfast very seriously.

00:53:25.402 --> 00:53:29.940
You can get yourself a
maple bacon croissant.

00:53:29.940 --> 00:53:31.741
It looks like it's a chicken sandwich

00:53:31.741 --> 00:53:36.112
that of course has bacon and
maple syrup on the croissant.

00:53:36.112 --> 00:53:38.315
We have what just appears
to be the bacon biscuit.

00:53:38.315 --> 00:53:41.284
Bacon, egg, cheese

00:53:41.284 --> 00:53:43.920
in the incredibly dry biscuit.

00:53:43.920 --> 00:53:45.388
Bacon croissant.

00:53:45.388 --> 00:53:46.590
I don't know about this one.

00:53:46.590 --> 00:53:50.794
Moving on to the sausage zone
of the Wendy's breakfast.

00:53:50.794 --> 00:53:53.830
This is the special sausage biscuit.

00:53:53.830 --> 00:53:56.132
No, no, no, no, no.

00:53:56.132 --> 00:53:57.234
Here's what I hate about this.

00:53:57.234 --> 00:54:00.070
Pick a drier thing to have for breakfast.

00:54:00.070 --> 00:54:02.105
I feel like it'd be impossible
to swallow a bite of this.

00:54:02.105 --> 00:54:03.640
You're going to choke on it.

00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:05.642
Here we go. See, this is
what I'm talking about.

00:54:05.642 --> 00:54:06.676
They might have gotten this backwards.

00:54:06.676 --> 00:54:08.578
This is actually the better sausage one.

00:54:08.578 --> 00:54:10.046
This at least has a better chance

00:54:10.046 --> 00:54:11.581
of not getting stuck in your throat.

00:54:11.581 --> 00:54:14.951
The sausage croissant
also has egg. Thank you.

00:54:14.951 --> 00:54:18.088
They have a few things that
are honey-butter-based.

00:54:18.088 --> 00:54:19.656
I am so glad that fast-food places

00:54:19.656 --> 00:54:22.292
are introducing honey
to their breakfast menu.

00:54:22.292 --> 00:54:23.326
I think maybe it has to do with the fact

00:54:23.326 --> 00:54:25.095
that chicken sandwiches
have become so popular.

00:54:25.095 --> 00:54:27.264
First one we got here is
the honey butter biscuit.

00:54:27.264 --> 00:54:29.032
[laughs]

00:54:29.032 --> 00:54:31.268
Hey, it's just a biscuit
with honey butter.

00:54:31.268 --> 00:54:33.570
I mean, yeah, I'll have this anytime.

00:54:33.570 --> 00:54:34.838
I'll have this anytime.

00:54:34.838 --> 00:54:36.773
This one has some heft to it.

00:54:36.773 --> 00:54:38.575
It's the hot honey biscuit.

00:54:38.575 --> 00:54:40.844
Yeah!

00:54:42.012 --> 00:54:43.713
A little chicken on there.

00:54:43.713 --> 00:54:44.547
Yep.

00:54:47.417 --> 00:54:49.119
I really like that.

00:54:49.119 --> 00:54:52.989
This is the special chicken croissant.

00:54:52.989 --> 00:54:55.725
So, here are our desserts.

00:54:55.725 --> 00:54:58.228
So here we have Melotozzo.

00:54:58.228 --> 00:55:00.897
So, Melotozzo are
maritozzo-style pastries,

00:55:00.897 --> 00:55:03.199
which are popular in
Rome and Japan as well,

00:55:03.199 --> 00:55:05.001
made with melon bread.

00:55:05.001 --> 00:55:07.437
So melon bread is a type
of sweet Japanese bread

00:55:07.437 --> 00:55:10.206
which has a sugar cookie
crust on the surface.

00:55:10.206 --> 00:55:11.708
But what's funny is that

00:55:11.708 --> 00:55:14.811
it doesn't have a melon flavor at all.

00:55:14.811 --> 00:55:15.645
At all.

00:55:15.645 --> 00:55:17.247
The reason it's called melon bread

00:55:17.247 --> 00:55:19.449
is that it just looks like melon.

00:55:19.449 --> 00:55:21.518
Does it look like melon?

00:55:21.518 --> 00:55:22.819
It does in Japan.

00:55:24.287 --> 00:55:25.755
Oh!

00:55:25.755 --> 00:55:26.890
And this time,

00:55:26.890 --> 00:55:30.627
First Kitchen made a
maritozzo using melon bread

00:55:30.627 --> 00:55:32.696
and mascarpone cheese whipped cream,

00:55:32.696 --> 00:55:34.998
and it's called Melotozzo.

00:55:34.998 --> 00:55:38.635
So here we have Melotozzo tiramisu

00:55:38.635 --> 00:55:41.738
and Melotozzo matcha and Melotozzo plain.

00:55:41.738 --> 00:55:45.975
So, actually, yesterday was
my birthday, February 18.

00:55:45.975 --> 00:55:48.411
Hey, it's your birthday!
Happy birthday, George!

00:55:48.411 --> 00:55:51.748
Thank you for your message!
Thank you! Arigatou gozaimasu!

00:55:51.748 --> 00:55:54.551
So this is my birthday present.

00:55:54.551 --> 00:55:57.454
All right, so let's give it a shot.

00:55:57.454 --> 00:56:00.323
Best birthday present ever.

00:56:00.323 --> 00:56:01.324
Itadakimasu.

00:56:02.859 --> 00:56:05.495
This is so good.

00:56:05.495 --> 00:56:08.198
I can't stop eating this.

00:56:08.198 --> 00:56:09.532
Mm.

00:56:09.532 --> 00:56:12.769
So, Wendy's in Japan has a
Japanese traditional sweet

00:56:12.769 --> 00:56:15.605
since it has been a
collaboration with First Kitchen.

00:56:15.605 --> 00:56:19.042
So we have shiratama cream zenzai.

00:56:19.042 --> 00:56:20.076
Ooh.

00:56:20.076 --> 00:56:23.179
So it has three main
ingredients, ice cream,

00:56:23.179 --> 00:56:25.715
and sweet red beans, and the shiratama,

00:56:25.715 --> 00:56:27.917
which is kind of like a mochi rice cake.

00:56:27.917 --> 00:56:31.388
And my grandma likes this type of zenzai.

00:56:31.388 --> 00:56:33.123
This is for you, my grandma.

00:56:33.123 --> 00:56:36.760
And also we have mini pancakes.

00:56:36.760 --> 00:56:38.762
In the US, we only have
two exclusive desserts,

00:56:38.762 --> 00:56:39.596
and they're both cookies.

00:56:39.596 --> 00:56:40.997
And that's no disrespect to cookies,

00:56:40.997 --> 00:56:42.866
cookies are great, but I want one of those

00:56:42.866 --> 00:56:45.168
fun Italian ice cream sandwiches they had.

00:56:45.168 --> 00:56:47.370
Anyway, you can get two
cookies here in the US,

00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:50.807
a chocolate chunk cookie
and a sugar cookie.

00:56:53.109 --> 00:56:56.913
Our Wendy's double burger is 578 calories

00:56:56.913 --> 00:57:00.250
and 29% of your daily recommended amount

00:57:00.250 --> 00:57:03.987
and 60% of the recommended daily sodium.

00:57:03.987 --> 00:57:06.956
Our double burger, the Dave's
double, isn't much better.

00:57:06.956 --> 00:57:09.426
Ours is 850 calories

00:57:09.426 --> 00:57:12.796
and way more fat. Over 70%!

00:57:12.796 --> 00:57:14.798
But less sodium,

00:57:14.798 --> 00:57:16.833
just a bit over half of the daily amount.

00:57:16.833 --> 00:57:18.768
Still, not great.

00:57:18.768 --> 00:57:20.470
Make it a meal in Japan,

00:57:20.470 --> 00:57:24.374
and that increases the calories to 1,089.

00:57:24.374 --> 00:57:29.145
That's 55% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

00:57:29.145 --> 00:57:31.448
And if you make it a combo
here, we chose the small

00:57:31.448 --> 00:57:33.216
and took a few sips,

00:57:33.216 --> 00:57:35.552
that's 440 more calories,

00:57:35.552 --> 00:57:38.621
bringing the total to 1,290,

00:57:38.621 --> 00:57:42.258
or 64.5% of your daily allowance.

00:57:42.258 --> 00:57:45.595
In Japan, the single menu
item with the most calories

00:57:45.595 --> 00:57:48.331
is the eight-piece fried-chicken pack,

00:57:48.331 --> 00:57:53.136
which contains [gasps] 4,018 calories,

00:57:53.136 --> 00:57:56.372
201% of your daily calories.

00:57:56.372 --> 00:57:58.675
In the US, our single
biggest-calorie menu item

00:57:58.675 --> 00:58:00.810
is the Feed the Fam deal.

00:58:00.810 --> 00:58:03.313
A fam, yeah, right! This is all for you.

00:58:03.313 --> 00:58:05.448
It is two spicy chicken sandwiches,

00:58:05.448 --> 00:58:07.183
two junior bacon cheeseburgers,

00:58:07.183 --> 00:58:10.019
and four small fries.

00:58:10.019 --> 00:58:12.455
Total 2,780 calories,

00:58:12.455 --> 00:58:17.060
which is 139% of your daily intake.

00:58:18.928 --> 00:58:22.799
Japan's Wendy's doesn't
disclose their ingredients list.

00:58:22.799 --> 00:58:24.167
Why, Japan?

00:58:24.167 --> 00:58:25.435
The US sure does.

00:58:25.435 --> 00:58:28.471
Now, is there anything we
should be looking out for?

00:58:28.471 --> 00:58:29.472
Of course there is.

00:58:29.472 --> 00:58:30.807
Let's start with sodium nitrate,

00:58:30.807 --> 00:58:34.210
which is found in the Baconator's
applewood-smoked bacon.

00:58:34.210 --> 00:58:37.413
Sodium nitrate is a chemical
that is used to cure meats

00:58:37.413 --> 00:58:40.550
and gives meat that appealing pink color.

00:58:40.550 --> 00:58:41.951
Perfect for bacon.

00:58:41.951 --> 00:58:43.520
Also, get this,

00:58:43.520 --> 00:58:44.921
it's super toxic.

00:58:44.921 --> 00:58:46.923
It is restricted for purchase online.

00:58:46.923 --> 00:58:49.626
People have accidentally
eaten too much of it and died.

00:58:49.626 --> 00:58:52.829
It's also been used in homicides. Yikes!

00:58:52.829 --> 00:58:54.531
Sodium nitrate is on a list

00:58:54.531 --> 00:58:57.300
of Japan's designated food additives,

00:58:57.300 --> 00:59:00.837
but our Wendy's gets its
bacon imported from Denmark,

00:59:00.837 --> 00:59:04.574
where it isn't banned,
but being reduced in use.

00:59:04.574 --> 00:59:06.476
Our American cheese contains lecithin,

00:59:06.476 --> 00:59:08.978
a common emulsifier that,
according to one academic,

00:59:08.978 --> 00:59:12.549
a worrisome number of scientific
studies have suggested

00:59:12.549 --> 00:59:15.785
that too much of it
can promote depression.

00:59:15.785 --> 00:59:16.786
[sighs]

00:59:16.786 --> 00:59:18.621
The pickles contain polysorbate 80.

00:59:18.621 --> 00:59:22.225
This is commonly used as
an emulsifier in foods,

00:59:22.225 --> 00:59:25.295
but in pickles, it tends to
be used as a solubilizer.

00:59:25.295 --> 00:59:26.863
Not how that's pronounced, sorry.

00:59:26.863 --> 00:59:29.899
Which helps other ingredients
in the brine fully dissolve.

00:59:29.899 --> 00:59:33.169
Studies have suggested it can
cause colon cancer in mice.

00:59:33.169 --> 00:59:34.604
Not fantastic.

00:59:34.604 --> 00:59:36.506
There is no info on Wendy's website

00:59:36.506 --> 00:59:38.541
of where the pickles come from,

00:59:38.541 --> 00:59:41.778
but we want to point
out that polysorbate 80

00:59:41.778 --> 00:59:44.714
is on Japan's list of
designated additives.

00:59:44.714 --> 00:59:48.518
And therefore, it's permitted
to be used in Japan.

00:59:48.751 --> 00:59:50.887
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:59:50.887 --> 00:59:52.689
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:59:52.689 --> 00:59:55.291
between Domino's in Japan and the US.

00:59:55.291 --> 00:59:57.393
This is "Food Wars."

01:00:00.363 --> 01:00:02.799
In Japan, Domino's pizzas
come in three sizes.

01:00:02.799 --> 01:00:05.401
Our Domino's pizza comes in four sizes.

01:00:05.401 --> 01:00:08.905
George: So, this one is medium,
which is cut into 8 slices.

01:00:08.905 --> 01:00:10.640
Joe: Over here on this
end, you got the small.

01:00:10.640 --> 01:00:13.376
That's 10-inch pizza.

01:00:13.376 --> 01:00:17.380
And here's regular, which is
also cut into eight slices.

01:00:17.380 --> 01:00:18.615
Joe: Next up is our medium.

01:00:18.615 --> 01:00:20.917
That's a 12-inch pizza.

01:00:20.917 --> 01:00:23.019
And this one is large.

01:00:23.019 --> 01:00:26.022
This one is cut into 12 slices.

01:00:26.022 --> 01:00:30.126
Joe: Then we move to our large, 14 inches.

01:00:30.126 --> 01:00:34.330
And finally, the extra
large, which is 16 inches.

01:00:34.330 --> 01:00:35.832
Look at all that grease.

01:00:41.371 --> 01:00:45.541
A Domino's large plain pizza
has a 33-centimeters diameter

01:00:45.541 --> 01:00:50.113
or an 855.3-square-centimeters area

01:00:50.113 --> 01:00:52.448
and costs 2,000 yen.

01:00:52.448 --> 01:00:53.716
So breaking that down,

01:00:53.716 --> 01:00:57.553
our pizza is 2.33 yen per square inch,

01:00:57.553 --> 01:00:59.656
or about 2 cents.

01:00:59.656 --> 01:01:02.125
Now take our large.
This is a 14-inch pizza,

01:01:02.125 --> 01:01:05.461
also a 35.56-centimeter pizza.

01:01:05.461 --> 01:01:06.896
And it has a surface area

01:01:06.896 --> 01:01:11.100
of 993.1 square centimeters.

01:01:11.100 --> 01:01:14.037
That's 1.4 cents per square inch,

01:01:14.037 --> 01:01:17.206
or 1.62 Japanese yen.

01:01:17.206 --> 01:01:21.310
But what gives you the
most food for your money?

01:01:21.310 --> 01:01:24.681
So, here's a large plain
slice with a pan crust.

01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:27.950
And here's another with hand-tossed crust.

01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:30.820
Let's weigh both right
now and see which is more.

01:01:30.820 --> 01:01:33.623
So, first let's weigh pan crust.

01:01:34.457 --> 01:01:36.125
51 grams.

01:01:36.125 --> 01:01:38.528
And hand-tossed crust.

01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:41.664
It weighs 49 grams.

01:01:41.664 --> 01:01:43.299
And we will do the same.

01:01:43.299 --> 01:01:45.868
I want to note that right now in America,

01:01:45.868 --> 01:01:49.372
you can only get the pan
Domino's in the medium size.

01:01:49.372 --> 01:01:52.241
Same exact experiment, only
I'm doing two medium pizzas.

01:01:52.241 --> 01:01:54.877
Medium pan slice, medium
hand-tossed slice.

01:01:54.877 --> 01:01:59.882
So, this is the hand-tossed slice,

01:01:59.882 --> 01:02:01.150
and it weighs

01:02:02.285 --> 01:02:04.253
a smidge over 75.

01:02:04.253 --> 01:02:05.288
We'll go 76.

01:02:05.288 --> 01:02:06.656
The pan.

01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:09.992
That goes in there too.

01:02:09.992 --> 01:02:11.861
110 grams.

01:02:11.861 --> 01:02:15.565
Making the difference this amount.

01:02:15.565 --> 01:02:17.200
I'm not doing math.

01:02:17.200 --> 01:02:20.069
In Japan, we have seven
different crust options.

01:02:20.069 --> 01:02:22.939
No. 1, we have pan.

01:02:22.939 --> 01:02:26.042
And No. 2 we have hand-tossed.

01:02:26.976 --> 01:02:30.813
And No. 3, we have ultra-crispy.

01:02:30.813 --> 01:02:31.681
Ooh.

01:02:31.681 --> 01:02:33.483
It's like a cracker.

01:02:35.184 --> 01:02:38.488
No. 4, we have cheese burst,

01:02:38.488 --> 01:02:42.225
where a string cheese is placed
around the edge of the crust

01:02:42.225 --> 01:02:45.461
and sprinkled with consommé
Parmesan seasoning.

01:02:45.461 --> 01:02:46.796
Ooh.

01:02:46.796 --> 01:02:50.233
No. 5, we have the cheese 'n' roll.

01:02:51.200 --> 01:02:54.303
It's got mozzarella cheese in the crust.

01:02:54.303 --> 01:02:58.541
And No. 6, we have mille-filet.

01:02:58.541 --> 01:03:01.611
Or mill-foy.

01:03:01.611 --> 01:03:03.679
Mille-fail.

01:03:03.679 --> 01:03:06.482
In Japanese we say mi-ru fi-yu.

01:03:06.482 --> 01:03:08.618
So this one is mi-ru-fi-yu pizza,

01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:10.586
which has two layers of crust

01:03:10.586 --> 01:03:13.189
with Camembert mixed cheese in between.

01:03:13.189 --> 01:03:14.757
Mille-fail.

01:03:14.757 --> 01:03:16.559
Mille-fee-yuh.

01:03:16.559 --> 01:03:19.629
French people, please
correct my pronunciation.

01:03:19.629 --> 01:03:22.398
No. 7, the last one we have,

01:03:22.398 --> 01:03:24.901
the triple mille-feuille.

01:03:24.901 --> 01:03:28.571
It's got three layers of
crust with cheese in between.

01:03:28.571 --> 01:03:29.438
Wow.

01:03:29.438 --> 01:03:32.275
In the US, we have only
five crust options.

01:03:32.275 --> 01:03:34.010
I realize there's four
pizzas in front of me.

01:03:34.010 --> 01:03:34.844
Let me explain.

01:03:34.844 --> 01:03:36.612
One crust option you can get here,

01:03:36.612 --> 01:03:40.483
and it's a small only,
is the gluten-free crust.

01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:45.488
I don't know how bread is gluten-free,

01:03:45.655 --> 01:03:47.790
but we figured it out.

01:03:47.790 --> 01:03:48.724
Ta-da.

01:03:48.724 --> 01:03:51.294
We also have the hand-tossed,

01:03:51.294 --> 01:03:54.297
which is more of a standard pillowy,

01:03:54.297 --> 01:03:55.498
I mean, right, this is
like standard dough,

01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:56.799
this is what we think a pizza looks like.

01:03:56.799 --> 01:03:59.202
This is the pan.

01:03:59.202 --> 01:04:00.603
Look how thick that is, man.

01:04:00.603 --> 01:04:02.638
That's, like, triple the dough thickness.

01:04:02.638 --> 01:04:03.840
Good on you for the pan.

01:04:03.840 --> 01:04:06.175
Now, you can get this in the medium only.

01:04:06.175 --> 01:04:09.011
We also have a crunchy thin crust.

01:04:09.011 --> 01:04:10.947
And we have so many
pizzas here, to be honest,

01:04:10.947 --> 01:04:12.181
I don't know which one it is.

01:04:12.181 --> 01:04:14.917
So when it just comes up in
the video, I'll show it off.

01:04:14.917 --> 01:04:17.887
But imagine a crunchy thin pizza.

01:04:17.887 --> 01:04:19.422
Oddly enough, we also
have something called

01:04:19.422 --> 01:04:20.723
the Brooklyn-style pizza.

01:04:20.723 --> 01:04:23.392
This is reserved for large
and extra-large pizzas only.

01:04:23.392 --> 01:04:26.295
And this is a Brooklyn-style
right here, extra large.

01:04:26.295 --> 01:04:28.865
Obviously it isn't crispy,
because it's sagging.

01:04:28.865 --> 01:04:30.299
This is really thin.

01:04:32.802 --> 01:04:35.571
Here's everything you can
get at the Japanese Domino's

01:04:35.571 --> 01:04:38.207
that you cannot get in the US.

01:04:38.207 --> 01:04:40.209
Here's everything you
can get at a US Domino's

01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:41.844
you cannot get in Japan.

01:04:41.844 --> 01:04:44.313
Everyone, look at this.

01:04:44.313 --> 01:04:47.016
This is a limited-time-offer pizza.

01:04:47.016 --> 01:04:50.019
It's called the Best 34.

01:04:50.019 --> 01:04:51.287
Look at this lid.

01:04:51.287 --> 01:04:53.689
It's disgusting!

01:04:53.689 --> 01:04:56.192
Don't look at me! Don't look at me!

01:04:56.192 --> 01:04:59.662
So, this one has all 34 Domino's toppings,

01:04:59.662 --> 01:05:04.133
like teriyaki chicken, mayo,
spinach, tomato, shrimp.

01:05:04.133 --> 01:05:06.168
This is huge.

01:05:06.168 --> 01:05:08.170
It's like my baby.

01:05:08.170 --> 01:05:12.008
[sings lullaby]

01:05:13.109 --> 01:05:15.111
The New Yorker-style pizza is similar

01:05:15.111 --> 01:05:18.214
to the Brooklyn XL option
you can get in America.

01:05:18.214 --> 01:05:21.450
But only in Japan you can
get the Quattro New Yorker.

01:05:21.450 --> 01:05:24.887
It's a 16-inch pizza with
each New Yorker topping style

01:05:24.887 --> 01:05:26.956
covering a quarter of the pizza.

01:05:26.956 --> 01:05:30.760
So one quarter is pepperoni,
and one is cheese,

01:05:30.760 --> 01:05:32.862
and one is pepperoni and sausage,

01:05:32.862 --> 01:05:35.197
and one is ham and mushroom.

01:05:35.197 --> 01:05:38.401
So, here we have Nippon favorites series.

01:05:38.401 --> 01:05:41.938
Nippon, or Nihon, means Japan in Japanese.

01:05:41.938 --> 01:05:44.440
So these pizzas feature
Japanese ingredients.

01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:46.876
This one charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken.

01:05:46.876 --> 01:05:50.646
It's got teriyaki chicken, teriyaki sauce,

01:05:50.646 --> 01:05:53.983
spinach, mayonnaise, and corn.

01:05:53.983 --> 01:05:56.752
Next we have Hokkaido three cheeses.

01:05:56.752 --> 01:06:00.523
So, Hokkaido is the northern
island prefecture in Japan,

01:06:00.523 --> 01:06:03.225
and it's famous for its cheese.

01:06:03.225 --> 01:06:05.094
It's got Hokkaido Gouda cheese,

01:06:05.094 --> 01:06:06.729
Hokkaido cheddar cheese,

01:06:06.729 --> 01:06:09.865
and Hokkaido Camembert
and sliced asparagus.

01:06:09.865 --> 01:06:12.401
We have spicy mayo and mochi.

01:06:12.401 --> 01:06:15.404
It's got mochi rice cake and corn,

01:06:15.404 --> 01:06:18.374
pork sausage and sliced asparagus,

01:06:18.374 --> 01:06:20.142
and Korean seaweed flakes.

01:06:20.142 --> 01:06:22.812
And last one, we've got
charcoal-grilled beef

01:06:22.812 --> 01:06:24.714
and spinach and mushrooms.

01:06:27.550 --> 01:06:29.418
Mm!

01:06:29.418 --> 01:06:30.853
Oh!

01:06:30.853 --> 01:06:32.154
Umai!

01:06:33.155 --> 01:06:34.857
Umai!

01:06:34.857 --> 01:06:37.093
This beef is so tender,

01:06:37.093 --> 01:06:42.098
and it's got so much,
like, charcoal flavor,

01:06:42.098 --> 01:06:44.000
which makes this amazing.

01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:45.267
I love this.

01:06:45.267 --> 01:06:47.570
So many exclusive pizzas
here at the US Domino's.

01:06:47.570 --> 01:06:48.437
I don't know where to begin,

01:06:48.437 --> 01:06:50.239
so I'll just start with
this one that I'm holding.

01:06:50.239 --> 01:06:54.710
This is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

01:06:54.710 --> 01:06:58.748
I don't know what makes it
California-in-y or Cali-y,

01:06:58.748 --> 01:07:01.550
but it definitely has
chicken, and bacon, and ranch,

01:07:01.550 --> 01:07:02.785
and it's big.

01:07:02.785 --> 01:07:03.886
Thank you very much.

01:07:03.886 --> 01:07:04.754
All right.

01:07:05.621 --> 01:07:07.023
Chicken taco pizza.

01:07:09.692 --> 01:07:11.193
Oh, yeah.

01:07:11.193 --> 01:07:12.762
Got taco spices to it.

01:07:12.762 --> 01:07:13.629
Good job on this one.

01:07:13.629 --> 01:07:15.431
Next one, the cheeseburger pizza.

01:07:15.431 --> 01:07:16.532
Um ...

01:07:19.702 --> 01:07:21.537
Yeah. Oh, my God.

01:07:21.537 --> 01:07:22.938
I'm going to say something crazy.

01:07:22.938 --> 01:07:25.341
This tastes exactly like
a McDonald's cheeseburger.

01:07:25.341 --> 01:07:27.943
Even has the oniony
and the ketchupy taste.

01:07:28.911 --> 01:07:30.479
Wow.

01:07:30.479 --> 01:07:32.148
That is a surprise.

01:07:32.148 --> 01:07:33.082
I thought this one was going to be bad,

01:07:33.082 --> 01:07:34.283
but it's actually pretty good.

01:07:34.283 --> 01:07:38.254
The extravaganZZa.

01:07:38.254 --> 01:07:42.591
This has pepperoni, sausage, ham,

01:07:42.591 --> 01:07:46.695
mushrooms, black olives, green peppers.

01:07:46.695 --> 01:07:48.197
This is the meatZZa,

01:07:48.197 --> 01:07:51.000
which I'm assuming is just a lot of meat.

01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:53.602
I'm seeing sausage, I'm seeing pepperoni,

01:07:53.602 --> 01:07:54.737
and maybe hamburger.

01:07:58.374 --> 01:07:59.442
Yeah, I'll put this in the good pile.

01:07:59.442 --> 01:08:00.276
I f--- with this one.

01:08:00.276 --> 01:08:01.277
Philly cheesesteak.

01:08:01.277 --> 01:08:02.812
Oh, no.

01:08:02.812 --> 01:08:05.214
In some weird way, I'm
blaming you for this.

01:08:05.214 --> 01:08:08.084
Since you handed this to
me, this is your fault.

01:08:08.084 --> 01:08:09.685
Look at this nightmare.

01:08:09.685 --> 01:08:11.520
Meat somewhere on here.

01:08:11.520 --> 01:08:13.456
I'm also seeing green peppers.

01:08:13.456 --> 01:08:16.459
Oh. Look, look, it's like,

01:08:16.459 --> 01:08:18.527
look at that, it's,
like, stuck to the box.

01:08:22.898 --> 01:08:24.266
No.

01:08:24.266 --> 01:08:25.201
Buffalo chicken.

01:08:25.201 --> 01:08:26.502
OK, OK.

01:08:26.502 --> 01:08:27.470
This is more my speed.

01:08:27.470 --> 01:08:28.337
Chicken.

01:08:28.337 --> 01:08:29.905
No, not tomato sauce, like a white sauce.

01:08:29.905 --> 01:08:30.739
Good call.

01:08:32.875 --> 01:08:34.710
Mm!

01:08:34.710 --> 01:08:36.378
This isn't Buffalo enough.

01:08:36.378 --> 01:08:38.981
The capital of the great state of New York

01:08:38.981 --> 01:08:41.317
needs to be better
represented in this pizza.

01:08:41.317 --> 01:08:44.487
The capital of New York
is Buffalo, correct?

01:08:44.487 --> 01:08:45.321
No?

01:08:45.321 --> 01:08:47.556
We got the Memphis barbecue chicken.

01:08:47.556 --> 01:08:48.691
Love Memphis.

01:08:48.691 --> 01:08:49.725
Love barbecue.

01:08:49.725 --> 01:08:50.726
Love chicken.

01:08:52.695 --> 01:08:54.063
Yeah.

01:08:54.063 --> 01:08:55.531
The key thing here is the barbecue sauce.

01:08:55.531 --> 01:08:58.134
I don't know what is in it,
but, man, that's really good.

01:08:58.134 --> 01:08:58.968
Memphis,

01:08:59.935 --> 01:09:02.771
capital of the great state of Tennessee.

01:09:02.771 --> 01:09:07.776
Everyone, here is the
ultra cheese New Yorker.

01:09:08.244 --> 01:09:10.546
It's got 1 kilogram of cheese,

01:09:10.546 --> 01:09:13.015
or 2.2 pounds.

01:09:13.015 --> 01:09:15.451
OMG.

01:09:15.451 --> 01:09:16.285
Ooh!

01:09:17.219 --> 01:09:20.289
Look how thick this cheese is!

01:09:20.289 --> 01:09:21.123
Go!

01:09:28.564 --> 01:09:29.632
Go home.

01:09:29.632 --> 01:09:32.034
It weighs 180 grams,

01:09:32.034 --> 01:09:35.070
180 times eight equals

01:09:35.070 --> 01:09:38.507
1,440 grams in total.

01:09:38.507 --> 01:09:41.544
So, here are other
Japanese specialty pizzas.

01:09:41.544 --> 01:09:44.880
So, here we have quattro meat max.

01:09:44.880 --> 01:09:47.383
So it's got charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken

01:09:47.383 --> 01:09:49.818
and charcoal-grilled beef

01:09:49.818 --> 01:09:53.355
and giga meat and Goryeo galbi.

01:09:53.355 --> 01:09:56.292
It's Korean-style beef pizza.

01:09:56.292 --> 01:09:58.494
And next we have seafood special.

01:09:59.562 --> 01:10:02.798
This part and this part
is shrimp mayonnaise.

01:10:02.798 --> 01:10:05.501
So this part, it's got shrimp, octopus,

01:10:05.501 --> 01:10:07.836
mussels, littleneck clams,

01:10:07.836 --> 01:10:10.339
Mactra clams, green peppers,

01:10:10.339 --> 01:10:11.941
and cherry tomatoes.

01:10:11.941 --> 01:10:15.144
Next we've got garlic master.

01:10:15.144 --> 01:10:16.912
Looks so spicy.

01:10:16.912 --> 01:10:20.783
Garlic and pork sausage and pancetta.

01:10:20.783 --> 01:10:24.320
And this part has got jalapeño, obviously.

01:10:24.320 --> 01:10:26.322
It's picante.

01:10:26.322 --> 01:10:29.792
Pepperoni and Italian sausage and onions.

01:10:29.792 --> 01:10:32.161
And look at this huge thing.

01:10:32.161 --> 01:10:33.662
Mayo jaga.

01:10:33.662 --> 01:10:37.666
So, jaga, or jagaimo,
means potato in Japanese.

01:10:37.666 --> 01:10:40.102
It's got potato and pork sausage

01:10:40.102 --> 01:10:41.971
and a lot of mayo.

01:10:41.971 --> 01:10:44.974
Joe: Our US Domino's has
sandwiches and pasta.

01:10:44.974 --> 01:10:47.576
I was not a fan of the
Philly cheesesteak pizza,

01:10:47.576 --> 01:10:49.545
but let's see what the Philly
cheesesteak tastes like

01:10:49.545 --> 01:10:52.915
in its native form of sandwich.

01:10:54.450 --> 01:10:55.851
Better than the pizza.

01:10:55.851 --> 01:10:57.086
Also at the US Domino's,

01:10:57.086 --> 01:10:58.854
you can get a Buffalo chicken sandwich,

01:10:58.854 --> 01:11:00.356
a chicken habanero sandwich,

01:11:00.356 --> 01:11:01.523
the Mediterranean veggie,

01:11:01.523 --> 01:11:02.358
no, thanks,

01:11:02.358 --> 01:11:03.592
a chicken bacon ranch,

01:11:03.592 --> 01:11:04.560
an Italian sandwich,

01:11:04.560 --> 01:11:07.429
and, of course, the chicken Parm sandwich.

01:11:07.429 --> 01:11:09.798
Our Domino's has four
pastas to choose from.

01:11:09.798 --> 01:11:11.934
I only got two, the chicken Alfredo

01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:14.036
and the Italian sausage marinara.

01:11:14.036 --> 01:11:17.573
You can also get a chicken
carbonara and a pasta primavera.

01:11:17.573 --> 01:11:19.575
I've just been informed
I have to eat this.

01:11:24.313 --> 01:11:26.315
Strong flavor on this.

01:11:26.315 --> 01:11:30.185
I would skip the pasta
at Domino's, personally.

01:11:30.185 --> 01:11:31.620
This thing is, like, baked on.

01:11:31.620 --> 01:11:32.588
See how baked this is?

01:11:32.588 --> 01:11:33.689
Like, come on.

01:11:33.689 --> 01:11:34.623
I feel like chef Ramsay here.

01:11:34.623 --> 01:11:38.427
Just, "Oh, come on. Oh,
this baked on here!"

01:11:38.427 --> 01:11:40.929
In the US, we have a few chicken options

01:11:40.929 --> 01:11:42.097
you can't get in Japan.

01:11:42.097 --> 01:11:43.565
Yes, Japan has wings,

01:11:43.565 --> 01:11:45.034
but they don't have these flavors.

01:11:45.034 --> 01:11:46.869
Visually, I can see why.

01:11:46.869 --> 01:11:50.939
First flavor we got here
is the garlic Parmesan.

01:11:50.939 --> 01:11:54.176
Hey, Domino's, what are you doing?

01:11:54.176 --> 01:11:55.678
Next one, we got,

01:11:55.678 --> 01:11:58.647
I'm assuming this is the honey barbecue.

01:11:58.647 --> 01:12:00.549
These drizzles! What are you
guys doing drizzling, man?

01:12:00.549 --> 01:12:01.784
Just toss it!

01:12:01.784 --> 01:12:03.452
Toss it in the sauce!

01:12:03.452 --> 01:12:04.720
Nobody wants a drizzle.

01:12:07.423 --> 01:12:08.590
Oh, wait a second.

01:12:09.692 --> 01:12:11.760
This is the sweet mango habanero.

01:12:11.760 --> 01:12:13.028
I wasn't expecting that heat.

01:12:14.663 --> 01:12:16.065
Oh, man.

01:12:16.065 --> 01:12:16.932
Very good.

01:12:16.932 --> 01:12:19.168
These are --

01:12:20.469 --> 01:12:21.804
why did you do this?

01:12:21.804 --> 01:12:23.639
Why did you do this?

01:12:23.639 --> 01:12:25.140
Toss it in the sauce.

01:12:25.140 --> 01:12:27.710
Why'd you just squirt it on
here, like, as an afterthought?

01:12:27.710 --> 01:12:28.811
Honey barbecue.

01:12:28.811 --> 01:12:29.878
Right? Is this not nuts?

01:12:29.878 --> 01:12:31.880
This is nuts, right, that
they did it like this.

01:12:34.650 --> 01:12:36.385
I like the sauce.

01:12:36.385 --> 01:12:40.122
So, Domino's also does their
wings in boneless flavors.

01:12:40.122 --> 01:12:41.957
They have obviously those three,

01:12:41.957 --> 01:12:44.126
and you can also get these two other ones.

01:12:44.126 --> 01:12:46.395
And I see we have the
crispy bacon and tomato,

01:12:46.395 --> 01:12:50.165
and this one must be the
spicy jalapeño pineapple.

01:12:50.165 --> 01:12:51.200
Whoa, what?

01:12:52.067 --> 01:12:53.102
Hell yeah.

01:12:53.102 --> 01:12:54.269
All right.

01:12:54.269 --> 01:12:55.270
Get that B-roll fast.

01:12:55.270 --> 01:12:58.374
There it goes!

01:12:59.241 --> 01:13:00.409
I know.

01:13:00.409 --> 01:13:04.279
Your audible gasps are warranted.

01:13:04.279 --> 01:13:06.615
I don't know what this --

01:13:06.615 --> 01:13:08.717
what am I supposed to do with this?

01:13:08.717 --> 01:13:10.886
Ooh, this one I'm looking
forward to, Yuelei.

01:13:10.886 --> 01:13:12.888
We got the food less than an hour ago.

01:13:12.888 --> 01:13:16.592
I don't think an hour is
unrealistic for food to sit.

01:13:16.592 --> 01:13:18.127
I think you guys gotta
put some more chemicals

01:13:18.127 --> 01:13:20.129
in your cheese to keep it goopier longer.

01:13:20.129 --> 01:13:21.930
Ooh, I got some pineapple,
and I got some jalapeño,

01:13:21.930 --> 01:13:22.831
and I got some chicken.

01:13:22.831 --> 01:13:23.699
Let's check it out.

01:13:26.568 --> 01:13:27.770
Yeah.

01:13:27.770 --> 01:13:30.439
Overall, everything
here tastes pretty good.

01:13:30.439 --> 01:13:32.441
Presentation, you gotta work on that.

01:13:32.441 --> 01:13:34.910
In Japan, we don't have boneless wings,

01:13:34.910 --> 01:13:38.013
but we have Japanese fried chicken,

01:13:38.013 --> 01:13:39.681
which is called karaage.

01:13:39.681 --> 01:13:42.151
It kind of looks like
American boneless wings.

01:13:43.051 --> 01:13:44.353
Ah.

01:13:44.353 --> 01:13:46.255
I love karaage.

01:13:46.255 --> 01:13:49.491
And also we have chicken nuggets.

01:13:49.491 --> 01:13:53.162
Both come in four, eight, and 12 pieces.

01:13:53.162 --> 01:13:56.632
Our Domino's has breads
and oven-baked dips.

01:13:56.632 --> 01:13:58.333
Let's review the breads first.

01:13:58.333 --> 01:13:59.301
Shall we?

01:13:59.301 --> 01:14:00.135
Over here,

01:14:00.135 --> 01:14:03.939
we have Parmesan bread twists
and garlic bread twists.

01:14:03.939 --> 01:14:08.110
I know that because of their
totally twisted shapes.

01:14:08.110 --> 01:14:10.045
They also have Parmesan bread bites

01:14:10.045 --> 01:14:11.346
that were currently unavailable.

01:14:13.348 --> 01:14:14.650
Whoa.

01:14:14.650 --> 01:14:15.818
Uh-oh.

01:14:15.818 --> 01:14:17.486
These are very good.

01:14:17.486 --> 01:14:19.021
To Parmesan we go.

01:14:21.323 --> 01:14:22.291
Not as good.

01:14:22.291 --> 01:14:23.892
But still pretty good.

01:14:23.892 --> 01:14:26.995
I mean, it's bread and
cheese and oil, right?

01:14:26.995 --> 01:14:29.865
US Domino's also has something
called stuffed cheesy bread.

01:14:29.865 --> 01:14:31.266
You can get your stuffed
cheesy bread with either

01:14:31.266 --> 01:14:35.304
spinach and feta or bacon and jalapeños.

01:14:35.304 --> 01:14:37.306
Take a wild guess which one I chose.

01:14:38.707 --> 01:14:41.376
[beep] Just ripping this
whole [beep] thing apart.

01:14:41.376 --> 01:14:43.011
Oh, God!

01:14:43.011 --> 01:14:44.913
This thing is especially greasy.

01:14:47.483 --> 01:14:51.687
For whatever reason,
Domino's didn't stop there.

01:14:51.687 --> 01:14:53.755
Domino's has something called dips.

01:14:53.755 --> 01:14:54.590
[sighs]

01:14:54.590 --> 01:14:56.158
What it appears to be

01:14:57.025 --> 01:14:59.528
is a giant dish of melted cheese.

01:14:59.528 --> 01:15:02.564
And you can get it in cheesy
marinara or five cheese.

01:15:02.564 --> 01:15:04.500
What are we doing, Domino's?

01:15:04.500 --> 01:15:07.369
[laughs]

01:15:07.369 --> 01:15:08.971
What is this?

01:15:08.971 --> 01:15:11.507
Come on, guys.

01:15:11.507 --> 01:15:13.542
So, this is the marinara
one, I'm assuming.

01:15:13.542 --> 01:15:15.978
A pizza without the bread, right?

01:15:15.978 --> 01:15:20.148
These dips are literally
zapping my will to live.

01:15:20.148 --> 01:15:21.617
Please don't ever get ...

01:15:23.285 --> 01:15:26.989
It's a whole bowl of cheese, Yuelei!

01:15:26.989 --> 01:15:29.925
Why would -- oh, look
at the oil in this too!

01:15:30.826 --> 01:15:32.794
Everyone in here just gagged.

01:15:32.794 --> 01:15:34.263
Can I even dip it?

01:15:41.403 --> 01:15:43.071
Oh, whoa.

01:15:44.273 --> 01:15:46.008
I don't know what of the
five cheeses is in here,

01:15:46.008 --> 01:15:46.875
like, which five.

01:15:48.310 --> 01:15:50.078
Why am I eating this?!

01:15:51.213 --> 01:15:52.648
Ugh!

01:15:54.616 --> 01:15:57.986
So, here are our Japanese
exclusive side-menu items.

01:15:57.986 --> 01:15:59.688
Let's start with this one.

01:15:59.688 --> 01:16:03.091
We've got oven-baked potato wedges.

01:16:03.091 --> 01:16:04.760
This one is plain.

01:16:04.760 --> 01:16:06.228
Consommé.

01:16:06.228 --> 01:16:07.963
Chili garlic.

01:16:07.963 --> 01:16:10.165
And this one is butter.

01:16:11.099 --> 01:16:14.536
And next we have cheese sticks.

01:16:15.404 --> 01:16:17.105
Shrimp popcorn.

01:16:18.740 --> 01:16:21.543
It comes with this tartar sauce.

01:16:21.543 --> 01:16:24.413
Here we have choregi salad.

01:16:24.413 --> 01:16:27.816
We've got Korean-style seaweed flakes

01:16:27.816 --> 01:16:30.252
and choregi dressing.

01:16:30.252 --> 01:16:35.157
So, choregi is, like,
Korean-style sesame-oil dressing.

01:16:35.157 --> 01:16:38.660
And fresh salad in the package.

01:16:40.095 --> 01:16:43.165
So, here we have corn potage.

01:16:43.165 --> 01:16:44.366
Clam chowder.

01:16:44.366 --> 01:16:45.701
Minestrone.

01:16:45.701 --> 01:16:47.603
Black chili.

01:16:47.603 --> 01:16:48.904
You've seen these before.

01:16:48.904 --> 01:16:52.441
It is the Domino's
marbled cookie brownies.

01:16:52.441 --> 01:16:54.876
♪ Liquid sugar ♪

01:16:54.876 --> 01:16:56.211
Oh, yeah.

01:16:56.211 --> 01:16:59.114
You can also get these
cinnamon bread twists.

01:16:59.114 --> 01:17:02.017
Lastly, another dip.

01:17:02.017 --> 01:17:05.520
I swear to God, if there's cheese in this,

01:17:05.520 --> 01:17:07.589
I'm walking out of here
and I'm never coming back.

01:17:11.059 --> 01:17:12.527
Baked apple dips.

01:17:12.527 --> 01:17:15.831
And I'm assuming you dip these into this.

01:17:15.831 --> 01:17:16.932
I'm not gonna.

01:17:16.932 --> 01:17:18.967
So, here are our other desserts.

01:17:18.967 --> 01:17:21.737
We have mini pancakes,

01:17:21.737 --> 01:17:24.439
heart-shaped fondant chocolate,

01:17:24.439 --> 01:17:28.143
and here we have egg custard tart.

01:17:28.143 --> 01:17:31.346
I have never tried this one before.

01:17:31.346 --> 01:17:32.514
Itadakimasu.

01:17:34.983 --> 01:17:36.585
Mm.

01:17:36.585 --> 01:17:38.120
Mm!

01:17:38.120 --> 01:17:39.321
This is so good.

01:17:39.321 --> 01:17:40.756
So flaky.

01:17:42.691 --> 01:17:43.592
Mm.

01:17:43.592 --> 01:17:46.461
This one is apple pie.

01:17:46.461 --> 01:17:49.264
And next we have custard pie.

01:17:50.098 --> 01:17:54.236
Lastly, of the sodas
you can get in the US,

01:17:54.236 --> 01:17:55.671
can't get in Japan,

01:17:55.671 --> 01:17:59.441
get yourself Fanta orange and Sprite.

01:17:59.441 --> 01:18:02.077
We have Coke Zero.

01:18:02.077 --> 01:18:03.445
It's supposed to be Zero,

01:18:03.445 --> 01:18:05.947
but they gave us just normal Coke.

01:18:05.947 --> 01:18:08.617
Next, we have ginger ale.

01:18:08.617 --> 01:18:10.118
Canada Dry.

01:18:10.118 --> 01:18:13.555
Canada is an amazing country, eh?

01:18:13.555 --> 01:18:14.990
Qoo orange juice.

01:18:15.824 --> 01:18:18.527
And here is Sokenbicha.

01:18:18.527 --> 01:18:20.696
It's Japanese blended tea.

01:18:20.696 --> 01:18:24.733
And last one, we've got Georgia Japan

01:18:24.733 --> 01:18:27.069
Craftsman café latte.

01:18:27.069 --> 01:18:28.670
Georgia Japan.

01:18:28.670 --> 01:18:31.106
Sounds like George Japan.

01:18:31.106 --> 01:18:33.041
I'd like to be sponsored by you.

01:18:33.041 --> 01:18:34.543
Let me try this.

01:18:36.778 --> 01:18:40.082
It's got a lot of milk and sugar in it.

01:18:40.082 --> 01:18:41.216
I gotta be honest.

01:18:41.216 --> 01:18:42.718
It's not my taste.

01:18:46.655 --> 01:18:47.522
Take two.

01:18:49.224 --> 01:18:50.859
I really love this.

01:18:50.859 --> 01:18:53.462
Please give me a sponsorship.

01:18:55.630 --> 01:18:57.365
A Japan large hand-tossed pizza

01:18:57.365 --> 01:19:00.001
is 130 calories per slice,

01:19:00.001 --> 01:19:04.606
or 1,560 calories for the full pizza.

01:19:04.606 --> 01:19:08.610
In the US, a large hand-tossed
pizza slice is 280 calories,

01:19:08.610 --> 01:19:13.248
which makes the entire
pizza 2,240 calories.

01:19:13.248 --> 01:19:15.584
A large big-pepperoni hand-tossed slice

01:19:15.584 --> 01:19:18.720
is 335 calories per slice,

01:19:18.720 --> 01:19:22.524
or 4,020 calories for the entire pizza.

01:19:22.524 --> 01:19:26.061
Our large pepperoni is
370 calories per slice,

01:19:26.061 --> 01:19:30.132
which makes the entire pie 2,960 calories.

01:19:30.132 --> 01:19:32.601
Japan's most calorific pizza is

01:19:32.601 --> 01:19:35.203
the ultra cheese New Yorker size.

01:19:35.203 --> 01:19:38.607
One slice is 478 calories.

01:19:38.607 --> 01:19:43.011
That's 3,827 for the full pizza.

01:19:43.011 --> 01:19:44.212
Ah.

01:19:44.212 --> 01:19:46.581
Our US Domino's pizza
with the most calories

01:19:46.581 --> 01:19:49.551
is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

01:19:49.551 --> 01:19:51.453
This is an XL of said pizza.

01:19:51.453 --> 01:19:54.089
One slice is 560 calories,

01:19:54.089 --> 01:19:58.960
and that makes the full
pie 3,360 calories.

01:19:58.960 --> 01:20:03.799
Our large plain pizza
has 1,620 calories total.

01:20:03.799 --> 01:20:06.768
Our large cheese is 2,240 calories.

01:20:06.768 --> 01:20:09.838
That's a 38.2% increase.

01:20:09.838 --> 01:20:14.342
Our large big pepperoni is 2,680 calories,

01:20:14.342 --> 01:20:18.113
over 34% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

01:20:18.113 --> 01:20:21.983
333% of your daily sodium.

01:20:21.983 --> 01:20:23.451
Ah!

01:20:23.451 --> 01:20:26.021
Too many tasty calories!

01:20:26.021 --> 01:20:28.190
Ours is 2,960 calories,

01:20:28.190 --> 01:20:32.561
48% over your daily recommended amount,

01:20:32.561 --> 01:20:34.996
but somehow ours has less sodium,

01:20:34.996 --> 01:20:38.867
only 299% of your daily sodium.

01:20:41.036 --> 01:20:42.137
In October of last year,

01:20:42.137 --> 01:20:45.407
a study found detectable
amounts of phthalate,

01:20:45.407 --> 01:20:47.576
a plastic softener, in common menu items

01:20:47.576 --> 01:20:50.679
from large fast-food
chains, including Domino's.

01:20:53.448 --> 01:20:56.351
The study analyzed 64 food samples

01:20:56.351 --> 01:20:58.286
from several popular fast-food chains

01:20:58.286 --> 01:21:03.225
and found phthalates DnBP and DEHP

01:21:03.225 --> 01:21:05.327
in a majority of the items.

01:21:05.327 --> 01:21:07.863
USA Today reported that,
"Food containing meat,

01:21:07.863 --> 01:21:09.764
such as chicken burritos
and cheeseburgers,

01:21:09.764 --> 01:21:12.067
had higher levels of
the chemicals studied,

01:21:12.067 --> 01:21:14.369
while cheese pizza had the lowest levels."

01:21:14.369 --> 01:21:16.738
OK, so that's good news
for Domino's, I guess.

01:21:16.738 --> 01:21:19.674
The study goes on to say
that "food handling gloves

01:21:19.674 --> 01:21:22.477
contain replacement plasticizers,

01:21:22.477 --> 01:21:25.113
which may be [a] source
of food contamination."

01:21:25.113 --> 01:21:26.648
Sounds to me like an easy fix.

01:21:26.648 --> 01:21:29.117
Just prepare the food without gloves.

01:21:29.117 --> 01:21:33.688
Japan has a ban on DEHP
in food-handling gloves.

01:21:33.688 --> 01:21:35.891
Good-er news, if you're
a fan of "Food Wars"

01:21:35.891 --> 01:21:38.460
and saw the US versus UK Domino's episode,

01:21:38.460 --> 01:21:42.464
we highlighted BHA and
BHT in the US pepperoni.

01:21:42.464 --> 01:21:46.101
Well, on the stewardship
page on Domino's website,

01:21:46.101 --> 01:21:47.836
they have stated, ahem,

01:21:47.836 --> 01:21:49.104
"We have eliminated a long list

01:21:49.104 --> 01:21:50.739
of ingredients from all
of our core products

01:21:50.739 --> 01:21:54.643
including BHA and BHT and PHOs,

01:21:54.643 --> 01:21:57.779
as well as trans-fat from
core pizza products,"

01:21:57.779 --> 01:21:59.447
which is fantastic news.

01:21:59.447 --> 01:22:01.349
I clearly was going to eat it anyway,

01:22:01.349 --> 01:22:03.184
but thank you regardless.

01:22:03.585 --> 01:22:05.720
From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:22:05.720 --> 01:22:07.589
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:22:07.589 --> 01:22:10.392
between Pocky in Japan and the US.

01:22:10.392 --> 01:22:11.993
This is "Food Wars."

01:22:15.931 --> 01:22:19.367
In Japan, our Pocky comes in a 72-gram box

01:22:19.367 --> 01:22:23.838
which contains two
packets and a nine-pack.

01:22:24.739 --> 01:22:26.474
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

01:22:26.474 --> 01:22:28.944
- Our Pocky's come in
basically three sizes.

01:22:28.944 --> 01:22:32.948
The one 1.14-ounce box,
the 2.47-ounce box,

01:22:32.948 --> 01:22:37.519
and the 4.13-ounce boxy bag.

01:22:37.519 --> 01:22:39.888
But our strawberry-flavored box is smaller

01:22:39.888 --> 01:22:41.056
than this chocolate box.

01:22:41.056 --> 01:22:43.758
This is a 3.81-ounce box,

01:22:43.758 --> 01:22:47.028
which is 0.32 ounces
smaller than this one.

01:22:47.028 --> 01:22:50.298
Largest box bag is this,
the Cookies &amp; Cream flavor,

01:22:50.298 --> 01:22:53.435
which is 4.57 ounces

01:22:53.435 --> 01:22:58.440
or 0.44 grams larger
than the chocolate box.

01:22:58.440 --> 01:22:59.941
One theory, my theory,

01:22:59.941 --> 01:23:02.677
is that the Pocky boxes
contain a specific number

01:23:02.677 --> 01:23:03.678
of Pocky sticks

01:23:03.678 --> 01:23:06.915
and each Pocky is a different weight

01:23:06.915 --> 01:23:09.017
based on the flavor coating.

01:23:09.017 --> 01:23:12.053
So we're gonna weigh
each Pocky individually

01:23:12.053 --> 01:23:13.621
to see if this is true.

01:23:13.621 --> 01:23:15.924
All right, chocolate first.

01:23:15.924 --> 01:23:20.528
So seven of these are 13 grams.
Can someone write that down?

01:23:20.528 --> 01:23:25.266
Strawberry, seven is 13 grams.

01:23:25.266 --> 01:23:27.969
Was that what the first one was? Okay.

01:23:27.969 --> 01:23:29.371
Cookies &amp; Cream!

01:23:29.371 --> 01:23:33.575
Cookies &amp; Cream, seven
of them are 18 grams.

01:23:33.575 --> 01:23:36.011
Well, the Cookies &amp; Cream ones
are definitely a lot heavier.

01:23:36.011 --> 01:23:36.845
A lot heavier.

01:23:36.845 --> 01:23:39.814
(Joe chomping)

01:23:39.814 --> 01:23:40.882
Mm!

01:23:40.882 --> 01:23:43.952
- So let's see how many
Pocky are in a box.

01:23:43.952 --> 01:23:47.722
(George counting in Japanese)

01:23:47.722 --> 01:23:51.493
(audio chirping)

01:23:51.493 --> 01:23:56.164
32, 33, 34.

01:23:56.164 --> 01:23:58.500
Thirty-four Pocky in total.

01:23:58.500 --> 01:24:00.769
So one packet has 17 Pocky

01:24:00.769 --> 01:24:03.872
and another one also has 17 Pocky.

01:24:03.872 --> 01:24:05.774
- Let's see how many
Pocky's are in this box.

01:24:05.774 --> 01:24:08.610
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

01:24:08.610 --> 01:24:10.111
(exhales) Oh, man.

01:24:12.947 --> 01:24:13.782
Is this normal?

01:24:14.616 --> 01:24:15.450
I think I can kind of like,

01:24:15.450 --> 01:24:18.686
do you wanna get a
close-up on there before?

01:24:18.686 --> 01:24:20.688
So one, two, three, those
are the broken ones.

01:24:20.688 --> 01:24:22.424
(audio chirping)

01:24:22.424 --> 01:24:27.429
30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36.

01:24:27.562 --> 01:24:28.763
You know how everyone
was complaining about

01:24:28.763 --> 01:24:31.366
how I eat Kit-Kats in the Kit-Kat episode?

01:24:31.366 --> 01:24:33.435
(suspenseful music)

01:24:33.435 --> 01:24:35.770
(Joe chomps)

01:24:35.770 --> 01:24:37.672
(Joe chewing)

01:24:37.672 --> 01:24:39.874
Mm!

01:24:39.874 --> 01:24:42.077
(upbeat music)

01:24:42.077 --> 01:24:44.212
Here's all the Pocky's
that are native to the US

01:24:44.212 --> 01:24:45.914
that are not in Japan.

01:24:45.914 --> 01:24:49.084
- And here are all the
Pocky's native to Japan.

01:24:49.084 --> 01:24:52.587
- Cookies &amp; Cream, Cookies &amp; Cream.

01:24:52.587 --> 01:24:54.456
Not a solid block, so that's good.

01:24:54.456 --> 01:24:56.958
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

01:24:56.958 --> 01:24:57.959
(Joe chomping)

01:24:57.959 --> 01:25:01.596
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:25:01.596 --> 01:25:03.164
Mm!

01:25:03.164 --> 01:25:03.998
I like those.

01:25:03.998 --> 01:25:05.600
This looks like fun, Yuelei.

01:25:05.600 --> 01:25:07.535
Chocolate Banana, have
you had these before?

01:25:07.535 --> 01:25:08.369
You have?

01:25:09.270 --> 01:25:10.905
No, mm-mm.

01:25:10.905 --> 01:25:12.807
That banana flavor hits right away.

01:25:14.876 --> 01:25:15.743
Oh, no.

01:25:16.911 --> 01:25:18.146
Matcha green tea.

01:25:18.146 --> 01:25:20.081
Any "Food Wars" heads watching know,

01:25:20.982 --> 01:25:22.283
Joe does not like matcha.

01:25:23.251 --> 01:25:26.154
Mm, smells like a freshly-cut lawn.

01:25:26.154 --> 01:25:27.088
(lawnmower rumbles)

01:25:27.088 --> 01:25:29.090
(Joe chomps)

01:25:29.090 --> 01:25:30.792
Yeah, nah.

01:25:30.792 --> 01:25:32.894
There's also a Crunchy Strawberry
flavor you can get here

01:25:32.894 --> 01:25:33.728
in the US,

01:25:33.728 --> 01:25:35.530
but I was not able to get my hands on it

01:25:35.530 --> 01:25:38.099
by the time of filming this episode.

01:25:38.099 --> 01:25:41.903
So here's just regular strawberry.

01:25:41.903 --> 01:25:42.737
Uh-oh.

01:25:42.737 --> 01:25:46.207
Oh, another solid block.

01:25:46.207 --> 01:25:47.041
Yeah.

01:25:49.811 --> 01:25:51.513
(Joe chomps)
(audience gasps)

01:25:51.513 --> 01:25:53.848
Mm, yeah, dude.

01:25:53.848 --> 01:25:55.917
Put me in jail for crimes against Pocky's.

01:25:57.185 --> 01:25:58.019
- George's energy.

01:25:58.019 --> 01:26:00.088
Bong, let's go!

01:26:00.088 --> 01:26:02.557
All right, let's start with this one.

01:26:02.557 --> 01:26:05.593
We have Pocky Luxury Milk Chocolate.

01:26:07.896 --> 01:26:10.265
(laughs) Is it Pocky?

01:26:10.265 --> 01:26:12.433
You look like corn dog.

01:26:12.433 --> 01:26:13.868
What happened to you?

01:26:16.171 --> 01:26:17.005
Hmm.

01:26:18.706 --> 01:26:23.444
It's got milk and fermented butter flavor.

01:26:23.444 --> 01:26:26.014
And we have another corn dog.

01:26:26.014 --> 01:26:28.483
It's a Almond Milk flavor.

01:26:28.483 --> 01:26:30.552
(George speaks in Japanese)

01:26:32.453 --> 01:26:34.022
Mm.

01:26:34.022 --> 01:26:36.824
It has strong almond milk flavor.

01:26:36.824 --> 01:26:39.961
I prefer this one, the milk chocolate,

01:26:39.961 --> 01:26:42.030
but both are so short.

01:26:42.030 --> 01:26:42.864
You should be longer.

01:26:42.864 --> 01:26:43.798
(whistle screeches)

01:26:43.798 --> 01:26:44.766
You too!

01:26:44.766 --> 01:26:47.602
We have this ultra-thin Pocky.

01:26:48.770 --> 01:26:51.406
Oh. (laughs)

01:26:51.406 --> 01:26:54.842
You are so thin this time.

01:26:54.842 --> 01:26:56.744
This one is short.

01:26:56.744 --> 01:26:58.079
This one is so thin.

01:27:00.915 --> 01:27:03.151
We have Tasty.

01:27:03.151 --> 01:27:04.686
Why is it Tasty?

01:27:04.686 --> 01:27:08.723
Oh, fermented butter
is used for this stick.

01:27:10.325 --> 01:27:11.159
Ooh.

01:27:12.527 --> 01:27:14.128
(George chomps)

01:27:14.128 --> 01:27:17.632
It's got just a little
bit of butter flavor.

01:27:17.632 --> 01:27:21.302
I still prefer this one, this corn dog.

01:27:21.302 --> 01:27:23.137
Almond Crush.

01:27:23.137 --> 01:27:25.873
It's a little different.
Look at the packets.

01:27:28.076 --> 01:27:30.812
Yeah, obviously, it's got almonds.

01:27:30.812 --> 01:27:32.280
Okey-dokey, Pocky.

01:27:32.280 --> 01:27:34.182
(George speaks in Japanese)

01:27:35.350 --> 01:27:36.351
I love this.

01:27:37.685 --> 01:27:40.054
I love this.

01:27:40.054 --> 01:27:41.055
Mm.

01:27:41.055 --> 01:27:44.292
We've got Pocky Chocolate Coconut.

01:27:44.292 --> 01:27:49.163
Oh, this one is also
this style of packets.

01:27:50.965 --> 01:27:52.433
Oh.

01:27:52.433 --> 01:27:55.603
It's pretty similar with
this one, Almond Crush.

01:27:56.771 --> 01:27:58.640
(George chomps)

01:27:58.640 --> 01:27:59.941
Hmm?

01:27:59.941 --> 01:28:02.810
Yeah, obviously, it's got coconut flavor,

01:28:02.810 --> 01:28:06.281
and also, it's got a
little bit of saltiness.

01:28:06.281 --> 01:28:07.482
It's not my taste.

01:28:07.482 --> 01:28:10.251
Strawberry chocolate Pocky.

01:28:10.251 --> 01:28:12.420
(George chomps)

01:28:12.420 --> 01:28:13.254
Oh.

01:28:14.222 --> 01:28:15.056
Ah.

01:28:15.890 --> 01:28:19.661
Right after you bite this,
you get some sweetness.

01:28:19.661 --> 01:28:21.829
But after that, you get sourness.

01:28:21.829 --> 01:28:23.264
It smells so strong.

01:28:25.099 --> 01:28:27.168
I can smell it from here.

01:28:27.168 --> 01:28:29.337
Cocoa powder Pocky,

01:28:29.337 --> 01:28:32.774
And it says you can only
get this in winter season.

01:28:32.774 --> 01:28:35.310
Oh yeah, look at this.
It's got cocoa powder.

01:28:38.079 --> 01:28:40.181
(George speaks in Japanese)

01:28:40.181 --> 01:28:41.716
(George's lips smack)

01:28:41.716 --> 01:28:44.919
We've got the cutest Pocky ever.

01:28:44.919 --> 01:28:46.888
Cherry heart-shaped Pocky.

01:28:47.955 --> 01:28:49.390
Aha.

01:28:50.992 --> 01:28:53.328
Oh, look at this!

01:28:53.328 --> 01:28:55.330
Heart! It's in there.

01:28:55.330 --> 01:28:56.864
How cute.

01:28:56.864 --> 01:28:59.634
And this part, cherry
chocolate is so awesome.

01:29:00.768 --> 01:29:02.870
You get strong cherry flavor.

01:29:02.870 --> 01:29:07.208
We've also got blueberry
heart-shaped chocolate Pocky.

01:29:07.208 --> 01:29:08.509
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

01:29:08.509 --> 01:29:10.978
Ooh, look at this.

01:29:10.978 --> 01:29:12.413
So blue.

01:29:12.413 --> 01:29:16.551
This color doesn't make me want
to eat this, but let's try.

01:29:16.551 --> 01:29:19.120
(George speaks in Japanese)

01:29:19.120 --> 01:29:20.655
Ooh!

01:29:20.655 --> 01:29:21.489
Mm.

01:29:22.357 --> 01:29:24.125
So sour.

01:29:24.125 --> 01:29:26.327
But look at this heart-shaped Pocky.

01:29:27.261 --> 01:29:28.062
Not for me.

01:29:28.996 --> 01:29:33.101
This is what I've been
waiting for, sakura matcha.

01:29:33.101 --> 01:29:36.070
So "sakura" means cherry blossom.

01:29:36.070 --> 01:29:37.839
Cherry blossom matcha taste.

01:29:39.140 --> 01:29:39.974
Ooh.

01:29:41.242 --> 01:29:42.877
Look at this!

01:29:42.877 --> 01:29:45.947
So it's got matcha chocolate

01:29:45.947 --> 01:29:48.916
and this stick is pink.

01:29:48.916 --> 01:29:51.085
(George chomps)

01:29:51.085 --> 01:29:54.922
Mm, this is so Japanese-y Pocky.

01:29:54.922 --> 01:29:56.524
Just sweet matcha.

01:29:56.524 --> 01:29:58.993
The feeling of spring has come to my life.

01:29:58.993 --> 01:30:00.228
(bird chirping)

01:30:00.228 --> 01:30:01.863
Spring days here in my body.

01:30:02.897 --> 01:30:07.835
(George sings in Japanese)

01:30:07.835 --> 01:30:10.371
Everybody's curious what these are.

01:30:10.371 --> 01:30:11.773
Megami no Ruby.

01:30:11.773 --> 01:30:14.208
Otona no Kohaku.

01:30:14.208 --> 01:30:15.410
What does it mean?

01:30:15.410 --> 01:30:18.045
I don't even know. (laughs)

01:30:19.280 --> 01:30:21.482
Anyway, so it says Megami no Ruby.

01:30:21.482 --> 01:30:25.920
It means like, "Goddess Ruby".

01:30:25.920 --> 01:30:29.424
Otona no Kohaku, in
English, it says, "amber."

01:30:29.424 --> 01:30:33.227
Kind of like stone, fossil, jewel.

01:30:33.227 --> 01:30:36.397
It says it goes well with red wine.

01:30:36.397 --> 01:30:37.365
Interesting.

01:30:37.365 --> 01:30:39.133
Ta-da!

01:30:39.133 --> 01:30:42.136
It looks like regular chocolate Pocky.

01:30:42.136 --> 01:30:44.272
(George chomps)

01:30:44.272 --> 01:30:45.106
Oh?

01:30:45.973 --> 01:30:47.041
What is this?

01:30:48.910 --> 01:30:51.412
This taste itself is like berries.

01:30:51.412 --> 01:30:54.382
This one goes well with whiskey.

01:30:54.382 --> 01:30:57.084
(George chomps)

01:30:57.084 --> 01:30:57.919
Huh?

01:30:58.953 --> 01:31:02.290
It's pretty close to dark
chocolate, it's bitter.

01:31:02.290 --> 01:31:05.560
In Japan, we have this
Gokuboso extra-fine Pocky,

01:31:05.560 --> 01:31:07.528
which are roughly half the thickness

01:31:07.528 --> 01:31:09.330
of a regular chocolate Pocky.

01:31:09.330 --> 01:31:12.200
- In the US, ours are
called the Ultra Slim.

01:31:12.200 --> 01:31:14.902
- I got a new digital scale.

01:31:14.902 --> 01:31:18.573
What I'm gonna do is weigh
a regular chocolate Pocky.

01:31:18.573 --> 01:31:21.275
2.13 grams.

01:31:21.275 --> 01:31:23.444
So ultra thin Pocky.

01:31:23.444 --> 01:31:27.114
So it weighs 1.52 grams.

01:31:27.114 --> 01:31:30.051
- Thinner, that's it?

01:31:30.051 --> 01:31:30.885
Here's a big boy.

01:31:32.320 --> 01:31:33.721
Here's the thin.

01:31:33.721 --> 01:31:34.856
Is it able to do this?

01:31:34.856 --> 01:31:36.390
Can I get out of the way so
it's just the white background?

01:31:36.390 --> 01:31:41.195
23, 24, 25, and there's another
bag in here, so 50 per box.

01:31:41.195 --> 01:31:43.731
Okay, so 50 instead of 36.

01:31:43.731 --> 01:31:46.000
Seven regular Pocky's are 13 grams.

01:31:46.000 --> 01:31:49.036
Let's see how many slim ones
we needed to get to 13 grams.

01:31:49.036 --> 01:31:52.607
5, 6, 7, 8 1/2.

01:31:52.607 --> 01:31:54.809
Eight and a half slim ones are the same

01:31:54.809 --> 01:31:56.511
as seven regular ones.

01:31:56.511 --> 01:31:58.012
Is that that much slimmer?

01:31:58.012 --> 01:31:59.347
I guess that's slimmer.

01:31:59.347 --> 01:32:01.549
Does anyone think that's
not significant enough

01:32:01.549 --> 01:32:03.084
to be a selling point?

01:32:03.084 --> 01:32:05.987
Pocky adjusts its sweetness
for different countries.

01:32:05.987 --> 01:32:09.056
Not surprisingly, the US
ones are meant to be sweeter.

01:32:09.056 --> 01:32:11.158
I'm gonna do a taste test side by side.

01:32:11.158 --> 01:32:13.261
We got the American ones
and the Japanese one,

01:32:13.261 --> 01:32:15.730
and we're gonna see just
how different they taste.

01:32:15.730 --> 01:32:19.200
I'm worried that these are
also gonna be a Pocky popsicle.

01:32:19.200 --> 01:32:20.034
Oh no, okay.

01:32:21.168 --> 01:32:22.537
Japanese.

01:32:22.537 --> 01:32:23.838
These are only Japanese ones I can find.

01:32:23.838 --> 01:32:27.041
Obviously, they're bigger. I
don't know if this is the norm.

01:32:27.041 --> 01:32:28.342
(Joe chomps)

01:32:28.342 --> 01:32:31.078
Mm-hm, in the baseline sweetness.

01:32:34.815 --> 01:32:36.350
Yeah.

01:32:36.350 --> 01:32:37.151
Mm.

01:32:38.286 --> 01:32:40.688
(Joe chomps)

01:32:42.857 --> 01:32:44.959
Yeah, it's noticeably different.

01:32:44.959 --> 01:32:49.964
They taste identical, but
ours has a sweet aftertaste.

01:32:50.498 --> 01:32:52.567
I like the Japanese ones much better.

01:32:52.567 --> 01:32:56.103
- So Pocky is in the Guinness
World Records three times.

01:32:56.103 --> 01:32:58.940
It's the largest
chocolate-coated biscuits brand,

01:32:58.940 --> 01:33:00.841
has the most mentions of a brand name

01:33:00.841 --> 01:33:03.177
on Twitter in 24 hours,

01:33:03.177 --> 01:33:08.049
which was 3,710,044 times.

01:33:08.049 --> 01:33:09.083
And finally, it was part

01:33:09.083 --> 01:33:12.219
of the most people opening
packaged food online

01:33:12.219 --> 01:33:15.990
simultaneously with 143 people.

01:33:15.990 --> 01:33:18.225
- 143 people, that's it?

01:33:18.225 --> 01:33:19.860
That doesn't seem like that many.

01:33:19.860 --> 01:33:21.862
I feel like I've been on Zoom work calls

01:33:21.862 --> 01:33:25.499
with 143 people in it, right?

01:33:25.499 --> 01:33:28.302
It would've been literally
one email to set that up.

01:33:28.302 --> 01:33:29.604
- I can do (George speaks in Japanese).

01:33:31.806 --> 01:33:35.643
Pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom.

01:33:35.643 --> 01:33:40.081
Now I got more than 200
George's clones right here.

01:33:40.081 --> 01:33:43.084
Simultaneously, three, two, one.

01:33:43.084 --> 01:33:43.918
Boom.

01:33:45.753 --> 01:33:49.056
Now I broke the Guinness World Records.

01:33:49.056 --> 01:33:51.892
So November 11th is known as
a Pocky (speaks in Japanese)

01:33:51.892 --> 01:33:54.061
or Pocky Day in Japan.

01:33:54.061 --> 01:33:57.632
This date was chosen because
a Pocky is shaped like a one.

01:33:57.632 --> 01:34:01.369
At November 11th, visually,
it looks like four Pocky.

01:34:01.369 --> 01:34:04.939
And also, Pretz are included
in this day, November 11th,

01:34:04.939 --> 01:34:07.041
which is the pretzel version of Pocky.

01:34:07.041 --> 01:34:10.711
And in Japan, you can get
them in flavors like Salad,

01:34:10.711 --> 01:34:15.716
Ripe Tomato, Sweet Potato,
and Roasted Bread flavor.

01:34:15.950 --> 01:34:17.752
In the US, we also have Pretz,

01:34:17.752 --> 01:34:22.189
and we get these fun flavors
like Sweet Corn, fun,

01:34:22.189 --> 01:34:24.191
and Pizza.

01:34:24.191 --> 01:34:25.359
Oh, God.

01:34:27.261 --> 01:34:28.629
It has nothing on it.

01:34:28.629 --> 01:34:29.864
(Joe chomps)

01:34:29.864 --> 01:34:30.765
Nope.

01:34:30.765 --> 01:34:34.735
I mean, yeah, it tastes like corn.

01:34:34.735 --> 01:34:35.736
Why though?

01:34:35.736 --> 01:34:39.740
What is the demand for
corn-flavored sticks?

01:34:39.740 --> 01:34:41.075
(Joe sighs)

01:34:41.075 --> 01:34:44.378
Besides pizza, anything
flavored like pizza is terrible.

01:34:44.378 --> 01:34:46.380
Even pizza combos aren't very good.

01:34:46.380 --> 01:34:48.149
(Pretz wrapper crinkles)

01:34:48.149 --> 01:34:49.183
No.

01:34:49.183 --> 01:34:51.252
(Joe chomps)

01:34:51.252 --> 01:34:53.054
I mean, it's up there with croutons.

01:34:53.054 --> 01:34:56.524
Does anyone grab a handful
of croutons on-the-go?

01:34:56.524 --> 01:34:58.159
And would just eating a box of croutons.

01:34:58.159 --> 01:35:00.327
These probably would be good on something.

01:35:00.327 --> 01:35:03.330
(catchy music)

01:35:03.330 --> 01:35:05.533
- In Japan, our chocolate Pocky box,

01:35:05.533 --> 01:35:08.669
per 100 grams, has 506 calories.

01:35:08.669 --> 01:35:11.539
Adjusted for the box size, 72 grams,

01:35:11.539 --> 01:35:16.110
the package contains 364.3 calories.

01:35:16.110 --> 01:35:19.747
And let's break it down
even further to per Pocky.

01:35:19.747 --> 01:35:24.518
One Pocky contains, on
average, 11.38 calories.

01:35:24.518 --> 01:35:29.490
- A US chocolate Pocky
box contains 340 calories.

01:35:29.490 --> 01:35:32.293
Just a little bit less
than a Japanese box,

01:35:32.293 --> 01:35:34.161
but note, there is a two-gram difference.

01:35:34.161 --> 01:35:37.264
Now here at "Food Wars", we
thrive on scientific accuracy.

01:35:37.264 --> 01:35:39.467
So let's break it down per Pocky.

01:35:39.467 --> 01:35:44.438
One US Pocky is 9.44444444444444444...

01:35:48.909 --> 01:35:50.111
calories.

01:35:50.111 --> 01:35:53.781
- The highest-calorie Pocky
in Japan is to be determined.

01:35:53.781 --> 01:35:55.616
We emailed the customer service,

01:35:55.616 --> 01:35:58.552
but we didn't get their response.

01:35:58.552 --> 01:36:00.621
What are you doing? Hurry up!

01:36:00.621 --> 01:36:05.626
But I guess this Pocky is
the most calorific Pocky.

01:36:05.659 --> 01:36:08.996
It's 196 calories.

01:36:08.996 --> 01:36:12.533
So it should be 'cause it's
got a lot of butter in it.

01:36:12.533 --> 01:36:13.901
- The US Pocky

01:36:13.901 --> 01:36:16.971
with the most calories
is the Cookies &amp; Cream.

01:36:16.971 --> 01:36:20.641
It contains total 630 calories.

01:36:20.641 --> 01:36:22.843
There's no question I
can murder this whole box

01:36:22.843 --> 01:36:24.111
in one sitting.

01:36:24.111 --> 01:36:25.579
630 calories? That's nothing.

01:36:25.579 --> 01:36:28.749
That's kind of reassuring
like, "Wow, only 630?

01:36:28.749 --> 01:36:30.151
Found my breakfast!"

01:36:30.151 --> 01:36:33.220
(steady music)

01:36:33.220 --> 01:36:35.656
- Japa-Pocky contains these ingredients.

01:36:35.656 --> 01:36:39.894
Wheat flour, sugar, cacao
mass, vegetable oils,

01:36:39.894 --> 01:36:43.430
whole-milk powder,
shortening, malt extract,

01:36:43.430 --> 01:36:48.102
starch, salt, yeast, cocoa powder, butter,

01:36:48.102 --> 01:36:52.606
emulsifier, flavoring, leavening
agent, annatto coloring,

01:36:52.606 --> 01:36:54.175
and mineral salt.

01:36:54.175 --> 01:36:57.912
- Any US Pocky contains
wheat flour, sugar,

01:36:57.912 --> 01:37:00.080
chocolate liquor, blend of vegetable oils,

01:37:00.080 --> 01:37:02.917
that blend being sunflower oil, palm oil,

01:37:02.917 --> 01:37:05.452
whole-milk powder,
vegetable oil shortening,

01:37:05.452 --> 01:37:08.689
which is palm oil, hydrogenated
palm oil, and cocoa butter,

01:37:08.689 --> 01:37:11.959
salt, artificial flavors,
yeast, soy lecithin,

01:37:11.959 --> 01:37:13.894
leavening, sodium bicarbonate,

01:37:13.894 --> 01:37:18.232
mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids.

01:37:18.232 --> 01:37:19.700
Wink.

01:37:19.700 --> 01:37:22.536
- In Japan, our Pocky
contains malt extract,

01:37:22.536 --> 01:37:24.738
which is sometimes used as a replacement

01:37:24.738 --> 01:37:26.240
for sugar in baking.

01:37:26.240 --> 01:37:28.108
It contains lots of maltose,

01:37:28.108 --> 01:37:29.243
a type of sugar

01:37:29.243 --> 01:37:32.012
which actually has a
higher glycemic index value

01:37:32.012 --> 01:37:33.247
than normal sucrose.

01:37:33.247 --> 01:37:36.150
So it's a surprise that
American Pocky are supposed

01:37:36.150 --> 01:37:37.651
to be sweeter.

01:37:37.651 --> 01:37:39.854
- There are actually differences
in the types of cocoa used.

01:37:39.854 --> 01:37:42.456
If you've watched the "US
versus UK Snickers" episode,

01:37:42.456 --> 01:37:45.693
you know that American
chocolate is not so great.

01:37:45.693 --> 01:37:48.629
In the US, our Pockys are
made with chocolate liquor

01:37:48.629 --> 01:37:50.030
and cocoa butter.

01:37:50.030 --> 01:37:52.466
Chocolate liquor is just
cocoa that's been processed

01:37:52.466 --> 01:37:53.767
into semisolid form,

01:37:53.767 --> 01:37:57.638
and it's actually around
50% cocoa butter itself.

01:37:57.638 --> 01:37:59.106
The trouble is for an American product

01:37:59.106 --> 01:38:00.841
to be classified as milk chocolate,

01:38:00.841 --> 01:38:04.311
it only needs to contain
around 10% of chocolate liquor,

01:38:04.311 --> 01:38:06.347
and the rest can be made up of sugars

01:38:06.347 --> 01:38:08.048
and various ingredients.

01:38:08.048 --> 01:38:10.150
- In Japan, the rules are different,

01:38:10.150 --> 01:38:12.152
depending on the type of product.

01:38:12.152 --> 01:38:14.121
Milk chocolate material must contain

01:38:14.121 --> 01:38:17.191
at least 21% cocoa content,

01:38:17.191 --> 01:38:19.627
double the required amount in America.

01:38:19.627 --> 01:38:22.129
So our chocolate has more chocolate.

01:38:22.129 --> 01:38:23.664
Are you jealous of us?

01:38:23.664 --> 01:38:24.698
Come to Japan.

01:38:26.133 --> 01:38:28.168
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:38:28.168 --> 01:38:30.004
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:38:30.004 --> 01:38:32.907
between 7-Eleven in Japan and the US.

01:38:32.907 --> 01:38:35.009
This is "Food Wars."

01:38:37.077 --> 01:38:38.579
In Japan, our coffees come in regular --

01:38:38.579 --> 01:38:40.281
Joe: In small, medium,

01:38:40.281 --> 01:38:41.415
large,
George: And large.

01:38:41.415 --> 01:38:42.850
and extra large.

01:38:42.850 --> 01:38:44.385
If you're getting coffee,

01:38:44.385 --> 01:38:45.886
why not grab a chocolate doughnut?

01:38:48.522 --> 01:38:52.593
Our 7-Eleven drinks come in
sizes of 200 milliliters,

01:38:52.593 --> 01:38:54.161
450 milliliters,

01:38:54.161 --> 01:38:55.296
and 1 liter,

01:38:55.296 --> 01:38:57.765
and 1.5 liters.

01:38:57.765 --> 01:38:59.300
I'm sorry, I couldn't get it.

01:38:59.300 --> 01:39:02.803
[laughing maniacally]

01:39:06.573 --> 01:39:08.208
In the US, we have Big Gulps,

01:39:08.208 --> 01:39:11.245
self-service fountain drink for sodas,

01:39:11.245 --> 01:39:13.514
and they come in these four sizes:

01:39:13.514 --> 01:39:16.550
medium, large, extra large,

01:39:16.550 --> 01:39:18.385
double extra large.
[air horn rings]

01:39:18.385 --> 01:39:21.689
So, I want to see how
much the biggest-size cup

01:39:21.689 --> 01:39:23.590
I could get at the 7-Eleven is.

01:39:23.590 --> 01:39:26.427
And to do that, I will need, hang on ...

01:39:27.428 --> 01:39:28.963
It's just past 40.

01:39:28.963 --> 01:39:30.731
It's exactly 48 ounces.

01:39:30.731 --> 01:39:33.067
That's hardly double extra.

01:39:33.067 --> 01:39:35.169
I'll round it up, 'cause
of this section here.

01:39:35.169 --> 01:39:36.403
I'll round it up to 50.

01:39:36.403 --> 01:39:40.374
7-Eleven also at one point offered a size

01:39:40.374 --> 01:39:43.177
that was even bigger,
called the Team Gulp,

01:39:43.177 --> 01:39:45.212
which, again, according to them,

01:39:45.212 --> 01:39:47.848
was 128 fluid ounces

01:39:47.848 --> 01:39:50.384
for your team,

01:39:50.384 --> 01:39:53.721
'cause who doesn't like
to, after a softball game,

01:39:53.721 --> 01:39:57.324
go to 7-Eleven, get a
Team Gulp and 10 straws?

01:39:57.324 --> 01:40:00.127
You know, just kick it
with the boys, right?

01:40:00.127 --> 01:40:01.261
Come on, team.

01:40:01.261 --> 01:40:04.264
Yeah, right. That's for one
person, don't be ridiculous.

01:40:05.966 --> 01:40:10.037
Here are many, many, many 7-Eleven items

01:40:10.037 --> 01:40:11.905
you can get in the US
you can't get in Japan.

01:40:11.905 --> 01:40:14.641
And here are many of the 7-Eleven items

01:40:14.641 --> 01:40:16.210
exclusive to Japan.

01:40:16.210 --> 01:40:20.014
Japan puts the "convenience"
in the convenience store.

01:40:20.014 --> 01:40:21.749
We call it konbini,

01:40:21.749 --> 01:40:24.351
which is the abbreviation
of the convenience store,

01:40:24.351 --> 01:40:26.687
and it makes our life a lot easier.

01:40:26.687 --> 01:40:30.257
For example, office workers
rely on stores like 7-Eleven

01:40:30.257 --> 01:40:32.693
for food and drink to keep them happy

01:40:32.693 --> 01:40:35.396
so that they can be productive at work.

01:40:35.396 --> 01:40:38.732
And for students, they tend
to buy juices and snacks

01:40:38.732 --> 01:40:41.368
and hot foods, instant noodles, you know.

01:40:41.368 --> 01:40:44.338
And when I was a kid, I would often eat

01:40:44.338 --> 01:40:46.040
hot foods and instant noodles

01:40:46.040 --> 01:40:50.778
with my friends and
with my ex-girlfriends.

01:40:50.778 --> 01:40:52.880
7-Eleven memories.

01:40:56.216 --> 01:40:58.118
And for families, there is pretty much

01:40:58.118 --> 01:41:00.354
every daily essential they may need.

01:41:00.354 --> 01:41:02.222
And also you can pay your bills,

01:41:02.222 --> 01:41:05.192
get ticket reservations
for music and sports,

01:41:05.192 --> 01:41:09.029
7-Eleven even has its own bank and ATMs.

01:41:09.029 --> 01:41:12.299
No matter where you go, especially
in big cities like Tokyo,

01:41:12.299 --> 01:41:16.103
you can find more than one
konbini on every block.

01:41:16.103 --> 01:41:18.205
Yeah, it's a bit different here in the US.

01:41:18.205 --> 01:41:20.774
I do frequent 7-Eleven, and it's not bad,

01:41:20.774 --> 01:41:22.443
but the vibe is more kind of like

01:41:22.443 --> 01:41:24.578
get the thing you need and go.

01:41:24.578 --> 01:41:27.581
The food is usually pretty hit or miss,

01:41:27.581 --> 01:41:29.716
usually miss in my experience.

01:41:29.716 --> 01:41:31.819
The hot food looks like it's
been sitting out for a while,

01:41:31.819 --> 01:41:33.454
so I usually don't get it.

01:41:33.454 --> 01:41:36.590
Since there are way too many
items exclusive to Japan

01:41:36.590 --> 01:41:38.992
for us to buy for one episode,

01:41:38.992 --> 01:41:42.229
so I've curated some of
my favorites for you guys.

01:41:42.229 --> 01:41:44.465
This is still a ton of food.

01:41:44.465 --> 01:41:47.668
So, here we have Japanese onigiris.

01:41:47.668 --> 01:41:49.436
This one is plum,

01:41:49.436 --> 01:41:50.771
tuna mayonnaise,

01:41:50.771 --> 01:41:52.639
shrimp and mayonnaise,

01:41:52.639 --> 01:41:55.909
mentaiko, which is spicy cod roe.

01:41:55.909 --> 01:41:58.278
I picked these onigiris from the back,

01:41:58.278 --> 01:42:02.816
because onigiri in the
back are fresh of all time.

01:42:02.816 --> 01:42:05.052
And let me show you how to open this one.

01:42:05.052 --> 01:42:09.356
Just pull this over till here ...

01:42:13.093 --> 01:42:15.996
Like this, so that you can have

01:42:15.996 --> 01:42:17.998
the dried seaweed.

01:42:19.867 --> 01:42:20.868
Itadakimasu.

01:42:22.936 --> 01:42:27.107
Mm, a little bit sweet,
a little bit of sour.

01:42:27.107 --> 01:42:30.277
So, here is our sushi.

01:42:30.277 --> 01:42:33.847
Look at this huge salmon sushi.

01:42:33.847 --> 01:42:35.182
Ah!

01:42:35.182 --> 01:42:37.885
Gorgeous. Gorgeous sushi.

01:42:37.885 --> 01:42:39.086
Itadakimasu.

01:42:39.086 --> 01:42:40.888
Oh, my God, this is so delicious.

01:42:41.989 --> 01:42:42.823
Mm.

01:42:46.560 --> 01:42:47.761
Osushi!

01:42:48.629 --> 01:42:52.099
We've got this long natto roll.

01:42:54.334 --> 01:42:56.270
Personally, I love natto.

01:42:56.270 --> 01:42:58.572
But even Japanese people,

01:42:58.572 --> 01:43:03.377
50% of them like it, 50%
of them don't like it.

01:43:03.377 --> 01:43:05.746
This is an acquired taste.

01:43:09.249 --> 01:43:11.852
So, after this sticky
and smelly natto roll,

01:43:11.852 --> 01:43:15.489
I've got sushi roll special package.

01:43:15.489 --> 01:43:18.425
So when it comes to this
one, it's called oinarisan.

01:43:18.425 --> 01:43:20.027
It has rice inside,

01:43:20.027 --> 01:43:22.996
and the skin is a sweet tofu skin.

01:43:25.866 --> 01:43:26.800
Mm!

01:43:26.800 --> 01:43:29.836
I'll admit, oinarisan umai wa.

01:43:29.836 --> 01:43:31.538
This is so good.

01:43:31.538 --> 01:43:34.041
So, my grandma always cooked this for me.

01:43:34.041 --> 01:43:37.844
And this makes me happy all the time.

01:43:37.844 --> 01:43:42.816
And next to oinarisan,
this gorgeous sushi roll,

01:43:42.816 --> 01:43:46.587
it's like Japanese version
of California roll.

01:43:46.587 --> 01:43:47.654
Itadakimasu.

01:43:49.723 --> 01:43:51.925
Wah!

01:43:51.925 --> 01:43:55.762
1,000% better than California roll.

01:43:55.762 --> 01:43:57.564
Kanpyo maki.

01:43:57.564 --> 01:44:01.568
In English it's, like, dried-gourd roll.

01:44:01.568 --> 01:44:02.569
Itadakimasu.

01:44:03.704 --> 01:44:05.105
Perfect sushi roll.

01:44:05.105 --> 01:44:08.408
And last one, we have
pickles, radish pickles.

01:44:08.408 --> 01:44:09.476
It's quite yellow.

01:44:09.476 --> 01:44:12.512
It definitely has yellow No. 5.

01:44:12.512 --> 01:44:13.747
Itadakimasu.

01:44:15.115 --> 01:44:18.118
I'm gonna give them Grammy award.

01:44:20.954 --> 01:44:22.522
And standing ovation.

01:44:24.458 --> 01:44:26.460
Ah, the hot food at a 7-Eleven in the US.

01:44:26.460 --> 01:44:29.763
We got a lot of options,
not as many as Japan.

01:44:29.763 --> 01:44:31.698
I'm not quite sure what
some of this stuff is

01:44:31.698 --> 01:44:34.134
just by looking at it, so
let me go down the list.

01:44:34.134 --> 01:44:36.303
Nachos. They're the self-service nachos,

01:44:36.303 --> 01:44:38.205
so they have the chips ready to go,

01:44:38.205 --> 01:44:39.640
and then you just open them up

01:44:39.640 --> 01:44:42.576
and add cheese and chili onto them.

01:44:44.878 --> 01:44:46.280
Ugh. No, thank you.

01:44:46.280 --> 01:44:47.914
Over here, these mini tacos.

01:44:47.914 --> 01:44:50.951
Man, these look really, like ...

01:44:51.885 --> 01:44:53.120
I bit my face.

01:44:53.987 --> 01:44:55.489
Oh, man. They've been sitting for a while,

01:44:55.489 --> 01:44:56.523
so I'll forgive them.

01:44:56.523 --> 01:45:00.527
We also have wings,
crispy and not so crispy.

01:45:00.527 --> 01:45:04.264
Pocket bean burrito guy. Look at that.

01:45:04.264 --> 01:45:07.034
Over here in the roller-taquito section,

01:45:07.034 --> 01:45:09.369
you can get a barbecue
bacon cheeseburger roller,

01:45:09.369 --> 01:45:10.937
spicy garlic roller,

01:45:10.937 --> 01:45:12.272
regular taquito,

01:45:12.272 --> 01:45:13.907
Korean barbecue taquito.

01:45:13.907 --> 01:45:15.609
Also, we have chicken sandwiches,

01:45:15.609 --> 01:45:16.910
a black bean burger,

01:45:16.910 --> 01:45:19.980
glazed cheesy barbecue meatballs.

01:45:19.980 --> 01:45:22.082
Also at our 7-Elevens, you
can get a pepperoni pizza,

01:45:22.082 --> 01:45:24.785
cheese, or seven-meat.

01:45:24.785 --> 01:45:27.788
And also for hot dogs, we got
an exclusive hot picante dog.

01:45:30.057 --> 01:45:30.891
No.

01:45:30.891 --> 01:45:33.327
So, here are our hot food sections.

01:45:33.327 --> 01:45:35.595
We've got steamed buns.

01:45:35.595 --> 01:45:38.265
It's got pork and bamboo shoots.

01:45:38.265 --> 01:45:41.668
And this is really standard nikuman.

01:45:41.668 --> 01:45:46.306
So, next size up, we
have the doubled nikuman.

01:45:46.306 --> 01:45:48.175
And next one, this little guy.

01:45:49.142 --> 01:45:51.011
What is this?

01:45:51.011 --> 01:45:52.679
Sweet beans steamed bun.

01:45:52.679 --> 01:45:57.150
And last steamed bun is pizza bun.

01:45:57.150 --> 01:45:59.886
You really are the pizza!

01:46:02.556 --> 01:46:03.657
Delicious.

01:46:03.657 --> 01:46:05.459
So, all these things, like,

01:46:05.459 --> 01:46:08.128
around 100 yen to 200 yen or so.

01:46:08.128 --> 01:46:12.466
So if you're broke, you
should definitely try this.

01:46:12.466 --> 01:46:16.002
We've got these ones.

01:46:16.002 --> 01:46:18.572
This one is called curry pan.

01:46:18.572 --> 01:46:21.074
So deep-fried curry bread.

01:46:21.074 --> 01:46:23.176
I wanna eat it. I wanna eat this!

01:46:23.176 --> 01:46:24.978
I wanna eat this right now!

01:46:24.978 --> 01:46:26.113
Itadakimasu!

01:46:29.883 --> 01:46:31.685
Holy moly.

01:46:31.685 --> 01:46:34.121
Um, it's freaking delicious.

01:46:34.121 --> 01:46:36.390
And next one, croquette.

01:46:36.390 --> 01:46:40.660
So it's basically got
potato and pork mince.

01:46:40.660 --> 01:46:44.431
And last hot food we've got is corn dog.

01:46:44.431 --> 01:46:46.833
So, this one right here is
a pretty Japanese-y one.

01:46:46.833 --> 01:46:48.902
It's got ketchup and mustard,

01:46:48.902 --> 01:46:51.738
and you just squeeze
this one onto this one.

01:46:51.738 --> 01:46:53.807
All right, let's go, let's go,

01:46:53.807 --> 01:46:55.876
let's go, let's go, let's go!

01:46:57.978 --> 01:47:00.714
In Japan, we have these chicken options.

01:47:00.714 --> 01:47:04.751
First, I'm going to start
with this one, karaage-bo.

01:47:09.723 --> 01:47:12.492
So, in Japan, when you make
Japanese fried chicken,

01:47:12.492 --> 01:47:14.261
you put some soy sauce on it.

01:47:14.261 --> 01:47:17.764
So it has soy-sauce flavor
and also garlic flavor.

01:47:17.764 --> 01:47:20.167
It's so freaking delicious.

01:47:20.167 --> 01:47:21.334
So, this karaage-bo,

01:47:21.334 --> 01:47:26.306
it's got one, two, three,

01:47:26.306 --> 01:47:28.308
and four karaages.

01:47:28.308 --> 01:47:31.278
We have fried chicken,

01:47:31.278 --> 01:47:33.346
spicy fried chicken,

01:47:33.346 --> 01:47:34.948
chicken nuggets.

01:47:34.948 --> 01:47:36.216
Hot sandwich,

01:47:36.216 --> 01:47:39.953
the Buffalo-style chicken slider.

01:47:39.953 --> 01:47:41.488
The cheeseburger

01:47:41.488 --> 01:47:43.390
and the bacon cheeseburger.

01:47:43.390 --> 01:47:45.659
Look, I mean, can you
even tell which one's,

01:47:45.659 --> 01:47:47.461
right, which one?

01:47:47.461 --> 01:47:48.295
Huh?

01:47:49.496 --> 01:47:51.832
I'm assuming, obviously,
this burger's been cooked.

01:47:53.700 --> 01:47:56.136
More on this in the ingredients section.

01:47:56.136 --> 01:47:59.606
7-Eleven in the US, and I think probably

01:47:59.606 --> 01:48:00.907
here in Southern California,

01:48:00.907 --> 01:48:02.943
has tacos and burritos.

01:48:02.943 --> 01:48:06.246
Get yourself a chicken fajita taco,

01:48:06.246 --> 01:48:07.547
al pastor taco.

01:48:07.547 --> 01:48:08.815
Bet this one's good.

01:48:08.815 --> 01:48:11.318
And a chorizo breakfast taco.

01:48:11.318 --> 01:48:14.521
The spicy beef, bean, and cheese burrito.

01:48:14.521 --> 01:48:15.922
This ain't any burrito, baby.

01:48:15.922 --> 01:48:18.992
It's The Bomb.

01:48:18.992 --> 01:48:21.061
Bombing out the toilet, good God.

01:48:21.061 --> 01:48:23.396
You're getting this and
you're microwaving it there.

01:48:23.396 --> 01:48:25.432
So if you're, like,
walking out the 7-Eleven

01:48:25.432 --> 01:48:26.566
chomping on The Bomb,

01:48:26.566 --> 01:48:28.969
like, better make it home in time.

01:48:28.969 --> 01:48:30.770
'Cause oh, man, it's coming.

01:48:30.770 --> 01:48:32.839
Empanadas, right?
Yuelei: Yeah.

01:48:32.839 --> 01:48:33.907
I don't want this.

01:48:33.907 --> 01:48:36.510
I'm gonna go ahead and put this in here

01:48:36.510 --> 01:48:37.577
and then close the lid

01:48:37.577 --> 01:48:39.012
like it's a coffin.

01:48:40.380 --> 01:48:41.448
Go away forever.

01:48:41.448 --> 01:48:44.518
All right, so here are my favorite bentos.

01:48:44.518 --> 01:48:46.253
Let's take a look at this one.

01:48:46.253 --> 01:48:48.255
It's called nori bento.

01:48:48.255 --> 01:48:50.857
This one is a pretty popular one in Japan.

01:48:50.857 --> 01:48:53.493
So it's got croquette,
a deep-fried fish cake,

01:48:53.493 --> 01:48:55.762
fried fish with tartar sauce.

01:48:55.762 --> 01:48:57.264
Kinpira gobo.

01:48:57.264 --> 01:48:59.933
It's like Japanese traditional salad.

01:48:59.933 --> 01:49:01.201
Pickles.

01:49:01.201 --> 01:49:02.402
And as you can see right here,

01:49:02.402 --> 01:49:04.504
it's got spicy cod roe.

01:49:04.504 --> 01:49:09.476
Under this seaweed, it's
got rice and fish flakes.

01:49:09.476 --> 01:49:10.911
I love this bento.

01:49:10.911 --> 01:49:12.579
Like, when I was a student,

01:49:12.579 --> 01:49:15.715
I think I would eat this every single day.

01:49:15.715 --> 01:49:19.185
So, after my favorite one,
this one. Look at this!

01:49:19.185 --> 01:49:23.189
So this one is a Korean-style beef bento.

01:49:23.189 --> 01:49:26.293
Oh, man, smells so good.

01:49:29.296 --> 01:49:30.764
Whoo!

01:49:30.764 --> 01:49:34.568
Everything right here is so amazing.

01:49:34.568 --> 01:49:35.569
Fantastic.

01:49:35.569 --> 01:49:38.271
This is so mashisoyo.

01:49:39.205 --> 01:49:40.774
Tonkatsu bento,

01:49:40.774 --> 01:49:44.177
and it comes with this
sauce for this tonkatsu.

01:49:44.177 --> 01:49:45.679
Look how thick it is.

01:49:45.679 --> 01:49:50.684
So, outside from bentos,
we have soba, soba noodle.

01:49:50.784 --> 01:49:52.852
Put this sauce first.

01:49:52.852 --> 01:49:55.956
Put wasabi and dried seaweed.

01:49:55.956 --> 01:49:58.925
And then you put water onto soba noodle.

01:49:58.925 --> 01:50:00.160
It's getting moist.

01:50:01.828 --> 01:50:05.165
And don't forget to put
green onions right here.

01:50:05.165 --> 01:50:06.099
Itadakimasu.

01:50:06.099 --> 01:50:09.469
So you put soba noodle in this box.

01:50:11.404 --> 01:50:13.106
[slurping]

01:50:14.341 --> 01:50:15.408
Umai!

01:50:15.408 --> 01:50:18.011
I guarantee you can't stop eating this,

01:50:18.011 --> 01:50:19.946
'cause it's so delicious.

01:50:19.946 --> 01:50:21.781
Sorry I slurped the noodles.

01:50:21.781 --> 01:50:24.517
Because Japanese people or Asian people

01:50:24.517 --> 01:50:27.587
do make noises when you eat noodles.

01:50:27.587 --> 01:50:28.955
We slurp.

01:50:28.955 --> 01:50:30.056
Slurp!

01:50:30.056 --> 01:50:31.725
Slurp right now!

01:50:31.725 --> 01:50:33.126
They got the meals over there in Japan.

01:50:33.126 --> 01:50:34.194
We got meals too,

01:50:34.194 --> 01:50:37.130
like this ready-made ricotta-, Romano-,

01:50:37.130 --> 01:50:39.032
and Parmesan-cheese-stuffed ravioli

01:50:39.032 --> 01:50:40.467
topped with marinara sauce and mozzarella.

01:50:40.467 --> 01:50:41.935
Ugh.

01:50:41.935 --> 01:50:43.703
Just stop, stop doing this.

01:50:43.703 --> 01:50:45.338
Stop, please.

01:50:45.338 --> 01:50:46.873
Stop.

01:50:46.873 --> 01:50:47.707
Oden.

01:50:47.707 --> 01:50:50.343
So, oden is like Japanese
traditional hot pot.

01:50:50.343 --> 01:50:54.714
It's got fish cake,
fried tofu, noodle thing.

01:50:54.714 --> 01:50:56.449
This is made from potato.

01:50:56.449 --> 01:50:58.251
Egg, radish.

01:50:58.251 --> 01:51:00.186
In winter, when you eat this,

01:51:00.186 --> 01:51:02.555
this warms you up, from your heart.

01:51:04.090 --> 01:51:04.924
To your body.

01:51:04.924 --> 01:51:07.661
And next, gratin doria.

01:51:07.661 --> 01:51:11.197
So, obviously it's got meat
sauce and a lot of cheese.

01:51:11.197 --> 01:51:14.601
Under this cheese, it's
got a lot of rice in there.

01:51:14.601 --> 01:51:16.436
It's like Japanese Western food.

01:51:16.436 --> 01:51:19.372
We have 7-Premium main dishes.

01:51:19.372 --> 01:51:22.542
Naan and butter chicken curry.

01:51:22.542 --> 01:51:25.378
And next we have 7-Premium side dishes.

01:51:25.378 --> 01:51:28.348
Mackerel, grilled mackerel.

01:51:28.348 --> 01:51:31.551
We also have mackerel in miso.

01:51:31.551 --> 01:51:34.120
Saba miso is [chef's kiss].

01:51:34.120 --> 01:51:35.789
Smoked tongue.

01:51:35.789 --> 01:51:37.891
In Japan, it's a pretty popular item,

01:51:37.891 --> 01:51:41.227
especially when you go to a
Japanese barbecue restaurant,

01:51:41.227 --> 01:51:44.698
we order the beef tongue or pig tongue.

01:51:44.698 --> 01:51:47.567
So this one used to be like this.

01:51:47.567 --> 01:51:49.369
Smells so good.

01:51:49.369 --> 01:51:50.570
So fancy.

01:51:52.939 --> 01:51:54.407
It's marvelous.

01:51:54.407 --> 01:51:57.043
So, after this sexy tongue,

01:51:57.043 --> 01:52:00.080
we have sexy fish cake.

01:52:00.080 --> 01:52:01.948
And look at this bar.

01:52:01.948 --> 01:52:02.982
It's a chicken bar,

01:52:02.982 --> 01:52:05.685
