with ham, egg, and cheese.

01:54:00.900 --> 01:54:03.136
Ooh, an English muffin with
bacon, egg, and cheese.

01:54:03.136 --> 01:54:05.405
We also have English muffins
with sausage, egg, and cheese,

01:54:05.405 --> 01:54:06.573
sausage biscuits,

01:54:06.573 --> 01:54:08.541
and sausage, egg, and cheese croissants.

01:54:08.541 --> 01:54:10.577
The 7-Eleven signature brand also has

01:54:10.577 --> 01:54:13.680
mini doughnuts, chocolate,
cinnamon, crunch,

01:54:13.680 --> 01:54:15.415
and, of course, powdered.

01:54:15.415 --> 01:54:16.249
Madeleines.

01:54:16.249 --> 01:54:18.284
7-Eleven has cookies right
at the register for a dollar.

01:54:18.284 --> 01:54:21.154
You can get yourself some
macadamia nut cookies,

01:54:21.154 --> 01:54:23.456
oatmeal raisin, sugar,

01:54:23.456 --> 01:54:24.924
but there's also a
chocolate chip cookie one.

01:54:24.924 --> 01:54:26.993
Baked goods, you get
yourself some muffins.

01:54:26.993 --> 01:54:28.228
This is a blueberry muffin.

01:54:28.228 --> 01:54:29.262
Coffee cake.

01:54:29.262 --> 01:54:30.597
Crispy rice treat bar.

01:54:30.597 --> 01:54:31.564
Notice it doesn't say Rice Krispie,

01:54:31.564 --> 01:54:33.366
'cause you know that's copywritten.

01:54:33.366 --> 01:54:34.934
Walnut fudge brownie,

01:54:34.934 --> 01:54:36.269
bear claw Danish,

01:54:36.269 --> 01:54:37.737
iced honey bun,

01:54:37.737 --> 01:54:38.705
cheese Danish,

01:54:38.705 --> 01:54:40.106
mixed berry Danish,

01:54:40.106 --> 01:54:42.408
glazed honey bun.

01:54:42.408 --> 01:54:45.144
I got these prepackaged, it
says "flavored snack pie."

01:54:45.144 --> 01:54:46.312
That's a weird way of putting it.

01:54:46.312 --> 01:54:49.782
Lemon, key lime, banana cream.

01:54:49.782 --> 01:54:51.684
I feel like they used the
same -- that's the same.

01:54:51.684 --> 01:54:53.253
That's Photoshop right there, buddy.

01:54:53.253 --> 01:54:55.388
Boston cream, apple,

01:54:55.388 --> 01:54:57.590
and the last one, strawberry cheesecake.

01:54:57.590 --> 01:54:58.524
Key lime.

01:55:01.127 --> 01:55:02.729
Look at all that cream in there.

01:55:02.729 --> 01:55:03.563
It's key limey.

01:55:03.563 --> 01:55:04.397
Oh, yeah.

01:55:04.397 --> 01:55:05.231
Oatmeal!

01:55:05.231 --> 01:55:07.467
That's obviously maple syrup right there.

01:55:07.467 --> 01:55:08.735
But the first thing I
did when I looked at it,

01:55:08.735 --> 01:55:11.037
I was like, "Wait, does
this have brandy in it?"

01:55:11.037 --> 01:55:12.071
Boozy oatmeal.

01:55:12.071 --> 01:55:14.007
You can put hot water in here, Joe.

01:55:14.007 --> 01:55:15.742
Or hot milk, Yuelei.

01:55:15.742 --> 01:55:17.477
Or hot whiskey.

01:55:17.477 --> 01:55:19.579
Your boss won't notice the difference.

01:55:19.579 --> 01:55:20.914
Well, at first.

01:55:20.914 --> 01:55:23.449
Here we have Japanese type of bread.

01:55:23.449 --> 01:55:26.052
Stir-fried-noodles-and-sauce bread.

01:55:26.052 --> 01:55:28.221
We call it yakisoba pan.

01:55:28.221 --> 01:55:33.226
Now, you may be thinking what
the [dolphin chirps] is this?

01:55:33.226 --> 01:55:36.829
So, it's like hot dog,
but instead of sausage,

01:55:36.829 --> 01:55:40.099
we've got stir-fried noodle inside.

01:55:40.099 --> 01:55:42.201
Carb, carb.

01:55:42.201 --> 01:55:43.069
It makes you fat.

01:55:43.069 --> 01:55:44.604
Bread makes you fat?!

01:55:44.604 --> 01:55:47.373
So, kids love this noodle and bread.

01:55:47.373 --> 01:55:48.641
Itadakimasu.

01:55:52.045 --> 01:55:53.279
Mm!

01:55:53.279 --> 01:55:56.115
This one reminds me of my childhood,

01:55:56.115 --> 01:56:00.486
me playing tags in the
mountain and chasing the girls.

01:56:00.486 --> 01:56:04.023
Now a lot of girls chasing me.

01:56:04.023 --> 01:56:06.125
This is a crab bread.

01:56:06.125 --> 01:56:08.828
It's got two crab-shaped bread.

01:56:08.828 --> 01:56:11.931
Now, the question is,
does it taste like crab?

01:56:13.833 --> 01:56:15.335
It doesn't taste like crab.

01:56:15.335 --> 01:56:17.537
Taste like just bread.

01:56:17.537 --> 01:56:18.571
Pink bread.

01:56:18.571 --> 01:56:22.442
It's a
cherry-blossom-flavored-coating bread.

01:56:22.442 --> 01:56:23.943
This pink stuff is,

01:56:23.943 --> 01:56:25.545
it's pretty sour.

01:56:28.047 --> 01:56:29.749
It tastes like cherry blossom

01:56:29.749 --> 01:56:32.218
and like my first kiss.

01:56:32.218 --> 01:56:35.588
This is the salty, savory snack zone.

01:56:35.588 --> 01:56:36.889
Ah, so much stuff.

01:56:36.889 --> 01:56:39.025
And I've hit the "Food Wars" wall.

01:56:39.025 --> 01:56:41.627
Hot and spicy cracklin
curls, the original,

01:56:41.627 --> 01:56:43.896
and the fried pork rinds, chili lime.

01:56:45.498 --> 01:56:48.167
I'm not tasting anything
pork-related to it.

01:56:48.167 --> 01:56:49.736
Little pig guy there.

01:56:49.736 --> 01:56:50.570
Little piggy guy.

01:56:50.570 --> 01:56:51.637
You're on the menu, buddy.

01:56:51.637 --> 01:56:55.541
Next, 7-Selects has
their own veggie straws.

01:56:55.541 --> 01:56:59.012
This will be the trail
mix and mix-like section.

01:56:59.012 --> 01:57:02.348
We got these
cheese-pizza-flavored snack mix.

01:57:02.348 --> 01:57:04.784
You're gonna be a stinky boy
if you have a bunch of these.

01:57:04.784 --> 01:57:07.453
Now they got the spicy ranch flavor mix.

01:57:07.453 --> 01:57:09.756
And this last one, just sesame sticks.

01:57:09.756 --> 01:57:12.158
For those of you who like
to get your trail mix

01:57:12.158 --> 01:57:14.327
or your Chex Mix and then unmix them

01:57:14.327 --> 01:57:16.029
and organize them and eat them like that,

01:57:16.029 --> 01:57:18.998
7-Eleven has got the snack for you.

01:57:18.998 --> 01:57:21.768
Oh, this is kind of a party snack mix.

01:57:21.768 --> 01:57:22.668
Eh.

01:57:22.668 --> 01:57:25.505
This is what I would totally
get, yogurt pretzels.

01:57:25.505 --> 01:57:27.040
They put yogurt on there,
and, like, you're thinking,

01:57:27.040 --> 01:57:28.107
"Oh, yogurt, that's healthy, right?"

01:57:28.107 --> 01:57:30.243
I mean, it's just, it's the same as icing.

01:57:30.243 --> 01:57:31.911
Now, you're looking at this going,

01:57:31.911 --> 01:57:35.181
"Jack Link's beef jerky?
That's not a 7-Eleven brand."

01:57:35.181 --> 01:57:36.215
No, it's not.

01:57:36.215 --> 01:57:39.252
But as you can see,
exclusive 7-Eleven flavors.

01:57:39.252 --> 01:57:41.788
See, this was like, "Hey,
Jack Link's, guess what?

01:57:41.788 --> 01:57:44.290
We're about to push you
out of our shelf space.

01:57:44.290 --> 01:57:46.159
So do a deal with us, or
you're gone completely."

01:57:46.159 --> 01:57:46.993
And Jack Link's was like,

01:57:46.993 --> 01:57:48.661
"No, I've got kids to feed, please!"

01:57:48.661 --> 01:57:50.830
Brown sugar bourbon,

01:57:50.830 --> 01:57:51.964
original recipe,

01:57:51.964 --> 01:57:53.032
original.

01:57:53.032 --> 01:57:54.434
Hickory-smoked bacon.

01:57:54.434 --> 01:57:56.436
Like snacking on cheese and nothing else?

01:57:56.436 --> 01:57:57.403
Full house, baby.

01:57:57.403 --> 01:57:59.972
This one is mozzarella cheese
wrapped in hard salami.

01:57:59.972 --> 01:58:01.240
Pepper Jack stick,

01:58:01.240 --> 01:58:02.408
Gouda cheese to go.

01:58:02.408 --> 01:58:04.544
Oh, the big one, the big
cheese, the white cheddar.

01:58:04.544 --> 01:58:06.512
This ain't your grandma's cheese.

01:58:06.512 --> 01:58:08.247
It's the big one.

01:58:08.247 --> 01:58:09.082
Just two.

01:58:09.082 --> 01:58:10.283
Cheddar cheese.

01:58:10.283 --> 01:58:13.119
Colby-Jack, which is
like camouflage cheese.

01:58:13.119 --> 01:58:14.153
Ugh!

01:58:14.153 --> 01:58:17.056
Pretzels. Mini twists, non yogurted.

01:58:17.056 --> 01:58:18.758
Pretzel nuggets. Ooh, gross.

01:58:18.758 --> 01:58:20.460
These ones have peanut
butter inside of them.

01:58:20.460 --> 01:58:22.361
Pretzel sticks. I feel like
there was a while there

01:58:22.361 --> 01:58:23.963
in the early '90s when they were like,

01:58:23.963 --> 01:58:25.998
"Chips are bad for you.
Eat pretzels instead."

01:58:25.998 --> 01:58:27.366
And these are really salty, too.

01:58:27.366 --> 01:58:29.235
A serving size of these is three.

01:58:29.235 --> 01:58:30.703
I would get this assuming I'm gonna sit

01:58:30.703 --> 01:58:32.305
and eat this whole bag in one sitting.

01:58:32.305 --> 01:58:33.539
I'm not gonna do three at a time.

01:58:33.539 --> 01:58:36.576
The whole bag is 1,160 milligrams,

01:58:36.576 --> 01:58:38.411
50% of your sodium intake.

01:58:38.411 --> 01:58:39.779
Mini rice cakes.

01:58:41.013 --> 01:58:41.848
Chips.

01:58:41.848 --> 01:58:45.051
7-Eleven has a bunch of
their own potato chips,

01:58:45.051 --> 01:58:47.887
including the original, fiery hot.

01:58:47.887 --> 01:58:49.355
Kettle chips, which are way better

01:58:49.355 --> 01:58:50.990
than regular chips, again.

01:58:50.990 --> 01:58:52.859
Spicy jalapeño, smoked Gouda.

01:58:52.859 --> 01:58:53.926
Ooh, Gouda.

01:58:53.926 --> 01:58:55.761
Barbecue, salt and pepper.

01:58:55.761 --> 01:58:58.731
Ruffles rip-offs. We got
cheddar and sour cream.

01:58:58.731 --> 01:59:00.399
Prime rib, I'm trying these.

01:59:00.399 --> 01:59:02.368
And Buffalo chicken dip.

01:59:02.368 --> 01:59:03.569
Prime rib?

01:59:03.569 --> 01:59:05.304
Woof, smells terrible.

01:59:06.272 --> 01:59:08.141
Oh, my God, that was so bad!

01:59:08.141 --> 01:59:10.042
It's definitely not this.

01:59:10.042 --> 01:59:11.477
Yeah, more like ground beef.

01:59:11.477 --> 01:59:12.979
And instead of one of these fancy forks,

01:59:12.979 --> 01:59:15.882
there'd be the plastic spork
that they have at 7-Eleven.

01:59:15.882 --> 01:59:18.184
They're opening the bag with the spork,

01:59:18.184 --> 01:59:19.352
meat's pouring out of it,

01:59:19.352 --> 01:59:21.754
it's on the floor of a 7-Eleven,

01:59:21.754 --> 01:59:23.756
with a guy mopping around it.

01:59:24.690 --> 01:59:27.126
Nuts, baby. Nuts.

01:59:27.126 --> 01:59:30.429
The rise and shine fiber blend
of a trail mix, whatever.

01:59:30.429 --> 01:59:32.698
Antioxidant. Yeah, right.

01:59:32.698 --> 01:59:35.868
Revive and thrive,
another antioxidant mix.

01:59:35.868 --> 01:59:38.337
Should've just handed
these out during COVID,

01:59:38.337 --> 01:59:39.672
would've bounced back in a week.

01:59:39.672 --> 01:59:41.007
Cashew halves.

01:59:42.008 --> 01:59:43.943
You like your nuts halved? Booyah.

01:59:43.943 --> 01:59:46.679
You like your nuts wholed? Booyah.

01:59:46.679 --> 01:59:48.114
Does it matter if they're whole or not?

01:59:48.114 --> 01:59:50.249
Would that affect the
flavor at all? Who cares?

01:59:50.249 --> 01:59:53.653
Spicy ranch pistachios.

01:59:53.653 --> 01:59:56.789
And, of course, jumbo flavored

01:59:56.789 --> 01:59:59.425
wasabi and soy nuts. Nope.

01:59:59.425 --> 02:00:02.628
Wasabi will never touch my
lips again after that video.

02:00:02.628 --> 02:00:05.898
So, here are my favorite instant noodles.

02:00:05.898 --> 02:00:06.999
Let's start.

02:00:06.999 --> 02:00:08.467
Ippudo ramen.

02:00:08.467 --> 02:00:10.336
Man, I love this.

02:00:10.336 --> 02:00:11.637
So, it's got some packets.

02:00:11.637 --> 02:00:13.539
Dried pork.

02:00:13.539 --> 02:00:16.075
It's a miso for the ramen soup.

02:00:16.075 --> 02:00:17.343
Dried veggies.

02:00:19.212 --> 02:00:20.479
And it's got noodles.

02:00:23.149 --> 02:00:24.650
All right.

02:00:24.650 --> 02:00:27.887
And you've got to wait for three minutes.

02:00:27.887 --> 02:00:31.324
So while I'm waiting for
this, I'm gonna go this one.

02:00:31.324 --> 02:00:33.726
So it's called Ippei-chan.

02:00:33.726 --> 02:00:36.395
So it basically is a yakisoba.

02:00:36.395 --> 02:00:39.398
Yakisoba is like Japanese
stir-fried noodles.

02:00:41.167 --> 02:00:43.903
So, you put some hot
water until this line.

02:00:44.770 --> 02:00:47.173
All right, so it's been three minutes.

02:00:47.173 --> 02:00:50.243
Put this soup into this bowl.

02:00:50.243 --> 02:00:51.477
Mix it.

02:00:53.713 --> 02:00:55.982
Smells so good!

02:01:00.653 --> 02:01:01.587
Bravo.

02:01:05.491 --> 02:01:08.361
So, Ippudo has a lot
of locations in Japan,

02:01:08.361 --> 02:01:11.631
including Tokyo, but this taste,

02:01:11.631 --> 02:01:13.666
this flavor is totally the same

02:01:13.666 --> 02:01:15.401
as the restaurant's serving.

02:01:15.401 --> 02:01:18.938
So just get it at 7-Eleven.

02:01:18.938 --> 02:01:22.708
Oh, shit, I totally forgot the, oh.

02:01:22.708 --> 02:01:24.377
So, I put some hot water, but --

02:01:24.377 --> 02:01:26.579
oh, shit!

02:01:26.579 --> 02:01:29.949
I should have thrown the
water away into the toilet.

02:01:29.949 --> 02:01:31.751
Gomen ne, noodles.

02:01:31.751 --> 02:01:33.486
Let's make yakisoba.

02:01:33.486 --> 02:01:37.857
[laughs] The volume of these noodles

02:01:37.857 --> 02:01:40.159
gets a lot bigger.

02:01:40.159 --> 02:01:42.295
OK, so put yakisoba sauce.

02:01:43.996 --> 02:01:45.231
And flakes.

02:01:46.165 --> 02:01:48.634
And most importantly, mayo.

02:01:48.634 --> 02:01:50.036
Mayo beam!

02:01:50.903 --> 02:01:52.405
Oh!

02:01:52.405 --> 02:01:54.106
And mix it up.

02:01:55.241 --> 02:01:56.075
Ta-da!

02:01:56.075 --> 02:01:58.144
So, this is yakisoba.

02:01:58.144 --> 02:02:01.447
We usually eat this,
like, at summer festival.

02:02:04.050 --> 02:02:05.685
Pretty good, as always.

02:02:05.685 --> 02:02:09.021
Next, we have tako-meshi.

02:02:09.021 --> 02:02:12.258
Look at this. So, it's got green onions,

02:02:12.258 --> 02:02:14.560
and I believe this is tako.

02:02:17.496 --> 02:02:20.132
So, three minutes again.

02:02:20.132 --> 02:02:22.968
Look at this final noodle.

02:02:22.968 --> 02:02:26.939
It says ultra-spicy final.

02:02:26.939 --> 02:02:29.675
You're going to be crying
because of the spiciness.

02:02:29.675 --> 02:02:31.210
It's too spicy.

02:02:31.210 --> 02:02:33.446
But I'm going to try this,

02:02:33.446 --> 02:02:35.081
only for shooting purpose.

02:02:35.081 --> 02:02:36.282
This is for you guys!

02:02:36.282 --> 02:02:37.483
We can do it.
Clip: Never give up!

02:02:38.984 --> 02:02:41.387
Oh, man, I'm so scared.

02:02:44.657 --> 02:02:48.094
All right, so I think
it's time to eat this one.

02:02:48.094 --> 02:02:52.765
So, I'm going to throw the
water away in the toilet again.

02:02:52.765 --> 02:02:54.367
Let's go to the toilet.

02:02:56.135 --> 02:02:58.771
And put yakisoba sauce.

02:02:58.771 --> 02:02:59.805
All righty.

02:03:02.375 --> 02:03:04.977
And the taste itself is
lighter than this one.

02:03:04.977 --> 02:03:07.680
I prefer this one, but,

02:03:07.680 --> 02:03:08.547
but,

02:03:08.547 --> 02:03:11.250
this is the king ramen.

02:03:11.250 --> 02:03:14.787
All right, so finally let's make

02:03:14.787 --> 02:03:17.022
the freaking spicy noodle.

02:03:17.022 --> 02:03:19.992
I call it death sauce.

02:03:19.992 --> 02:03:21.727
In case I'm dead,

02:03:21.727 --> 02:03:24.196
please find another Japanese host.

02:03:24.196 --> 02:03:26.432
It was nice to meet you, Food Insider.

02:03:26.432 --> 02:03:28.367
Go!

02:03:28.367 --> 02:03:31.170
Oh, man, look at this.

02:03:31.170 --> 02:03:33.672
It's not red, it's blood.

02:03:33.672 --> 02:03:35.274
I don't want to eat this.

02:03:36.242 --> 02:03:40.279
[coughing]

02:03:44.450 --> 02:03:45.551
Ah!

02:03:46.952 --> 02:03:47.787
Oh.

02:03:54.360 --> 02:03:57.196
Ah!

02:03:58.631 --> 02:04:01.100
I'm not joking, I'm not joking.

02:04:01.100 --> 02:04:03.169
Ah, ah.

02:04:07.239 --> 02:04:08.374
It hurts!

02:04:09.542 --> 02:04:10.676
Am I alive?

02:04:11.777 --> 02:04:13.846
Am I not dead?

02:04:13.846 --> 02:04:15.981
Am I in heaven?

02:04:15.981 --> 02:04:17.883
Hell?

02:04:17.883 --> 02:04:19.385
I feel like I'm in hell.

02:04:20.252 --> 02:04:22.655
It's not all junk food at
the 7-Eleven, Joe and Yuelei.

02:04:22.655 --> 02:04:27.226
They also have delicious
freshly sliced fruit.

02:04:27.226 --> 02:04:28.727
Prepackaged and everything,

02:04:28.727 --> 02:04:29.862
came straight from the ground,

02:04:29.862 --> 02:04:33.532
and it comes in a
container that will be here

02:04:33.532 --> 02:04:35.835
until the sun explodes.

02:04:35.835 --> 02:04:38.471
This, I mean, this has to be an LA thing.

02:04:38.471 --> 02:04:39.839
You can get mango with

02:04:39.839 --> 02:04:41.507
tajin seasoning.
Automated voice: Tajin.

02:04:41.507 --> 02:04:42.908
Fantastic combination.

02:04:42.908 --> 02:04:44.376
Finally, grape cup.

02:04:44.376 --> 02:04:48.714
7-Eleven also has its own
brand of packaged candies.

02:04:48.714 --> 02:04:50.282
Sour gummy bears,

02:04:50.282 --> 02:04:52.685
sour neon gummy worms,

02:04:52.685 --> 02:04:54.587
sour watermelon wedges,

02:04:54.587 --> 02:04:56.355
green apple rings,

02:04:56.355 --> 02:04:59.859
gummy worms for catching gummy fish.

02:04:59.859 --> 02:05:01.126
Heh-heh. You like that?

02:05:01.126 --> 02:05:02.895
Fruit leather, whatever we call this.

02:05:02.895 --> 02:05:04.730
Chili mango. Hell yeah, I'm trying these.

02:05:04.730 --> 02:05:05.698
Sweetened mango,

02:05:05.698 --> 02:05:08.400
and a sweetened fruit medley.

02:05:10.803 --> 02:05:13.439
Not bad. Oh, a little
spicier that I thought, whoa.

02:05:13.439 --> 02:05:15.908
There's also gummy bears and gummy sharks.

02:05:15.908 --> 02:05:17.343
There's also gummy peach rings.

02:05:17.343 --> 02:05:18.477
They got jelly beans,

02:05:18.477 --> 02:05:20.479
and they got sour cherries.

02:05:20.479 --> 02:05:22.114
7-Eleven Selects in the US also has

02:05:22.114 --> 02:05:25.985
their own line of sandwich cookies.

02:05:25.985 --> 02:05:29.054
Vanilla, pumpkin spice,

02:05:29.054 --> 02:05:31.090
double chocolate, peppermint,

02:05:31.090 --> 02:05:33.325
s'mores, the duplexes,

02:05:33.325 --> 02:05:34.527
lemon crème.

02:05:34.527 --> 02:05:35.694
Mm-mm-mm.

02:05:35.694 --> 02:05:38.197
So, here are Japanese sweets.

02:05:38.197 --> 02:05:41.767
Pink rice cake with red bean paste.

02:05:41.767 --> 02:05:45.204
So basically it's like
cherry blossom mochi.

02:05:45.204 --> 02:05:46.305
Itadakimasu.

02:05:49.542 --> 02:05:51.844
Mm, mm.

02:05:51.844 --> 02:05:55.748
I want to eat this under
the tree of cherry blossom.

02:05:55.748 --> 02:05:58.517
Cherry blossom, pew.

02:06:01.487 --> 02:06:04.256
Next, we have ninja gummy.

02:06:04.256 --> 02:06:06.892
He's like ninja salaryman.

02:06:06.892 --> 02:06:08.961
So, it's a hard gummy.

02:06:10.763 --> 02:06:13.399
It's really tough, like stones.

02:06:13.399 --> 02:06:15.401
[crunching]

02:06:15.401 --> 02:06:16.669
Toppo.

02:06:16.669 --> 02:06:20.272
It's like Pocky, but
the chocolate is inside.

02:06:21.273 --> 02:06:22.474
I'm loving it.

02:06:22.474 --> 02:06:24.643
Look at this cute guy!

02:06:24.643 --> 02:06:26.579
Koala no Machi.

02:06:26.579 --> 02:06:29.615
Koala's March Chocolate.

02:06:29.615 --> 02:06:32.151
My favorite would be this one.

02:06:32.151 --> 02:06:36.088
When I was a kid, I would
eat this every single day.

02:06:36.088 --> 02:06:38.991
And this taste is so nostalgic.

02:06:38.991 --> 02:06:41.760
Oh, little George is calling me like,

02:06:41.760 --> 02:06:43.629
"Hey, I wanna eat this! I wanna eat -- "

02:06:43.629 --> 02:06:46.565
Hey! We are filming right now.

02:06:46.565 --> 02:06:48.834
Later, after shooting, OK?

02:06:48.834 --> 02:06:49.668
"OK."

02:06:49.668 --> 02:06:51.737
OK. We're good.

02:06:51.737 --> 02:06:53.138
Pudding.

02:06:53.138 --> 02:06:54.873
Please prepare the plate.

02:06:54.873 --> 02:06:56.675
And you just do like this.

02:06:56.675 --> 02:06:58.944
One, two, three, go.

02:06:59.878 --> 02:07:01.814
The shape is like cherry blossom.

02:07:01.814 --> 02:07:03.248
Look how jelly it is.

02:07:07.953 --> 02:07:09.121
Mm!

02:07:09.121 --> 02:07:11.590
This is the best pudding ever.

02:07:11.590 --> 02:07:13.993
We had to go on a run to get more stuff.

02:07:13.993 --> 02:07:16.829
That's why visually this
all doesn't connect.

02:07:16.829 --> 02:07:19.865
7-Eleven's got macarons, French macarons.

02:07:19.865 --> 02:07:21.800
Ooh, mini cheesecakes,

02:07:21.800 --> 02:07:24.503
New York style and strawberry swirl.

02:07:24.503 --> 02:07:25.838
These I can get behind.

02:07:25.838 --> 02:07:27.740
Our 7-Eleven in the US has ice cream,

02:07:27.740 --> 02:07:30.876
such as banana cream pie,
caramel butter pecan,

02:07:30.876 --> 02:07:33.445
chocolate-covered strawberry,
double cookie dough,

02:07:33.445 --> 02:07:35.614
cookies 'n' cream, sea-salt caramel,

02:07:35.614 --> 02:07:37.916
strawberry-banana shortcake.

02:07:37.916 --> 02:07:39.785
So, let's start with cold stuff.

02:07:39.785 --> 02:07:43.088
We've got fried dumplings. It's frozen.

02:07:43.088 --> 02:07:45.257
Frozen takoyaki,

02:07:45.257 --> 02:07:47.493
frozen fried rice.

02:07:47.493 --> 02:07:51.964
So, after these frozen
meals, I got ice cream.

02:07:51.964 --> 02:07:53.632
Choco Monaka Jumbo.

02:07:53.632 --> 02:07:54.767
So, Choco Monaka Jumbo

02:07:54.767 --> 02:07:57.636
is like Japanese ice cream sandwich.

02:07:57.636 --> 02:08:00.305
Ah!

02:08:00.305 --> 02:08:01.807
Let me bite. Itadakimasu.

02:08:05.244 --> 02:08:07.179
Sorry, it looks gross. [laughs]

02:08:07.179 --> 02:08:08.414
So it's got ice cream,

02:08:08.414 --> 02:08:10.315
and it's got chocolate in the middle,

02:08:10.315 --> 02:08:13.052
and this crunchy on the outside.

02:08:13.052 --> 02:08:15.254
Every Japanese people get this one

02:08:15.254 --> 02:08:17.523
at least once in their life.

02:08:17.523 --> 02:08:19.858
And last ice cream, I got this one.

02:08:19.858 --> 02:08:22.394
Gorilla chocolate ice cream. [laughs]

02:08:22.394 --> 02:08:23.829
I don't know what this is.

02:08:23.829 --> 02:08:25.731
Ah.

02:08:25.731 --> 02:08:29.868
Ah! Ch-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t-t!

02:08:29.868 --> 02:08:33.238
Ah, sorry! Itadakimasu!

02:08:35.207 --> 02:08:36.642
This is delicious.

02:08:36.642 --> 02:08:40.279
Not only me, but Gorilla would love this.

02:08:40.279 --> 02:08:41.980
Lot of exclusive drinks.

02:08:41.980 --> 02:08:42.981
I don't know really where to begin,

02:08:42.981 --> 02:08:46.552
so I kind of lined them up
by perception of healthiness.

02:08:46.552 --> 02:08:48.854
So, all the way down
on this end, we've got

02:08:48.854 --> 02:08:50.823
7-Eleven Select Go Smart

02:08:50.823 --> 02:08:53.826
cold organic pressed juices.

02:08:53.826 --> 02:08:55.627
This one's the tropical glow.

02:08:55.627 --> 02:08:58.297
And this gross-looking one is, of course,

02:08:58.297 --> 02:09:00.165
clean and green.

02:09:00.165 --> 02:09:02.434
After that, we got these
prepackaged juices.

02:09:02.434 --> 02:09:06.605
These are the 7-Select Farmer's Grove.

02:09:06.605 --> 02:09:08.907
Cranberry cocktail, raspberry lemonade,

02:09:08.907 --> 02:09:11.977
orange juice, of course, regular lemonade.

02:09:11.977 --> 02:09:13.312
Then next up in the bigger ones

02:09:13.312 --> 02:09:16.248
we have the 7-Eleven teas.

02:09:16.248 --> 02:09:18.117
Peach black tea, sweet tea.

02:09:18.117 --> 02:09:19.485
They weren't kidding, man, look at that.

02:09:19.485 --> 02:09:20.886
Lemon sweet tea

02:09:20.886 --> 02:09:22.988
and green tea.

02:09:22.988 --> 02:09:25.324
Fruit punch, mango, guava.

02:09:25.324 --> 02:09:28.494
Energy, come on, herbal tonic.

02:09:28.494 --> 02:09:30.095
Herbal? This is herbal, guys? Yeah?

02:09:30.095 --> 02:09:32.498
7-Eleven also their own brand of ...

02:09:32.498 --> 02:09:34.500
are these considered energy drinks?

02:09:34.500 --> 02:09:36.135
The Gatorades and Powerades and the like.

02:09:36.135 --> 02:09:38.237
So Replenish, and of
course Replenish zero.

02:09:38.237 --> 02:09:40.405
I'm assuming zero added sugar.

02:09:40.405 --> 02:09:42.574
Orange mango, fruit punch, lemonade.

02:09:42.574 --> 02:09:44.576
The cherry is clear.

02:09:44.576 --> 02:09:46.445
What? Why is cherry clear?

02:09:46.445 --> 02:09:48.213
Guava splash, orange mango.

02:09:48.213 --> 02:09:49.548
♪ These are bad ♪

02:09:49.548 --> 02:09:51.817
7-Eleven energy.

02:09:51.817 --> 02:09:53.385
"Strawberry lemonade energy shot,

02:09:53.385 --> 02:09:55.587
one and half times the
caffeine of a cup of coffee."

02:09:55.587 --> 02:09:56.855
Oh, good God.

02:10:00.259 --> 02:10:01.160
Undrinkable.

02:10:01.160 --> 02:10:02.961
How bad does it have to
taste where this is too --

02:10:02.961 --> 02:10:03.796
I couldn't get to this?

02:10:03.796 --> 02:10:04.930
You've seen this show, right?

02:10:04.930 --> 02:10:06.498
You'll see what I'll tolerate.

02:10:06.498 --> 02:10:08.066
This, I can barely tolerate this.

02:10:10.903 --> 02:10:14.406
Here's something that
they don't have in Japan.

02:10:14.406 --> 02:10:15.407
They don't have Slurpees.

02:10:15.407 --> 02:10:16.608
That's nuts, right?

02:10:16.608 --> 02:10:18.477
Slurpees are -- how do
you describe a Slurpee?

02:10:18.477 --> 02:10:21.213
It's like a flavored slush.

02:10:21.213 --> 02:10:23.081
We have endless Slurpee flavors.

02:10:23.081 --> 02:10:25.651
The ones currently you can
get here in America are

02:10:25.651 --> 02:10:27.152
blue rocketberry,

02:10:27.152 --> 02:10:28.120
blood orange,

02:10:28.120 --> 02:10:29.755
Vitaminwater XXX,

02:10:29.755 --> 02:10:30.856
blue raspberry,

02:10:30.856 --> 02:10:32.624
blueberry lemonade bliss,

02:10:32.624 --> 02:10:34.226
cherry, Coca-Cola,

02:10:34.226 --> 02:10:36.461
Mountain Dew citrus, peach perfect,

02:10:36.461 --> 02:10:39.965
piña colada, and pineapple whip.

02:10:39.965 --> 02:10:42.367
So, here are Japanese exclusive drinks.

02:10:42.367 --> 02:10:45.003
We have vegetable juice, of course.

02:10:45.904 --> 02:10:48.273
Mm! Oishii.

02:10:48.273 --> 02:10:51.677
A lot of Japanese salarymen
drink this one every morning

02:10:51.677 --> 02:10:54.012
to get their day started.

02:10:54.012 --> 02:10:56.248
So this one is for Joe.

02:10:56.248 --> 02:10:58.917
Joe, you're missing a lot of veggies,

02:10:58.917 --> 02:11:01.019
so you should drink this one.

02:11:01.019 --> 02:11:04.723
Oi Ocha, my favorite green tea.

02:11:04.723 --> 02:11:07.159
And these two are hot drinks,

02:11:07.159 --> 02:11:09.962
black coffee and café latte.

02:11:09.962 --> 02:11:12.631
And this is our first time filming this.

02:11:12.631 --> 02:11:14.433
We have alcohol.

02:11:14.433 --> 02:11:17.736
We have 7-Premium beer.

02:11:17.736 --> 02:11:19.438
And this one is not beer.

02:11:19.438 --> 02:11:22.307
It's like Sprite with alcohol.

02:11:22.307 --> 02:11:25.244
It contains 9% of alcohol.

02:11:25.244 --> 02:11:26.745
It's pretty delicious,

02:11:26.745 --> 02:11:29.014
but at the same time,
it's pretty dangerous.

02:11:29.014 --> 02:11:31.116
Japanese sake.

02:11:31.116 --> 02:11:32.885
When you come to Japan, you can see

02:11:32.885 --> 02:11:35.687
a lot of people drinking alcohol outside.

02:11:35.687 --> 02:11:38.390
They're like [groans].

02:11:40.259 --> 02:11:42.661
They are not dead, they're just sleeping.

02:11:42.661 --> 02:11:43.929
They're drunk.

02:11:43.929 --> 02:11:44.963
Whisky.

02:11:44.963 --> 02:11:48.166
7-Eleven in the US has its own

02:11:48.166 --> 02:11:50.435
private brand wines,

02:11:50.435 --> 02:11:53.305
Yosemite Road, Trojan Horse,

02:11:53.305 --> 02:11:56.275
Plot and Point, and Voyager Point.

02:11:56.275 --> 02:11:59.745
It also has its own canned
wine brand, called Roamer.

02:11:59.745 --> 02:12:02.915
Perhaps the reason 7-Eleven
has such a wide variety

02:12:02.915 --> 02:12:06.752
of products in Japan is that
it's everywhere in Japan.

02:12:06.752 --> 02:12:10.722
There are 21,215 stores in Japan.

02:12:10.722 --> 02:12:12.257
That's crazy!

02:12:12.257 --> 02:12:16.361
Which is nearly 30% of all
the 7-Elevens in the world.

02:12:16.361 --> 02:12:20.032
Of course, all 37
prefectures have a 7-Eleven.

02:12:20.032 --> 02:12:21.733
And out of all of them,

02:12:21.733 --> 02:12:24.269
the city of Tokyo has the most locations,

02:12:24.269 --> 02:12:26.738
with 2,850.

02:12:26.738 --> 02:12:27.839
To put that in perspective,

02:12:27.839 --> 02:12:31.243
the US has 9,417 7-Elevens,

02:12:31.243 --> 02:12:33.946
and there's no 7-Elevens in 18 states.

02:12:33.946 --> 02:12:36.381
As far as states, California has the most,

02:12:36.381 --> 02:12:38.984
1,823.

02:12:38.984 --> 02:12:42.521
But as far as denseness in area,

02:12:42.521 --> 02:12:46.758
Las Vegas, Nevada, has the most, with 158.

02:12:48.961 --> 02:12:52.397
In Japan, our hot dog is 290 calories

02:12:52.397 --> 02:12:54.967
and 720 milligrams of sodium,

02:12:54.967 --> 02:12:59.237
which is 31.3% of your daily allowance.

02:12:59.237 --> 02:13:00.806
Our hot dog is 180 calories.

02:13:00.806 --> 02:13:02.474
Ooh. How about this?

02:13:02.474 --> 02:13:05.310
Our hot dog is 180 calories,
but for the frank only.

02:13:05.310 --> 02:13:06.578
The stats, for some reason,

02:13:06.578 --> 02:13:08.113
don't say anything about the bun.

02:13:08.113 --> 02:13:10.148
But this isn't much better for you.

02:13:10.148 --> 02:13:12.617
It's 570 milligrams of sodium,

02:13:12.617 --> 02:13:16.254
so around 24.8% of your daily allowance.

02:13:16.254 --> 02:13:18.857
Japan's hand-rolled tuna and mayo onigiri

02:13:18.857 --> 02:13:22.728
has 258 calories and is very filling.

02:13:22.728 --> 02:13:24.663
Remember this guy? The tuna sandwich.

02:13:24.663 --> 02:13:27.766
Here in the US, ours is 420 calories

02:13:27.766 --> 02:13:31.069
and lots of sodium, over 800 milligrams.

02:13:31.069 --> 02:13:32.237
Fuck!

02:13:32.237 --> 02:13:35.140
And in the US, a Super
Big Gulp of Coca-Cola,

02:13:35.140 --> 02:13:38.143
this isn't Coca-Cola, is 44 fluid ounces.

02:13:38.143 --> 02:13:42.347
It's 513 calories and 143 grams of carbs.

02:13:42.347 --> 02:13:44.783
That's over half your daily intake.

02:13:46.685 --> 02:13:49.321
In Japan, 7-Eleven does not disclose

02:13:49.321 --> 02:13:52.824
the ingredients list of its
freshly made food items.

02:13:52.824 --> 02:13:55.761
It does, however, tell
us the country of origin

02:13:55.761 --> 02:13:58.130
for the raw materials for certain items,

02:13:58.130 --> 02:14:01.133
like the fried food, yakitori, oden,

02:14:01.133 --> 02:14:03.135
and Chinese steamed buns.

02:14:03.135 --> 02:14:05.937
The chicken for our fried
chicken is from Thailand.

02:14:05.937 --> 02:14:08.440
The pork for our sausages and hot dogs

02:14:08.440 --> 02:14:11.543
comes from USA, Canada, and Japan.

02:14:11.543 --> 02:14:13.879
The wheat for the buns comes from Canada,

02:14:13.879 --> 02:14:15.881
the USA, and Japan.

02:14:15.881 --> 02:14:18.216
And adzuki beans come from Canada,

02:14:18.216 --> 02:14:20.118
cheese comes from New Zealand,

02:14:20.118 --> 02:14:23.588
and the shrimp for the shrimp
chili buns is from Vietnam.

02:14:23.588 --> 02:14:25.424
This is the pepperoni pizza in the US.

02:14:25.424 --> 02:14:28.360
And it contains all this junk.

02:14:28.360 --> 02:14:31.463
I mean, what's this thing?

02:14:31.463 --> 02:14:33.732
Never heard of that.

02:14:33.732 --> 02:14:35.233
What about chicken strips?

02:14:35.233 --> 02:14:37.002
It's got all this stuff!

02:14:37.002 --> 02:14:38.670
Just like mom used to make.

02:14:38.670 --> 02:14:41.540
And, of course, the 7-Eleven
Select cheeseburger,

02:14:41.540 --> 02:14:43.408
which contains ... [sighs]

02:14:43.408 --> 02:14:45.510
sesame seed bun has enriched flour,

02:14:45.510 --> 02:14:46.978
excuse me, enriched wheat flour,

02:14:46.978 --> 02:14:48.914
wheat flour, niacin, reduced iron,

02:14:48.914 --> 02:14:51.917
monoserititate, serotitititate,

02:14:51.917 --> 02:14:54.686
calcium propionate as a
preservative, calcium sulfate,

02:14:54.686 --> 02:14:57.789
royal beef patty got smoke flavor added,

02:14:57.789 --> 02:14:59.558
and it's beef, encapsulated
salt, potassium ...

02:14:59.558 --> 02:15:00.592
Is anything else after that?

02:15:00.592 --> 02:15:03.195
Salt, spice, pasteurized
process American cheese.

02:15:03.195 --> 02:15:04.729
Ah, cheese -- they're sitting down.

02:15:04.729 --> 02:15:05.964
That's how long this is going.

02:15:05.964 --> 02:15:07.899
My cameraperson just sat down.

02:15:07.899 --> 02:15:10.969
A preservative, paprika,
and annatto color.

02:15:10.969 --> 02:15:12.704
So I guess the last takeaway

02:15:12.704 --> 02:15:14.706
from this video is that in the US,

02:15:14.706 --> 02:15:17.242
some of our 7-Eleven items can be

02:15:17.242 --> 02:15:19.411
a little bit of a gamble with your health.

02:15:19.411 --> 02:15:21.346
Speaking of gambling, you know your boy

02:15:21.346 --> 02:15:23.482
got some scratchers when
he was over at 7-Eleven.

02:15:23.482 --> 02:15:25.617
Mm-hmm, OK. So there's
the winning numbers.

02:15:25.617 --> 02:15:28.653
OK, so we didn't win anything on that one.

02:15:28.653 --> 02:15:30.555
I have no clue how to do this.

02:15:30.555 --> 02:15:31.857
Did I win?

02:15:31.857 --> 02:15:35.961
If you haven't subscribed
yet, subscribe now!

02:15:35.961 --> 02:15:39.131
'Cause we were filming this for six hours.

